('This is no way to die.', 'This is no way to die.', 162035, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I could feel the cold overtaking me...', 'I could feel the cold overtaking me...', 162034, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have my thanks.', 'You have my thanks.', 162033, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This had better not be a trap, we still require $n\'s services.', '', 162032, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am ready to leave Fate\'s End.', 'I am ready to leave Fate\'s End.', 162031, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am ready to go to Fate\'s End.', 'I am ready to go to Fate\'s End.', 162030, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What in the? What does Magni Bronzebeard need?', '', 162029, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Didn\'t you hear? The Horde has Derek Proudmoore\'s body at Plunder Harbor. Lady Proudmoore\'s practically sent the whole navy to retrieve it.', 'Didn\'t you hear? The Horde has Derek Proudmoore\'s body at Plunder Harbor. Lady Proudmoore\'s practically sent the whole navy to retrieve it.', 162025, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sure is quiet today. Where is everybody?', 'Sure is quiet today. Where is everybody?', 162024, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Stone seems to be shaping up rather well.\n\nIn time, I believe she will prove to be quite a loyal ally.', 162023, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 669, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It was... invigorating seeing those people get what they deserved.\n\nIs this what it is like to be free? To set your own rules?\n\nPerhaps I could get used to this.', 162021, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 669, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Amalia seems to be coping relatively well. \n\nWhat she\'s going through isn\'t easy, but she\'s stronger than I was when I was turned. I killed nearly everyone who angered me. Amalia has only closed herself off.\n\nGiven time, she will come around. Trust me.', 162020, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They\'re gettin\' closer! Put the hurt on \'em!', '', 162019, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Come on boys, keep the pain comin\'!', '', 162018, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You will falter... he rises... he rises...', '', 162017, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Leave me alone. I don\'t want to talk to you.', 162016, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The master hungers... the Heart shall feed his waking dream...', '', 162015, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Da Zandalari be worshipin\' ol\' Bwonsamdi for a long time, just like da Darkspear.\n\nLook at dis Bwonsamdi idol I bought in da harbor. It be amazin\'! Better den most I seen back home.\n\nDa Darkspear and Zandalari got plenty of differences, true, but we got even more in common.\n\nIf da Zandalari ever get da sticks outta their bums, I tink we gonna be good friends!', '', 162014, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'No! Our home...', 162013, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You will not take another step towards our home, $r! Tor ilisar\'thera\'nal!', 162012, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Too late... fools...', '', 162011, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We will raze what is left of this little village, then be rid of you once and for all!', '', 162010, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I hear the Zandalari worship a pterrordax loa.\n\nA reptile god... that flies!\n\n<Lasan seems to have a twinkle in his eye.>\n\nAviash is ready to take their best riders in a race. Or better yet, a fight!\n\nDoesn\'t matter to us. We\'ll beat \'em in both!\n\nHahahahahahahahahaha!', '', 162009, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 574, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me your plan, Nathanos.', 'Tell me your plan, Nathanos.', 162008, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Very good. $n, tell Tattersail we are ready to depart.', '', 162007, 0, 0, 273, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And the Horde is going to steal it.', '', 162006, 0, 0, 2, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
