('The smell of blood in the water will just attract more sharks.', '', 160429, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Feeding time, boys!', '', 160428, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Big deal you beat me. I\'m still stuck down here for eternity. At least I had a conversation today.', '', 160427, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('One person against one shark, maybe an even fight.  One person against three? You\'re insane.', '', 160426, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you want to beat the likes of me you\'re going to need a bigger boat to haul these out of here.', '', 160425, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Your determination is admirable, but the outcome of this has already been determined.', 160424, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Return to where you came from!', 160423, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This was not supposed to happen, the prophecy spoke otherwise.', 160422, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You need much more training before you can handle a master like myself.', 160421, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Strange creatures on this island will make for a strange battle I suspect.', 160420, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You\'re better suited to be chum on a fishing boat than battling for my team.', 160419, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Looks like that one now sleeps with the fishes!', 160418, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Always more fish in the ocean, right?  Maybe that\'s not what that saying means now that I think about it.', 160417, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Never a doubt in my mind.', 160416, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ve found the toughest sea creatures around to battle for me, you don\'t stand a chance.', 160415, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Every time I train up new bees, it\'s always the same thing. They get big and strong and seemingly unbeatable, and then they sting something and die.', '', 160414, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Score one for the bees!', '', 160413, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not my bees! No!', '', 160412, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bees are clearly superior. This proves it.', '', 160411, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Just remember as we start this battle, you asked for this.', '', 160410, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'That was my least favorite of the bunch, time to play with the real hard hitters, get ready!', 160409, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Score one for team Fizzie!', 160408, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'But my pets are infused with Azerite! It\'s what pets crave!', 160407, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Can\'t say I\'m surprised, my team is clearly the best.', 160406, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You think your pets have a chance against my Azerite infused team? You wish!', 160405, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'There are many creatures in Zuldazar, some small, others huge. I have taken it upon myself to capture and train the smallest creatures as a reminder that great things can come from small beginnings.', 160404, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Meet me below deck when you\'re done. I\'ll find a way to destroy the barrier protecting Blood Prince Dreven.', 160403, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fetid Devourer has successfully |TInterface\\ICONS\\Ability_Creature_Poison_01.blp:20|t used |cFFFF0000|Hspell:262370|h[Consume Corruption]|h|r! Be sure to kill Corruption Corpuscles when they spawn!', 'Fetid Devourer has successfully |TInterface\\ICONS\\Ability_Creature_Poison_01.blp:20|t used |cFFFF0000|Hspell:262370|h[Consume Corruption]|h|r! Be sure to kill Corruption Corpuscles when they spawn!', 160402, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shandris\'ll be waitin\' for ye on board. Good luck.', '', 160401, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nice throwin\'! Now let\'s get ye over tae the Crimson Squall.', '', 160400, 0, 0, 4, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Aaaaargh!', 160399, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'YESSSSSSSSS! G\'huun\'s blood flows through our veins!', 160398, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Blood of our master... our flesh, our lives for G\'huun!', 160397, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I got ye, Swiftwing. No Horde cannon\'s bringing us down today.', '', 160396, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh wow! This is great! Thanks $uMister:Miss;!', 'Oh wow! This is great! Thanks $uMister:Miss;!', 160395, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You... you brought us new candy? Better candy?', 'You... you brought us new candy? Better candy?', 160394, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey! You\'re the $r that took our candy before!', 'Hey! You\'re the $r that took our candy before!', 160393, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Only a few candy wrappers remain from your raid on this chest... Wrappers and your own shame.>', '<Only a few candy wrappers remain from your raid on this chest... Wrappers and your own shame.>', 160392, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Place some better candy into the chest.>', '<Place some better candy into the chest.>', 160391, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I cannot wait to delve into Xibala\'s secrets. This place raises so many questions!\n\nWho is Xibala? What is Xibala? Why did the Zandalari abandon this place? What does the Eye of Xibala do?\n\nUnder Examiner Tae\'shara\'s guidance I am certain we will find out!', 'I cannot wait to delve into Xibala\'s secrets. This place raises so many questions!\n\nWho is Xibala? What is Xibala? Why did the Zandalari abandon this place? What does the Eye of Xibala do?\n\nUnder Examiner Tae\'shara\'s guidance I am certain we will find out!', 160390, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you think Astrandis could introduce me to Chief Telemancer Oculeth...?\n\nI have heard so much about him. Do you think he will sign my tabard?', 'Do you think Astrandis could introduce me to Chief Telemancer Oculeth...?\n\nI have heard so much about him. Do you think he will sign my tabard?', 160389, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I must hand it to them. After spending a small eternity cloistered in a perfect world of plush couches and wine, these nightborne are adapting very well to the vigors of the world beyond.\n\nWhy, I was even able to teach one to wield a shovel!', 'I must hand it to them. After spending a small eternity cloistered in a perfect world of plush couches and wine, these nightborne are adapting very well to the vigors of the world beyond.\n\nWhy, I was even able to teach one to wield a shovel!', 160388, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Examiner Tae\'shara is a remarkably patient woman. A worthy successor to her father, should he rescind his claim to his position.\n\nThough I wonder if this Astrandis fellow might be testing her prodigious tolerance.', 'Examiner Tae\'shara is a remarkably patient woman. A worthy successor to her father, should he rescind his claim to his position.\n\nThough I wonder if this Astrandis fellow might be testing her prodigious tolerance.', 160387, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Reliquary jumped at the opportunity to excavate such a site. We are fortunate that the trolls who live here did not object.', 'The Reliquary jumped at the opportunity to excavate such a site. We are fortunate that the trolls who live here did not object.', 160386, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I offered a nightborne a pickaxe and he gave me the most bewildered look.\n\n\"What is it for?\" He asked, as if he could hardly fathom an answer.\n\nTheir magical prowess speaks volumes as to their capability as a race, but they have a great deal to learn about the world. Luckily we sin\'dorei are well equipped to teach them.', 'I offered a nightborne a pickaxe and he gave me the most bewildered look.\n\n\"What is it for?\" He asked, as if he could hardly fathom an answer.\n\nTheir magical prowess speaks volumes as to their capability as a race, but they have a great deal to learn about the world. Luckily we sin\'dorei are well equipped to teach them.', 160385, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The nightborne have been incredibly useful on this expedition, but not in the ways I expected.\n\nThey do bring a certain level of comfort with them when they travel, which is a welcome step above the usual roughness of camp.\n\n<He sips from a glass of wine.>', 'The nightborne have been incredibly useful on this expedition, but not in the ways I expected.\n\nThey do bring a certain level of comfort with them when they travel, which is a welcome step above the usual roughness of camp.\n\n<She sips from a glass of wine.>', 160384, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do not look now, but I think that shal\'dorei is holding his survey tool upside down.', 'Do not look now, but I think that shal\'dorei is holding his survey tool upside down.', 160383, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I confess, I did not know what I was getting into when I agreed to visit to this strange land.\n\nIt is hotter than I expected. Much hotter. But this is an invaluable opportunity to advance the First Arcanist\'s cause and ingratiate ourselves with our new allies.\n\nI suppose that is as good a reason as any to grin and bear it, if you will.\n\n<He puts on a very strained smile.>', 'I confess, I did not know what I was getting into when I agreed to visit to this strange land.\n\nIt is hotter than I expected. Much hotter. But this is an invaluable opportunity to advance the First Arcanist\'s cause and ingratiate ourselves with our new allies.\n\nI suppose that is as good a reason as any to grin and bear it, if you will.\n\n<She puts on a very strained smile.>', 160382, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I hope we are making a good impression with the Zandalari. They were very kind-- and reluctant!-- to allow us the opportunity to study this site.', 'I hope we are making a good impression with the Zandalari. They were very kind-- and reluctant!-- to allow us the opportunity to study this site.', 160381, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you think our Reliquary allies will allow me to use one of those tiny brushes...?', 'Do you think our Reliquary allies will allow me to use one of those tiny brushes...?', 160380, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Our sin\'dorei allies have been regaling me with stories of their past expeditions. I sense a recurring theme with their repeated encounters with dwarven-kind.', 'Our sin\'dorei allies have been regaling me with stories of their past expeditions. I sense a recurring theme with their repeated encounters with dwarven-kind.', 160379, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you think the trolls will allow us to bring one of those large long-necked creatures back to Suramar...? Su\'esh would adore a companion!\n\nMaybe you should ask them!', 'Do you think the trolls will allow us to bring one of those large long-necked creatures back to Suramar...?\n\nMaybe you should ask them!', 160378, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<He swats at a passing mosquito.>\n\nThe things we endure to demonstrate our worth to the Horde! These work conditions are appalling!', '<She swats at a passing mosquito.>\n\nThe things we endure to demonstrate our worth to the Horde! These work conditions are appalling!', 160377, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<He fans himself vigorously with a hand.>\n\nI failed to properly appreciate Suramar\'s climate before now. It shall be a welcome relief to return home once this digging business is done.', '<She fans herself vigorously with a hand.>\n\nI failed to properly appreciate Suramar\'s climate before now. It shall be a welcome relief to return home once this digging business is done.', 160376, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I read about jungles in our library but somehow they failed to mention the sweltering heat!\n\nMy clothes are sticking to me. There are insects. Insects!\n\nWhy would anyone willingly live in such a place?', 'I read about jungles in our library but somehow they failed to mention the sweltering heat!\n\nMy clothes are sticking to me. There are insects. Insects!\n\nWhy would anyone willingly live in such a place?', 160375, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, those two. You can find dem constantly bickering inside de Great Seal. Dey\'re up on de balcony on de east side.\n\nDey make me want to avoid going in dere. Have to say though, I agree with de tauren. Mostly.', 'Oh, those two. You can find dem constantly bickering inside de Great Seal. Dey\'re up on de balcony on de east side.\n\nDey make me want to avoid going in dere. Have to say though, I agree with de tauren. Mostly.', 160374, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re looking for Cringely and Ulla. They are having a spirited debate about the Warchief\'s policies. Of course, Cringely is correct, but Ulla, bless her, is stubborn.\n\nYou can\'t help but find them inside the Great Seal. They\'re up on the eastern balcony overlooking the gallery.', 'You\'re looking for Cringely and Ulla. They are having a spirited debate about the Warchief\'s policies. Of course, Cringely is correct, but Ulla, bless her, is stubborn.\n\nYou can\'t help but find them inside the Great Seal. They\'re up on the eastern balcony overlooking the gallery.', 160373, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Cod in stock! Prepared and ready to eat!', '', 160372, 0, 0, 753, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Catch of the day! Fresh shark, harpooned this morning!', '', 160371, 0, 0, 753, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Carry us through the storm.', '', 160370, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114349, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Guide us through the treacherous waters, now your domain.', '', 160369, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114348, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Part the veil and step onto shore.', '', 160368, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114347, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Souls washed to sea, return to us.', '', 160367, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114346, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We are beacons to guide you home.', '', 160366, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114345, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We lift our lanterns over the dark waters.', '', 160365, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114344, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Their tolling calls you home.', '', 160364, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114341, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hear our bells ring out over the storm\'s song.', '', 160363, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114340, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('On smooth waters and swift currents, sail home.', '', 160362, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114343, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('With blood we calm the wild seas that claimed you.', '', 160361, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114342, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Leave the embrace of the Abyss to aid your brethren once more.', '', 160360, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114339, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Weary souls lost to the depths, we call upon you.', '', 160359, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114338, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wind and current carry our plea.', '', 160358, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114337, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Made with the best ham in the Eastern Kingdoms! Directly from Fallhaven!', 160357, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Sausages! Freshly packaged from Drustvar and Stormwind!', 160356, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Nothing better than sipping exotic beer while walking down the market row! Or if beer isn\'t your thing, I\'ve also brought plenty of tea!', 160355, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Brew for sale! Kegs straight from the Pandaria!', 160354, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey! You there! Yeah, you! I might have something of interest for a person of your... vocation.', '', 160353, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now more than ever, the Warchief needs us sharp and organized. What will your guild sacrifice to further the Horde cause?', '', 160352, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Fresh cabbages, grown locally!', 160351, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Vegetables straight from the farms of Stormsong! Best corn you\'ll ever taste!', 160350, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t know where the ship is now.', 'I don\'t know where the ship is now.', 160349, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Relentless should have just left the Stormwind Docks.', 'The Relentless should have just left the Stormwind Docks.', 160348, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Relentless should have just left Boralus.', 'The Relentless should have just left Boralus.', 160347, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you ever need an answer to any shoe related problem, I\'ll always be here. Enjoy your newly found shine!', '', 160346, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('One shoe shine, coming up!', '', 160345, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A professional, are you? Good. We can always use more. If you\'re looking for de tools of your trade, find a tauren by de name of Hanul Swiftgale. Just look for him in de Hall of Ancient Paths, which is a room on de east side inside de Great Seal.', 'A professional, are you? Good. We can always use more. If you\'re looking for de tools of your trade, find a tauren by de name of Hanul Swiftgale. Just look for him in de Hall of Ancient Paths, which is a room on de east side inside de Great Seal.', 160344, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you\'re looking for trade goods, you want to head inside the Great Seal. Once inside, head east into the Hall of Ancient Paths. You\'re looking for a tauren named Hanul Swiftgale. He should have anything you need.', 'If you\'re looking for trade goods, you want to head inside the Great Seal. Once inside, head east into the Hall of Ancient Paths. You\'re looking for a tauren named Hanul Swiftgale. He should have anything you need.', 160343, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('General goods? De Horde brought their own with dem. Go speak with de orc, Araka, inside de Hall of Ancient Paths. Dat\'s a room on de east side of de Great Seal. She has all de general goods you need.', 'General goods? De Horde brought their own with dem. Go speak with de orc, Araka, inside de Hall of Ancient Paths. Dat\'s a room on de east side of de Great Seal. She has all de general goods you need.', 160342, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Araka can help you. She\'s inside the Hall of Ancient Paths just off the east side of the Great Seal.', 'Araka can help you. She\'s inside the Hall of Ancient Paths just off the east side of the Great Seal.', 160341, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You looking to create a new guild? It\'s Dockwarden Finnson and Perry Charlton who you\'re after. They\'re a shady couple, but they\'ll show you the ropes.\n\nLook for them in the building on the city-side entrance of the harbor proper.', 'You looking to create a new guild? It\'s Dockwarden Finnson and Perry Charlton who you\'re after. They\'re a shady couple, but they\'ll show you the ropes.\n\nLook for them in the building on the city-side entrance of the harbor proper.', 160340, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Leila Stafford is just the best. Helped me more than once with my little Fluffy when she was sick.\n\nYou\'ll find her on the upper level of Tradewinds Market on the west side.', 'Leila Stafford is just the best. Helped me more than once with my little Fluffy when she was sick.\n\nYou\'ll find her on the upper level of Tradewinds Market on the west side.', 160339, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We had a barber, but then he disappeared not long ago and no one knows what happened to him. It was all the news for about a day.\n\nNow this gnome has moved into his old place. Look I\'m not suggesting anything here, but if you\'re looking for a cut or a color change, you can look for Teri Lockfield at Hook Point. Just watch your lower back.', 'We had a barber, but then he disappeared not long ago and no one knows what happened to him. It was all the news for about a day.\n\nNow this gnome has moved into his old place. Look I\'m not suggesting anything here, but if you\'re looking for a cut or a color change, you can look for Teri Lockfield at Hook Point. Just watch your lower back.', 160338, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Fjarnskaggl is popular among nobles here. I run out of stock quickly.\n\nCheck back next week, maybe I will have more.', 160337, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You already purchased your seals for the week. Stop wasting my time.\n\nI should have more available next week.', '', 160336, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Henrick Wyther sells all manner of goods to support professionals such as yourself. You can find him on the upper level of Tradewinds Market.\n\nYou can\'t miss his stall. He\'s a bit of a conspiracy nut. Don\'t laugh at his maps and notes. He takes that stuff very seriously and he\'s a nice guy.', 'Henrick Wyther sells all manner of goods to support professionals such as yourself. You can find him on the upper level of Tradewinds Market.\n\nYou can\'t miss his stall. He\'s a bit of a conspiracy nut. Don\'t laugh at his maps and notes. He takes that stuff very seriously and he\'s a nice guy.', 160335, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Trade Goods', 'Trade Goods', 160334, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t get me started on the gold I\'ve spent on repairs. Thankfully, the admiralty has its own blacksmith to take care of our issued gear. But, for your personal stuff, I highly recommend you go see Patrick Markson. Yes, I know he sells firearms. But, he\'s also great at fixing just about anything.\n\nLook for his stall at the fountain on the lower level of Tradewinds Market, just down the stairs from the inn.', 'Don\'t get me started on the gold I\'ve spent on repairs. Thankfully, the admiralty has its own blacksmith to take care of our issued gear. But, for your personal stuff, I highly recommend you go see Patrick Markson. Yes, I know he sells firearms. But, he\'s also great at fixing just about anything.\n\nLook for his stall at the fountain on the lower level of Tradewinds Market, just down the stairs from the inn.', 160333, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 274, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you ever wish to retry your fate?  Perhaps, for a special armor piece, a weapon or a trinket of great power?\n\nFor a price, I will provide you a seal that twists fate and grants an extra result at a past chance. \n\nOnce you possess a seal, it will activate after defeating powerful foes in difficult dungeons and raids.\n\nSoon, I will be able to provide Seals of Wartorn Fate for Gold, War Resources or Marks of Honor. \n\nI have none to offer to you at this time.', '', 160332, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I offer various ways to purchase a Seal of Wartorn Fate. \n\nWhat do you prefer to give up for the opportunity to twist fate?', '', 160331, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You already hold the most seals that you can. \n\nUse the seals you have before bothering me for more.', '', 160330, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('General goods. Got it. You\'re looking for Ninette Shoams. She sets out her wares every day down at the fountain in lower Tradewinds Market.', 'General goods. Got it. You\'re looking for Ninette Shoams. She sets out her wares every day down at the fountain in lower Tradewinds Market.', 160329, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This dock now serves as the landing spot for The Relentless.\n\nShe\'s been chartered by the Alliance as the main transportation for diplomats between Stormwind and Kul Tiras. The ship will take you straight to the Boralus Harbor.', 'This dock now serves as the landing spot for The Relentless.\n\nShe\'s been chartered by the Alliance as the main transportation for diplomats between Stormwind and Kul Tiras. The ship will take you straight to the Boralus Harbor.', 160328, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('General Goods', 'General Goods', 160327, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Relentless docks here routinely to get folks back to the mainland. If you\'re looking to go to Stormwind, she\'s your ship. She\'ll land in the city harbor.', 'The Relentless docks here routinely to get folks back to the mainland. If you\'re looking to go to Stormwind, she\'s your ship. She\'ll land in the city harbor.', 160326, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Vendors. Right. What kind of merchant are ya lookin\' for?', 'Vendors. Right. What kind of merchant are ya lookin\' for?', 160325, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A fresh look. I hear you. It\'s the strangest thing, but you need to go see Warpweaver Ezil. I know, it\'s just odd because he looks like a walking bandage. But trust me, he can work wonders for you. If you can get an appointment.\n\nHe\'s set up shop in the building next to the Snug Harbor Inn.', 'A fresh look. I hear you. It\'s the strangest thing, but you need to go see Warpweaver Ezil. I know, it\'s just odd because he looks like a walking bandage. But trust me, he can work wonders for you. If you can get an appointment.\n\nHe\'s set up shop in the building next to the Snug Harbor Inn.', 160324, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Whether you\'re looking to learn a new style of embroidering or how to staunch a bleeding wound. Or, maybe even a new bag... you want to train with Daniel Brineweaver. Look for him at the north end of Tradewinds Market on the upper level.\n\nDaniel\'s a good guy, if a little mopey. He\'s bandaged me up more times than I care to admit. Passing on his mastery always seems to brighten his day.', 'Whether you\'re looking to learn a new style of embroidering or how to staunch a bleeding wound. Or, maybe even a new bag... you want to train with Daniel Brineweaver. Look for him at the north end of Tradewinds Market on the upper level.\n\nDaniel\'s a good guy, if a little mopey. He\'s bandaged me up more times than I care to admit. Passing on his mastery always seems to brighten his day.', 160323, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 273, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You some big time hunter? I got news for you, friend. The things over here have tougher hides than anything you\'ve ever faced. We grow \'em tough and deadly in Kul Tiras.\n\nIf you want to learn, you need to learn from the best. You\'re looking for Camilla Darksky. She\'s on the upper level on the north side of Tradewinds Market.', 'You some big time hunter? I got news for you, friend. The things over here have tougher hides than anything you\'ve ever faced. We grow \'em tough and deadly in Kul Tiras.\n\nIf you want to learn, you need to learn from the best. You\'re looking for Camilla Darksky. She\'s on the upper level on the north side of Tradewinds Market.', 160322, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Safe? Have you seen the things creeping around this place?\n\nThanks, but I\'ll stick to my guns... gun... You know what I mean.', '', 160321, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You don\'t need to brandish your weapon here. It\'s safe.', 'You don\'t need to brandish your weapon here. It\'s safe.', 160320, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be ready for anything.', '', 160319, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Battle is upon us. We could use a $r like you among our ranks.', '', 160318, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('I can see it in your eyes. Your mind, eroded by the gnawing madness. Yet there may be a reprieve.$b$bThe sages once thrived here, trying to combat the darkness. They built chapels, bulwarks of faith and fortitude. They erected a tavern, to drown the whispers under a sea of mead. Dust and rubble now...$b$bMake your way to the northwest. Upon that point is the last of their presence, a large, abyssal idol. Find the effigy, and you may yet wash away the horrors of this place. Beware, for you will need to drink deep, and the sea always exacts her toll.', '', 160317, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am troubled. Can you help me?', 'I am troubled. Can you help me?', 160316, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can you feel it? The walls... crumbling. They are coming through, one terrible whisper at a time.', '', 160315, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Once, this ruin was the envy of the valley.', '', 160314, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I must confess that I cannot recall when that letter was even sent...', '', 160313, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Remember, overconfidence is a slow and insidious destroyer.', '', 160312, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Digging for gold? Platinum? Storm Silver?! If you\'re looking for the latest mining techniques, you\'re looking for Myra Cabot. She has a preternatural ability to sniff out a vein.\n\nShe\'s up at the north side of Tradewinds Market on the upper level. Let me know if you strike it rich, friend.', 'Digging for gold? Platinum? Storm Silver?! If you\'re looking for the latest mining techniques, you\'re looking for Myra Cabot. She has a preternatural ability to sniff out a vein.\n\nShe\'s up at the north side of Tradewinds Market on the upper level. Let me know if you strike it rich, friend.', 160311, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alright, we\'ll come back later tae finish \'em off.', '', 160310, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s not my thing, but if you\'re looking to improve your leatherworking chops, I have just the Kul Tiran for you. Her name\'s Cassandra Brennor, and she\'s a wizard with an awl and punch.\n\nYou can usually find her working with Camilla Darksky. They share a space on the upper level at the north end of Tradewinds Market.', 'It\'s not my thing, but if you\'re looking to improve your leatherworking chops, I have just the Kul Tiran for you. Her name\'s Cassandra Brennor, and she\'s a wizard with an awl and punch.\n\nYou can usually find her working with Camilla Darksky. They share a space on the upper level at the north end of Tradewinds Market.', 160309, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let me know when ye are ready tae start the bombing run.', '', 160308, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Samuel D. Colton the third is who you\'re after. It\'s a miracle he doesn\'t add a doctorate and an esquire in there. I\'ll give him this, though... his work is exquisite. If you\'re looking for training, you can\'t do better.\n\nYou\'ll find him standing proudly behind his display case in the middle of the upper level on the north side of Tradewinds Market.', 'Samuel D. Colton the third is who you\'re after. It\'s a miracle he doesn\'t add a doctorate and an esquire in there. I\'ll give him this, though... his work is exquisite. If you\'re looking for training, you can\'t do better.\n\nYou\'ll find him standing proudly behind his display case in the middle of the upper level on the north side of Tradewinds Market.', 160307, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You want Zooey Inksprocket. She recently rented herself a spot up at the north end of Tradewinds Market on the upper level. \n\nHard to believe you can fit so much knowledge and power in such a tiny person.', 'You want Zooey Inksprocket. She recently rented herself a spot up at the north end of Tradewinds Market on the upper level. \n\nHard to believe you can fit so much knowledge and power in such a tiny person.', 160306, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If we are to have any hope of bringing the Zandalari into the Horde, we must keep each other strong.', '', 160305, 0, 55301, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You like flowers? Me too. They smell so good. Well, most of \'em anyway.\n\nIf you\'re looking for the secret to how to best go about handling the flora in this part of the world, go speak with Declan Senal. You\'ll find him tending his garden on the upper level on the north side of Tradewinds Market.', 'You like flowers? Me too. They smell so good. Well, most of \'em anyway.\n\nIf you\'re looking for the secret to how to best go about handling the flora in this part of the world, go speak with Declan Senal. You\'ll find him tending his garden on the upper level on the north side of Tradewinds Market.', 160304, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Someone\'s protectin\' the Banshee\'s Wail with fancy tidesage magic!', '', 160303, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alan Goyle has his fish shack up above Tradewinds Market. He\'s always up there fishing from his pond. Don\'t ask me how it stays stocked. Guess the fish fall down the waterfalls.\n\nThere\'s a trick to getting up there. You need to find the stairs up between the jewelcrafting and tailoring trainers.', 'Alan Goyle has his fish shack up above Tradewinds Market. He\'s always up there fishing from his pond. Don\'t ask me how it stays stocked. Guess the fish fall down the waterfalls.\n\nThere\'s a trick to getting up there. You need to find the stairs up between the jewelcrafting and tailoring trainers.', 160302, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Take me hammers, $p, and throw \'em with all of yer strength!', '', 160301, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wildhammers, focus yer attention on the Banshee\'s Wail! Keep \'em locked down!', '', 160300, 0, 0, 22, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You a grenadier, sharpshooter, or one of those crazy inventor types? Maybe all three?\n\nRegardless, you\'re looking for Layla Evenkeel. You can find her dabbling with her machines on the upper level at the north end of Tradewinds Market.', 'You a grenadier, sharpshooter, or one of those crazy inventor types? Maybe all three?\n\nRegardless, you\'re looking for Layla Evenkeel. You can find her dabbling with her machines on the upper level at the north end of Tradewinds Market.', 160299, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Mag\'har... will... endure...', 160298, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 113949, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Your end is at hand!', 160297, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113955, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your hollow victory... means nothing...', '', 160296, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113971, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You will fall!', 160295, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113954, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Look! They\'re withdrawing!', 160294, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 0, 114175, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Haaa-ha! Take that, ya bilge-suckers!', 160293, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114174, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Lok-tar ogar!', 160292, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113953, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Dranosh\'ek mag\'har!', 160291, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113952, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I await you... in the Blighted Lands...', '', 160290, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113962, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We will never yield!', 160289, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113951, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Our battle... is not over... interloper...', '', 160288, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113961, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'For the mag\'har!', 160287, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 113950, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will... return...', '', 160286, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113964, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fools... you have merely... defeated... a vessel...', '', 160285, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113963, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Think you have won? Look around... What you seek is not here.', '', 160284, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 113974, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your lost little girl is in my keeping. Oh, how she weeps. Her suffering will be unending!', '', 160283, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 113975, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'If Azerite is capable of this kind of destruction, I fear not even the great gate of Boralus could withstand it.', 160282, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114165, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Such devastation... Daelin\'s Gate never stood a chance.', 160281, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114164, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Aim for their powder barrels!', 160280, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114173, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Emily Fairweather is who you\'re after. You\'ll find her at the tippy-top of Tradewinds Market on the north side.\n\nShe magicked me up some bracers once, in fact. Can\'t recommend her enough.', 'Emily Fairweather is who you\'re after. You\'ll find her at the tippy-top of Tradewinds Market on the north side.\n\nShe magicked me up some bracers once, in fact. Can\'t recommend her enough.', 160279, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 273, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The creatures out here can be nasty, but I\'ve got thick skin and I\'m determined to capture every last one of them.  My collection isn\'t too large yet, but the ones I have captured pack a punch.  Up for a fight?', 160278, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A visitor to my den? How curious.', '', 160277, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114668, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('When de last fire is lit, de city will know dat we are clear! I will see my crew return!', '', 160276, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He is vulnerable within his own realm, and he will go to great lengths to prevent you from entering it.', '', 160275, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114677, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wish you luck on your journey, mainlander. Tread carefully, for Gorak Tul\'s eyes will be upon you.', '', 160274, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114676, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Verdant Hollow is a fine location fer a hidden outpost. There\'s plenty o\' Azerite nearby and not a single troll in sight! What\'s not to like?', '', 160273, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We have become used to the various insects that fly around these lands, some are very docile, some are very dangerous.  I have collected quite a few species over many, many years, and we are more than happy to entertain other pet battlers with a skirmish.  Interested?', 160272, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We should hit the next one from the air. Are you with me?', 160271, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114172, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Gah! Maybe that was too close...', 160270, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114171, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Unearthing', 'Unearthing', 160269, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, you\'re looking for the \"Cap\'n\". Look for his outdoor restaurant nestled between the corral and the blacksmith\'s pit on the upper level of Tradewinds Market. It\'s on the north side.\n \nYou absolutely must try the Swamp Fish \'n Chips! Just thinking about going over there makes my mouth water.', 'Oh, you\'re looking for the \"Cap\'n\". Look for his outdoor restaurant nestled between the corral and the blacksmith\'s pit on the upper level of Tradewinds Market. It\'s on the north side.\n \nYou absolutely must try the Swamp Fish \'n Chips! Just thinking about going over there makes my mouth water.', 160268, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 273, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do I know where the blacksmithing trainer is? Of course, I know where he is. I\'m a guard, aren\'t I?\n\nHead to the upper level of Tradewinds Market. On the north side, you\'ll find a pit. In it, you\'ll see the most skilled smiths I know, Grix \"Ironfists\" Barlow. You can\'t miss him.', 'Do I know where the blacksmithing trainer is? Of course, I know where he is. I\'m a guard, aren\'t I?\n\nHead to the upper level of Tradewinds Market. On the north side, you\'ll find a pit. In it, you\'ll see the most skilled smiths I know, Grix \"Ironfists\" Barlow. You can\'t miss him.', 160267, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 5, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will begin preparations. Meet me once you have collected what we need.', '', 160266, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114334, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That was too close for comfort. Thanks for the timely rescue!', 'That was too close for comfort. Thanks for the timely rescue!', 160265, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I oversee all registry duties for guilds and trading companies in the harbor. How can I assist you?', '', 160263, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Digging in the dirt for lost treasure? That\'s the life. You got ya one of them fancy surveying gizmos?\n\nYou\'re looking for Jane Hudson on the upper level of Tradewinds Market. Once you get up there, you can usually find her inside her business on the west side of the terrace near the corral.', 'Digging in the dirt for lost treasure? That\'s the life. You got ya one of them fancy surveying gizmos?\n\nYou\'re looking for Jane Hudson on the upper level of Tradewinds Market. Once you get up there, you can usually find her inside her business on the west side of the terrace near the corral.', 160262, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Ready?! Throw!', 160261, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114170, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A potion master. Got it. Yep, you want Elric Whalgrene. You can find him in on the very north edge of Tradewinds Market on the upper level overlooking the blacksmith\'s pit.\n\nDon\'t let the lack of a top hat and cane fool you, that guy\'s a wizard. A powerful and strange one. I mean, drinking a potion to turn into a cloud? Weird. Have to admit I do love a dose of his Lightfoot concoction every now and then. Puts a spring in your step.', 'A potion master. Got it. Yep, you want Elric Whalgrene. You can find him in on the very north edge of Tradewinds Market on the upper level overlooking the blacksmith\'s pit.\n\nDon\'t let the lack of a top hat and cane fool you, that guy\'s a wizard. A powerful and strange one. I mean, drinking a potion to turn into a cloud? Weird. Have to admit I do love a dose of his Lightfoot concoction every now and then. Puts a spring in your step.', 160260, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In order for our land to heal, there must be the hope of redemption. For all of us.', '', 160259, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114332, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How keenly she must have felt those deaths! How much does she, too, long for atonement?', '', 160258, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114331, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lady Jaina stood aside as her father and countrymen perished.', '', 160257, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114330, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wonder, even now, if I could have done more. The thought of it haunts my dreams.', '', 160256, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114329, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They were lost to madness, but I still feel remorse for their deaths.', '', 160255, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114328, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I have had to fight, and even kill, my own people. It was a hard choice, but necessary.', '', 160254, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114327, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Many of my countrymen believe Jaina Proudmoore to be a traitor. Some would question my decision to help spare her.', '', 160253, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114326, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You a professional? Looking for some training, are ya? We got it all. This is Boralus, you know. None better.', 'You a professional? Looking for some training, are ya? We got it all. This is Boralus, you know. None better.', 160252, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blow the $pr down!', '', 160251, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I wandered all around these dunes and found some of the most spectacular species of pets I\'ve ever seen.  They scavenge and survive off of whatever they can, just like us. Their will to survive is strong and makes them durable.  Want to see my findings?', 160250, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t eat me Milden, I\'m your friend!', '', 160249, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Only swallow bad people!', '', 160248, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They tried to scare Milden off, but he got very mad!', '', 160247, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He swallowed mister Anderson!', '', 160246, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hurry up in there!', 'Hurry up in there!', 160245, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You must gather what I require quickly. A life is at stake.', '', 160244, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114333, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But we are far from finished cleansing our homeland of its corruption.', '', 160242, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114325, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Loyal brothers and sisters have joined me to turn the tides--quite literally, in some cases.', '', 160241, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114324, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lord Stormsong is no more, but the darkness that claimed him still lingers.', '', 160240, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114323, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('To even set foot upon that shore is to be condemned to death.', '', 160239, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114322, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We tidesages are the only ones who can venture there safely, but even we remain in the water.', '', 160238, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114321, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I have never borne the burden of escorting any soul to Fate\'s End.', '', 160237, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114320, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m sorry, child... I cannot allow you in here. Take what you came for and leave.', '', 160236, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If Lady Jaina was sent to that wretched shore, we may not have much time. Come with me.', '', 160235, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114319, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('She condemned her daughter to Fate\'s End? Merciful tides!', '', 160234, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114318, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lady Katherine has reconsidered her order to have her daughter executed. We know Jaina was taken to Fate\'s End. I seek passage there.', 'Lady Katherine has reconsidered her order to have her daughter executed. We know Jaina was taken to Fate\'s End. I seek passage there.', 160233, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Time is short and we must work quickly if we are to save Jaina.', '', 160232, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your head is perfect for my next creation!', '', 160230, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Some of my best work. The pieces blend together beautifully.', '', 160229, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, $n. It is good to see you again, my friend. What brings you back to Stormsong?', '', 160228, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114317, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lady Katherine will surely wish to know what you found.', '', 160227, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114356, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'He is ancient... and more terrible than you know...', 160226, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Be mine. Forever.', 160225, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hello, darling. Would you like to hear my song?', 160224, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re a fool... to trust...just like us.', '', 160223, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'ll not have these artifacts!', '', 160222, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The shipments can\'t be delayed!', '', 160221, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What possible business could you have with that crazy gnome? His whole area is a bit of a mess if you ask me.\n\nWell, I see I cannot dissuade you. The individual you\'re looking for is Crenzo Sparkshatter. He\'s on the upper level of Tradewinds Market on the east side. You\'ll find him tinkering atop his ever-growing pile of junk. Best of luck, friend.', 'What possible business could you have with that crazy gnome? His whole area is a bit of a mess if you ask me.\n\nWell, I see I cannot dissuade you. The individual you\'re looking for is Crenzo Sparkshatter. He\'s on the upper level of Tradewinds Market on the east side. You\'ll find him tinkering atop his ever-growing pile of junk. Best of luck, friend.', 160220, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let me tell you, friend, the city\'s ferry system is one of the true wonders of the world. Not only can it take you from place to place inside the wonderous waterways of Boralus proper, the ferry masters also serve the outskirts into the rest of Tiragarde Sound.\n\nIf you\'re looking for a pleasant boat ride, look no further than Will Melbourne. You can find him and his daughter, Sally down at water level on the south side of Tradewinds Market.', 'Let me tell you, friend, the city\'s ferry system is one of the true wonders of the world. Not only can it take you from place to place inside the wonderous waterways of Boralus proper, the ferry masters also serve the outskirts into the rest of Tiragarde Sound.\n\nIf you\'re looking for a pleasant boat ride, look no further than Will Melbourne. You can find him and his daughter, Sally down at water level on the south side of Tradewinds Market.', 160219, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ferry Master', 'Ferry Master', 160218, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There are all sorts of interesting places scattered about Boralus. What can I interest you in, friend?', 'There are all sorts of interesting places scattered about Boralus. What can I interest you in, friend?', 160217, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you\'re lookin\' for a place to catch twenty winks, might I suggest heading over to the Snug Harbor inn? You\'ll find it on the upper level overlooking the fountain.\n\nWesley Rockhold is your man. He\'ll set you up with a nice, comfy bed. No straw mattresses. And if he has a pot of his legendary stew on, make sure you grab a trencher.', 'If you\'re lookin\' for a place to catch twenty winks, might I suggest heading over to the Snug Harbor inn? You\'ll find it on the upper level overlooking the fountain.\n\nWesley Rockhold is your man. He\'ll set you up with a nice, comfy bed. No straw mattresses. And if he has a pot of his legendary stew on, make sure you grab a trencher.', 160216, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wgullll naq xizzuoog', '', 160215, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wgul naq zzigla ouug anagih', '', 160214, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You don\'t gotta tell me twice!', '', 160213, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Looking to take a trip, eh? Yeah, I know. The thrill of soaring through the clouds to distant, exotic lands. The excitement of the unknowable danger on the other end. The promise of that sweet, sweet treasure once you\'ve vanquished the villain?\n\nNo? Uh... oh, you\'re just looking for a flight? Well, why didn\'t you say so? Just head to the upper level of the west side of Tradewinds Market. You can\'t miss Joan Weber near the gryphon roost.', 'Looking to take a trip, eh? Yeah, I know. The thrill of soaring through the clouds to distant, exotic lands. The excitement of the unknowable danger on the other end. The promise of that sweet, sweet treasure once you\'ve vanquished the villain?\n\nNo? Uh... oh, you\'re just looking for a flight? Well, why didn\'t you say so? Just head to the upper level of the west side of Tradewinds Market. You can\'t miss Joan Weber near the gryphon roost.', 160212, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Be on your way.', 160211, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'And you, Speaker of de Horde. I will consider what to do with you.', 160210, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You, small green one, are no longer welcome in Warbeast Kraal. Begone!', 160209, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Good. Dis unnatural voodoo is undone.', 160208, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This wasn\'t in my... contract...', 160207, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You\'re intruding on Ashvane company property!', 160206, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Direhorn Juvenile groans and collapses.', '', 160205, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Direhorn Juvenile shies away at the taste.', '', 160204, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We\'ll need a boat to reach the next ship.', 160203, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114169, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t ask me how I know this, but I do. If you want to get in good with those mysterious tortoise people, you must talk with their emissary, Collector Cojo.\n\nNow where might he be? Here\'s the bad news. He\'s all the way up in Stormsong Valley at a place they call, Seekers Vista. You\'re on your own getting up there, friend. But, by the look of you, I bet you already have a way.', 'Don\'t ask me how I know this, but I do. If you want to get in good with those mysterious tortoise people, you must talk with their emissary, Collector Cojo.\n\nNow where might he be? Here\'s the bad news. He\'s all the way up in Stormsong Valley at a place they call, Seekers Vista. You\'re on your own getting up there, friend. But, by the look of you, I bet you already have a way.', 160202, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s hammerin\' time!', '', 160201, 0, 0, 22, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can\'t beat the hammers, can\'t stop the gryphons!', '', 160200, 0, 0, 679, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Now! Let \'em have it!', 160199, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114168, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gettin\' in good with the admiralty, eh? Good on you.\n\nYeah, I know where she is. You\'re looking for Provisioner Fray inside the Harbormaster\'s Office. She\'s stuffed in there with all the big wigs.', 'Gettin\' in good with the admiralty, eh? Good on you.\n\nYeah, I know where she is. You\'re looking for Provisioner Fray inside the Harbormaster\'s Office. She\'s stuffed in there with all the big wigs.', 160198, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Proudmoore Admiralty Emissary', 'Proudmoore Admiralty Emissary', 160197, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Emissaries, huh? Which one are you looking for?', 'Emissaries, huh? Which one are you looking for?', 160196, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The bank. Aye. You\'ll find the bankers in the northwest corner of the city in the Tradewinds Market district. They\'re on the east side of the lower level.\n\nThat reminds me. I need to go double-check my account after this shift is over. They don\'t offer overdraft protection.', 'The bank. Aye. You\'ll find the bankers in the northwest corner of the city in the Tradewinds Market district. They\'re on the east side of the lower level.\n\nThat reminds me. I need to go double-check my account after this shift is over. They don\'t offer overdraft protection.', 160195, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, hey $c. What\'s shakin\'?', '', 160194, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s dive!', 'Let\'s dive!', 160193, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Perfect. Let\'s see here...\n\n<Hobart flips through a soggy manual.>\n\nSafety rules three through seventeen are unimportant and boring. You ready to go?', '', 160192, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t leave my headlamp on too long. Understood.', 'Don\'t leave my headlamp on too long. Understood.', 160191, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sweet. Rule number two: DON\'T LEAVE YOUR HEADLAMP ON.\n\nSeriously. Don\'t leave your headlamp on for longer than, oh, I dunno, twenty seconds or so. Unless you wanna get eaten by a shark. You see a shark, you turn that light off. Understood?', '', 160190, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t take my helmet off. Got it.', 'Don\'t take my helmet off. Got it.', 160189, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Great! Rule number one: Keep your helmet on at all times.\n\nI don\'t care about no water-breathing magical flim-flam. The pressure down there will crush |5$r\'s skull. Plus, I\'ll be using a static-proof earpiece to communicate with you during the mission. Got it?', '', 160188, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, I\'m paying attention.', 'Yes, I\'m paying attention.', 160187, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Aha! Our diver\'s here!\n\nYour timing\'s perfect. I just finished patching up the last hole in the air hose.\n\nI got a few diver\'s safety rules for you before we go. You payin\' attention?', '', 160186, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I would shut my mouth if I were you.', 160185, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can\'t we talk this out? I mean, this is pretty mild as far as side effects--', '', 160184, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh... it\'s YOU. My, my, this IS a delight!', '', 160183, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'How could those monsters do this?', 160182, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113854, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Woah! Hey, hey, hey! You mind putting the pointy things down?!', '', 160181, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We must find a way to endure.', 160180, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113846, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Explain yourself!', 160179, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I will be waiting in the shadows, $n. Should you have need of me, just call.', 160178, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'My advice: avoid wells of magical energy. Not only will you become addicted, you will devolve into some flavor of... derivative elf.', 160177, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114788, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'No, I am NOT into blindfolds. Well... perhaps a little.', 160176, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114787, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I like you. Say... would you happen to have a twin brother?', 160175, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114786, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Attempt to stop me from taking him away, and die... or remain there, kneeling in the dirt, and live.', 160174, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113858, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'King Anduin gave me a hearthstone back to Stormwind. There I will tend my love\'s wounds... and help my people find respite from this madness.', 160173, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 113860, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s get out of here.', 'Let\'s get out of here.', 160172, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Honorguard will clean up the rest of this mess. Are you quite ready?', '', 160171, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Stand ready.', 160170, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114785, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Champion!', 160169, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114784, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Watch out!', 160168, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114783, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|cFF0000FF(Quest)|r Take us to Marshal Valentine\'s shipwreck, in the middle of the Great Sea.', '|cFF0000FF(Quest)|r Take us to Marshal Valentine\'s shipwreck, in the middle of the Great Sea.', 160167, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This way.', 160166, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114782, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hail and well met, traveler. What can I help you with today?', 'Hail and well met, traveler. What can I help you with today?', 160165, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Over here!', 160164, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114781, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'In her light, all truths are revealed.', 160163, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113853, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('De Azerite... this not... what Zul promised...', '', 160162, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ya efforts are in vain! De powers of de Azerite flow through me!', '', 160161, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fall back! We\'ll catch them on the other side!', 'Fall back! We\'ll catch them on the other side!', 160160, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We got ye, $p!', '', 160159, 0, 0, 22, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would like to trade.', 'I would like to trade.', 160158, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s get back to the portal.', '', 160157, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It is my honor to serve Elune.', 160156, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113852, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I speak for my people.', 160155, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113851, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Our foes will know our fury.', 160154, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113845, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have your mother\'s heart.', '', 160153, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t think anyone should lose their home. Not if it makes them feel like that.', '', 160152, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mother spoke of it sometimes. I... I think it made her cry.', '', 160151, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The kaldorei will endure.', 160150, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113844, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We were... not ourselves. It is difficult to explain, boy.', '', 160149, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Didn\'t it make everyone sad?', '', 160148, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That was long ago.', '', 160147, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You told me that we orcs once lost our home.', '', 160146, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'There is a time for patience... and a time for action.', 160145, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113843, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why?', '', 160144, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I feel bad that the elves lost their tree.', '', 160143, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Then your boon I shall restore to the powers below!', '', 160142, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Grant me your might to put down our foes...', '', 160141, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Though punish us whilst against your will we abuse.', '', 160140, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We will fight to protect our future.', 160139, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113842, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yet your power permit us to harness, to use...', '', 160138, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Heed the voice of Elune.', 160137, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 113841, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We will see, boy. We will see.', '', 160136, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you think this war is going to change the Horde?', '', 160135, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The oceans will remain long after mankind.', '', 160134, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wars never change. Only the warriors do.', '', 160133, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is this a bad war? I mean... worse than the others?', '', 160132, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tides that churn and ties that bind...', '', 160131, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What is it, boy?', '', 160130, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Father?', '', 160129, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Mount Mugamba is a savage, unforgiving place. Guarded by a tribe of giant gorillas and surrounded by treacherous cliffs, the Horde is unlikely to come looking for us here.', 160128, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'When you wish to return to Darkshore as it appears in the present, you have but to ask.', 160127, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will, Father.', '', 160126, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Remember that, boy.', '', 160125, 0, 0, 25, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('War is a test of honor. Once lost, it is not easily reclaimed.', '', 160124, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('War brings out the worst in everyone.', '', 160123, 0, 0, 274, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I heard other children talking about the war. Did... did the Horde do something bad?', '', 160122, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You are quiet. More so than usual.', '', 160121, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, Father?', '', 160120, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Boy.', '', 160119, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This land is full of wonderful and interesting creatures. Just as our temple defenders pride themselves on being stalwart and capable in battle, I pride myself on training my pets to be as capable as possible, they are dedicated to their skills in battle.  Are yours up to the challenge?', '', 160118, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can you show me what the world was like before the burning of Teldrassil?', 'Can you show me what the world was like before the burning of Teldrassil?', 160117, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hang on... did you just make a crack about my weight? I was carrying a very important chest, you know!', '', 160116, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114510, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is done. Grab the scepter and let\'s get out of here!', '', 160115, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get away from that!', '', 160114, 0, 0, 22, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Well, you could have ditched that ratty old coat of yours, Flynn.', 160113, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 114520, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blasphemy!', '', 160112, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114511, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fine, fine. We\'ll pick up some fish for the wonderbird and give her a breather before we head back.', '', 160111, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114509, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I don\'t want to run my sweet girl ragged. She\'s had to carry a heavy load today.', 160110, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 114519, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We\'ll head back to the city. But first, Galeheart needs a bit of rest.', 160109, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 114518, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Make room, Taelia. I\'m riding your gryphon on an actual seat this time!', '', 160108, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114570, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Right. While $n pays a visit to Tol Dagor, we should get this chest to Boralus.', '', 160107, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114569, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You are too kind for dis world, $n. Now where was I? Ah, yes. Our doomed escape.', '', 160106, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Much better. Let me continue...', '', 160105, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, dat feels much better.', '', 160104, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nooo! Not... again....', '', 160103, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I feel de life returning to my form! I must have more power!', '', 160102, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Unfortunately, the ship is currently under repairs. Its unwavering service record may have been tarnished; however, I am here to provide you with other means to reach your destination.\n\nA simple portal may not match the thrill of having the wind flow through your hair on the high seas, but you will be able to continue on with your business unimpeded.\n\nPlease, use this portal whenever you feel the need. I am at your service.', 'Unfortunately, the ship is currently under repairs. Its unwavering service record may have been tarnished; however, I am here to provide you with other means to reach your destination.\n\nA simple portal may not match the thrill of having the wind flow through your hair on the high seas, but you will be able to continue on with your business unimpeded.\n\nPlease, use this portal whenever you feel the need. I am at your service.', 160101, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gah!', 'Gah!', 160100, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am going to gut whoever put dis here!', 'I am going to gut whoever put dis here!', 160099, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not again!', 'Not again!', 160098, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Who put dis here?!', 'Who put dis here?!', 160097, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Bridgeport is just ahead! We\'ll land there!', 160096, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114517, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thros awakens!', '', 160095, 0, 0, 463, 64, 0, 113967, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You know you cannot defeat me, Ulfar. But if it is a fight you seek, then you shall have it!', '', 160094, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 113966, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My... power...', 'My... power...', 160093, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Power... greater den I ever experience! I must have more!', 'Power... greater den I ever experience! I must have more!', 160092, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Here you will find de ship dat sails from de Port of Zandalar to de Echo Isles.\n\nIs dat where you are heading?', '', 160091, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'These will do nicely. Let\'s get clear of the ship and give them a try!', 160090, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114167, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Take care of this nuisance, $n.', '', 160089, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You spit on my loa! I will bite your lips off!', 'You spit on my loa! I will bite your lips off!', 160088, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will teach you to disrespect my loa!', 'I will teach you to disrespect my loa!', 160087, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You will pay for dis insult!', 'You will pay for dis insult!', 160086, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why would you do dat?', 'Why would you do dat?', 160085, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What in de name of all de loa do you think you are doing?', 'What in de name of all de loa do you think you are doing?', 160084, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Knock dat off!', 'Knock dat off!', 160083, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s go.', 'Let\'s go.', 160082, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It seems we have a visitor. Care to join me to give our hellos?', '', 160081, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Katherine will stop at nothing to reclaim her son\'s body.\n\nWe will use her emotions to our advantage, to gain the upper hand over her fleet.', '', 160080, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Another ramshackle Alliance scheme thwarted. Still, I suppose congratulations are in order.', '', 160079, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113900, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Alliance has cobbled together their own Azerite-powered war machine. If it\'s even half as potent as ours, it must be destroyed... now!', '', 160078, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113899, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('\"Doom\'s Howl\", indeed. Well done!', '', 160077, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113898, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Horde forces have assembled another Azerite-powered war machine. Destroy it--before they can use it to decimate Stromgarde!', '', 160076, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 113897, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Time to fight fire with fire. Let\'s search one of their ships for some of those Azerite bombs.', 160075, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114166, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I will see justice delivered. First to these pirates, and then to the Ashvane Company.', 160074, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114163, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hang in there, Flynn. Just... don\'t die.', 160073, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114162, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Our location overlooking the Golden Road gives us an excellent vantage point to monitor enemy traffic to and from the Zandalari capital.', '', 160072, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Baiting', 'Baiting', 160071, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So be it, corpse. I will recover Derek\'s body over your dead one.', '', 160070, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But frankly, you can do what you want with Valentine. He means nothing to us.', '', 160069, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, my good man. That is a tactic that I could see working on somebody other than myself...', '', 160068, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Return Derek Proudmoore to my hands, and you shall have your man back.', '', 160067, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Inverting', 'Inverting', 160066, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('When I heard the trolls speak of shadows, I assumed they meant actual shadows. Who knew they were so big on metaphor?', 'When I heard the trolls speak of shadows, I assumed they meant actual shadows. Who knew they were so big on metaphor?', 160065, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('You know what this place needs? Some nice green sludge.', 'You know what this place needs? Some nice green sludge.', 160064, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Intolerable! The water here is much too blue for my liking.', 'Intolerable! The water here is much too blue for my liking.', 160063, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You know, I think I need a new look, too. You\'re looking for Warpweaver Hayri down near the docks.\n\nTo get there, go down to the Grand Bazaar, which is one terrace up from the port. He runs a place on the east side called, The Maelstrom Mercantile.', 'You know, I think I need a new look, too. You\'re looking for Warpweaver Hayri down near the docks.\n\nTo get there, go down to the Grand Bazaar, which is one terrace up from the port. He runs a place on the east side called, The Maelstrom Mercantile.', 160062, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Surely a few body parts scavenged from the battlefield won\'t be noticed.', 'Surely a few body parts scavenged from the battlefield won\'t be noticed.', 160061, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Looking to change your look up a bit? Dere\'s an ethereal named Warpweaver Hayri down in de dock area.\n\nTo find him, first go to de Grand Bazaar one terrace up from de port. You\'ll find him in a place called de Maelstrom Mercantile on de east side.', 'Looking to change your look up a bit? Dere\'s an ethereal named Warpweaver Hayri down in de dock area.\n\nTo find him, first go to de Grand Bazaar one terrace up from de port. You\'ll find him in a place called de Maelstrom Mercantile on de east side.', 160060, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This place isn\'t the Apothecarium, but it\'ll have to do.', 'This place isn\'t the Apothecarium, but it\'ll have to do.', 160059, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You there, you seem like you have some experience in pet battles.  Lets not dance around, want to battle?', '', 160058, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This city is far too open for my tastes. I need dark places like this to complete my work.', 'This city is far too open for my tastes. I need dark places like this to complete my work.', 160057, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Excellent! I sense the power returnin\' tae Azeroth already.', '', 160056, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114026, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Transmogrifier', 'Transmogrifier', 160055, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I sense Azerite nearby... and something drawin\' a great deal o\' power from it! Ye need tae stop it!', '', 160054, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114025, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It wasn\'t until many days later that I realized de horrible truth...\n\nKaiani was dead, killed by her father, but I was to take de blame. \n\n<Zenbaro coughs violently.>\n\nI don\'t think I have much longer. \n\nWould you fetch dis dying man one last drink from de spring?', '', 160053, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In a year\'s time, I had enough for me and Kaiani to run away. \n\nWe made our plan to leave dat night. I told her to meet me near de old merchant road at twilight. \n\nAs soon as de sun set behind de mountains, I ran toward my future.\n\nWhen I reached de merchant road, armed guards were waiting. \n\nDe took me away without saying a word.', '', 160052, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Such a shame... puttin\' their own greed afore the health o\' Azeroth. Thank ye, champion.', '', 160051, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114028, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('During my time working for her father, we became close. \n\nShe begged me to leave de scamps and leave de city, but I knew dere was no escape. \n\nI had no coin. Everything I stole went straight to Rajin. But did it have to?\n\nFrom that day on, for every two coins I stole, I hid one away for myself. \n\n<Zenabo coughs violently.>\n\nI need water, $n. Please...', '', 160050, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I had earned Rajin\'s trust and respect, as much as anyone could. \n\nFor a scamp, that\'s de dream, but I had other things on my mind... \n\nRajin had a daughter, Kaiani. She was everything he was not: honest, kind... beautiful.', '', 160049, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('De boss took notice of my skills early on. \n\nBefore long, I was running personal errands for Rajin himself. \n\nIf someone needed a talking to, I was the guy to do it. \n\nBut trust me, there wasn\'t much talking involved. \n\n<Zenbaro coughs.>\n\nI could use more water, $n.', '', 160048, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Someone in this cave is mining Azerite from the world\'s open wounds. Put a stop to it!', '', 160047, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114027, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me more.', 'Tell me more.', 160046, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is unwise to poke the bear.', '', 160045, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114947, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My ways embrace death as part of the natural cycle. Care for a demonstration?', '', 160044, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114946, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I may be old, but I am not senile. Quit it.', '', 160043, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114945, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stand strong.', '', 160042, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114937, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Strength of the forest go with you.', '', 160041, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114936, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Strike fast. Strike true.', '', 160040, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114935, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be wary of the woods.', '', 160039, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114934, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Maintain the balance.', '', 160038, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114933, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well met, Mainlander.', '', 160037, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114944, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Our roots run deep in this land.', '', 160036, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114943, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We strike back against the darkness.', '', 160035, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114942, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There is a rhythm to life. Can you feel it?', '', 160034, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114941, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Have you come to learn?', '', 160033, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114940, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Choke on this cabbage!', 160032, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My wisdom is not for the faint of heart.', '', 160031, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114939, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What do you ask of the Thornspeakers?', '', 160030, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114938, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How can we bid on what we need when we possess no money?', 'How can we bid on what we need when we possess no money?', 160029, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We haven\'t many valuables left to sell.', 'We haven\'t many valuables left to sell.', 160028, 0, 0, 274, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This should be enough to afford supplies... I hope.', 'This should be enough to afford supplies... I hope.', 160027, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How much gold do we have remaining?', 'How much gold do we have remaining?', 160026, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do we have anything valuable left to sell?', 'Do we have anything valuable left to sell?', 160025, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m not sure goblin bankers are a step up from those copper-pinching Montagues.', 'I\'m not sure goblin bankers are a step up from those copper-pinching Montagues.', 160024, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shake harder! Wait... not too hard!', '', 160023, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114567, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I can\'t shake the last one!', 160022, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 114515, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We fled so suddenly, I had to leave everything behind!', 'We fled so suddenly, I had to leave everything behind!', 160021, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Get away from here, $r!', 160020, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'They will hunt you down, $r!', 160019, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Get out of Stormwind, $r!', 160018, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let us see who Proudmoore has sent now.', '', 160017, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stop!', 'Stop!', 160016, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thought you could get past us, did ya?', 'Thought you could get past us, did ya?', 160015, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ha! Caught ya snoopin\' around.', 'Ha! Caught ya snoopin\' around.', 160014, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Git outta here, ya Horde scum!', 'Git outta here, ya Horde scum!', 160013, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'OUTRIGGERS! OPEN FIRE!', 160012, 0, 0, 0, 70, 3180, 0, 114024, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Power restored. Continue prime directive. Exterminate!', 'Power restored. Continue prime directive. Exterminate!', 160011, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll be prying that hammer from your cold dead hands!', 'I\'ll be prying that hammer from your cold dead hands!', 160010, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We have something for every taste here!', 160009, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I see a $r that could use some vitamins!', 160008, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You look like you could use a ripe turnip!', 160007, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'All sorts of things for sale here!', 160006, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get away from there!', '', 160005, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Halt!', '', 160004, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What are you doing there?!', '', 160003, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stop right there!', '', 160002, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Show your face, Horde scum! We have a friend of yours.', '', 160001, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m getting out of here as soon as it\'s clear. I\'ll see you back at Grandma\'s house, good luck!', '', 160000, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Where do we go from here, Warchief?', 'Where do we go from here, Warchief?', 159999, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s a piece of cake to bake a pretty cake!', '', 159998, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('One of the Darkspear by the name of Foreman Al\'jibo is handling that for most of our forces. You can find him at the Hall of Ancient Paths just inside the Great Seal on the east side.', 'One of the Darkspear by the name of Foreman Al\'jibo is handling that for most of our forces. You can find him at the Hall of Ancient Paths just inside the Great Seal on the east side.', 159997, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Looking to offload some of those ill-gotten gains? I hear ya. What good is going on campaign if there aren\'t spoils? Am I right? Or, maybe you just needs some repairs?\n\nWhat kind of merchant are you looking for?', 'Looking to offload some of those ill-gotten gains? I hear ya. What good is going on campaign if there aren\'t spoils? Am I right? Or, maybe you just needs some repairs?\n\nWhat kind of merchant are you looking for?', 159996, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pin\'jin the Patient is the one you want to learn more about Tailoring. Steady hand with a needle for embroidering your robes and knows how to sew you up real nice, to boot. Reattached my arm the other day.\n\nLook for him behind the blathering nobles down at the Terrace of Crafters on the west side of Dazar\'alor.', 'Pin\'jin the Patient is the one you want to learn more about Tailoring. Steady hand with a needle for embroidering your robes and knows how to sew you up real nice, to boot. Reattached my arm the other day.\n\nLook for him behind the blathering nobles down at the Terrace of Crafters on the west side of Dazar\'alor.', 159995, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Feel free to give\'m a spin any time and see for yourself!', '', 159994, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m just going to flat out state the obvious... Rana the Cutta has to be one of the best skinners in the world. Have you seen the wildlife around here?\n\nLook for her down at the Terrace of Crafters at the base of the pyramid on the west side of Dazar\'alor.', 'I\'m just going to flat out state the obvious... Rana the Cutta has to be one of the best skinners in the world. Have you seen the wildlife around here?\n\nLook for her down at the Terrace of Crafters at the base of the pyramid on the west side of Dazar\'alor.', 159993, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mining? Delicious. If I were a miner, I\'d mine right into their fabled \"City of Gold\", Atal\'Dazar. Just don\'t get caught, $n.\n\nIf you\'re looking for more training, speak with Secott the Goldsmith. To find him, head down to the Terrace of Crafters on the lower, west side of Dazar\'alor.', 'Mining? Delicious. If I were a miner, I\'d mine right into their fabled \"City of Gold\", Atal\'Dazar. Just don\'t get caught, $n.\n\nIf you\'re looking for more training, speak with Secott the Goldsmith. To find him, head down to the Terrace of Crafters on the lower, west side of Dazar\'alor.', 159992, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'When you wish to return to Tirisfal Glades as it appears in the present, you have but to ask.', 159991, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This thing is the bomb! No, seriously, it could blow the top hat off of Gallywix\'s pleasure palace!', '', 159990, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 114043, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, makes a goblin proud, ya know?', '', 159989, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 114044, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A couple of dashes of my secret ingredient... and voila! The modifications are complete!', '', 159987, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114042, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A little gunpowder... some fuses and copper chips...', '', 159986, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114041, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll add in a bit of this. Smash it in reeeeal good.', '', 159985, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lemme just... hold on a second, will ya?', '', 159984, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 114039, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oooh, you got me some Azerite? That\'s the good stuff...', '', 159983, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 114038, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You want explosions? Buddy, you got it. Hop into one of these beauties and take it for a spin.', '', 159982, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 114037, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hands off my potion!', 'Hands off my potion!', 159981, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mista Nice not want me talkin\' to adults.', '', 159980, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Busted gears and wires hang from this broken harvester.', 'Busted gears and wires hang from this broken harvester.', 159979, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A worn hammer rests on the table.', 'A worn hammer rests on the table.', 159978, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Repair the harvester.', 'Repair the harvester.', 159977, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Have you seen the leather armor the Zandalari fashion? If you\'re looking to learn their secrets, head down to the Terrace of Crafters on the lower, west side of Dazar\'alor.\n\nOnce you\'re down there, be on the lookout for Xanjo. He\'s their resident leatherworking expert.', 'Have you seen the leather armor the Zandalari fashion? If you\'re looking to learn their secrets, head down to the Terrace of Crafters on the lower, west side of Dazar\'alor.\n\nOnce you\'re down there, be on the lookout for Xanjo. He\'s their resident leatherworking expert.', 159976, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Retrieve the hammer.', 'Retrieve the hammer.', 159975, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Examine the potion\'s properties.', 'Examine the potion\'s properties.', 159974, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Derek will be returned to us... one way or another.', '', 159973, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|A:Warfronts-BaseMapIcons-Alliance-MainHall-Minimap:25:23:0:0|aNew construction available!', '|A:Warfronts-BaseMapIcons-Alliance-MainHall-Minimap:25:23:0:0|aNew construction available!', 159972, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The bottle is filled with a strange swirling liquid.', 'The bottle is filled with a strange swirling liquid.', 159971, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
