('', 'Regardless of what your warchief wants, I must return to my people. We are going to Zuldazar, as dis is my ship and dis is your only way out of Stormwind.\n\nDo you have a problem with dat?', 148274, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not at all.', 'Not at all.', 148273, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll cut ye down ta size!', 'I\'ll cut ye down ta size!', 148272, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 99217, 99218, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Face the might o\' the mountain!', 'Face the might o\' the mountain!', 148271, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 99215, 99216, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll teach ye to challenge a Dark Iron!', 'I\'ll teach ye to challenge a Dark Iron!', 148270, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 99213, 99214, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ye don\'t belong here!', 'Ye don\'t belong here!', 148269, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 99211, 99212, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m ready.', 'I\'m ready.', 148267, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve seen \'er myself, the witch of the woods! I\'m getting out before she finds me again!', '', 148266, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How can we be expected to keep working in these conditions?', '', 148265, 0, 0, 6, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All Algerson wants is money, but we\'ve got bigger problems here.', '', 148264, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There\'s a witch in these woods, and she\'s angry! I quit!', '', 148263, 0, 0, 412, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Them beasts ain\'t natural! It\'s the witch!', '', 148262, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We have to get to work figuring out how to kill Zulajin.', '', 148261, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('De infection is gone! And it is... thanks to you and $n.', '', 148260, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You are right. I should be dead. But that doesn\'t mean I\'m going to let you die. Now hold on!', '', 148259, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Agh! You are killing me! Exile is too kind for you!', '', 148258, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dis is some strong voodoo infecting you... stay still, I almost have it!', '', 148257, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hold still, Zaluto. We are going to cure your infection.', 'Hold still, Zaluto. We are going to cure your infection.', 148256, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Their \"prophet\" has been proven false.', '', 148255, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 115039, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dey say Rastakhan has no power here. Show dem de error of their ways. Drive their heresy from Tal\'gurub.', '', 148254, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 115038, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Thank you for your hard work recovering dese artifacts.', 148253, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 110715, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Atal\'Gral fell into de sea, but all is not lost. We must recover what we can of de loa\'s temple.', 148252, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 110714, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nature bless you, friend! Good luck!', 'Nature bless you, friend! Good luck!', 148251, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thank you for freeing me!', 'Thank you for freeing me!', 148250, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('At least... I died fightin\'...', 'At least... I died fightin\'...', 148249, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109581, 109582, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah... bested at last...', 'Ah... bested at last...', 148248, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109579, 109580, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So this... is what it feels like...', 'So this... is what it feels like...', 148247, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109577, 109578, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bury me... with my rum...', 'Bury me... with my rum...', 148246, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109575, 109576, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll run ya through!', 'I\'ll run ya through!', 148245, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109573, 109574, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s a watery grave for you.', 'It\'s a watery grave for you.', 148244, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109571, 109572, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Show yer steel!', 'Show yer steel!', 148243, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109569, 109570, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('To whomever reads this - do not trust the sisterhood\'s magic!\n\nI don\'t know where they came from, but their circle grew in secret in the dark places of Corlain. Now, they have taken to the streets, killing all who stand in their way and hunting the others with their wicker abominations!\n\nNobody knows what they want. All they speak of is revenge for their master, and glory to their traitorous leader, \"The Mother.\"\n\nI don\'t think I will make it out of Corlain alive. I can only hope my words reach someone who can take action. Do not allow these \"sisters\" into your town! Their corruption will devour it from the inside, just like it has Corlain!', 'To whomever reads this - do not trust the sisterhood\'s magic!\n\nI don\'t know where they came from, but their circle grew in secret in the dark places of Corlain. Now, they have taken to the streets, killing all who stand in their way and hunting the others with their wicker abominations!\n\nNobody knows what they want. All they speak of is revenge for their master, and glory to their traitorous leader, \"The Mother.\"\n\nI don\'t think I will make it out of Corlain alive. I can only hope my words reach someone who can take action. Do not allow these \"sisters\" into your town! Their corruption will devour it from the inside, just like it has Corlain!', 148242, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There has been a third disappearance this week. The guards insist there is nothing to be worried about, but I know better.\n\nI spoke with Mr. Knowlton just last night, and he saw the body of Jon the stablehand, who was the first to go missing. The image was burned in his brain, he said - profane markings covering the wall of his servant\'s shack, and his body sprawled on his cart, a gaping hole in his chest where his heart used to be.\n\nKnowlton is gone, now, and the guards are silent.\n\nI feel that Corlain is no longer safe for me and my family. Once we are able, we should relocate to Arom\'s Stand.', 'There has been a third disappearance this week. The guards insist there is nothing to be worried about, but I know better.\n\nI spoke with Mr. Knowlton just last night, and he saw the body of Jon the stablehand, who was the first to go missing. The image was burned in his brain, he said - profane markings covering the wall of his servant\'s shack, and his body sprawled on his cart, a gaping hole in his chest where his heart used to be.\n\nKnowlton is gone, now, and the guards are silent.\n\nI feel that Corlain is no longer safe for me and my family. Once we are able, we should relocate to Arom\'s Stand.', 148241, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ceridwen keeps trying to get me to join her \"sister circle.\"\n\nI don\'t like it. Every day that passes I see more and more girls about town wearing the wicker charm. At this pace, the whole town is going to join before I know it.\n\nAnd the men don\'t even seem to notice - they\'re even more oblivious than usual. It\'s almost as if they\'re under some sort of spell.', 'Ceridwen keeps trying to get me to join her \"sister circle.\"\n\nI don\'t like it. Every day that passes I see more and more girls about town wearing the wicker charm. At this pace, the whole town is going to join before I know it.\n\nAnd the men don\'t even seem to notice - they\'re even more oblivious than usual. It\'s almost as if they\'re under some sort of spell.', 148240, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('At last, there is a light of hope for Drustvar. Lady Waycrest emerged from the manor today to help assuage the fears of the townspeople due to Lord Waycrest\'s absence. \n\nShe assured us that the Lord is in good health, but it was rather peculiar the way that she ordered about the guards. She had never wielded that kind of authority before.\n\nI\'m sure I\'m just overthinking it. After the trials of the past few weeks, we should take whatever blessings we can get.', 'At last, there is a light of hope for Drustvar. Lady Waycrest emerged from the manor today to help assuage the fears of the townspeople due to Lord Waycrest\'s absence. \n\nShe assured us that the Lord is in good health, but it was rather peculiar the way that she ordered about the guards. She had never wielded that kind of authority before.\n\nI\'m sure I\'m just overthinking it. After the trials of the past few weeks, we should take whatever blessings we can get.', 148239, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is the third night that our Maggie has secreted away when she thought her father and I were asleep. I tried to follow, but I lost her outside the courtyard to Waycrest Manor.\n\nThe Daveys said that their girl has also gone missing some nights, only to return as mysteriously as she left, acting as if nothing is the matter. \n\nHer father swears he saw her enter the manor, but that\'s preposterous. Nobody has been in or out of that manor in weeks!', 'This is the third night that our Maggie has secreted away when she thought her father and I were asleep. I tried to follow, but I lost her outside the courtyard to Waycrest Manor.\n\nThe Daveys said that their girl has also gone missing some nights, only to return as mysteriously as she left, acting as if nothing is the matter. \n\nHer father swears he saw her enter the manor, but that\'s preposterous. Nobody has been in or out of that manor in weeks!', 148238, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We cannot survive without help from the loa.', '', 148236, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stand and deliver!', 'Stand and deliver!', 148235, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109567, 109568, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It has been a fortnight since anyone in Corlain has seen or heard from Lord or Lady Waycrest. Solicitors are turned back by the gate guards with no word on their condition.\n\nRumors are abound that the lord is suffering from a wasting sickness, and that the lady is so grief-stricken she has locked herself in his chambers.\n\nThese are truly dark times for Drustvar.', 'It has been a fortnight since anyone in Corlain has seen or heard from Lord or Lady Waycrest. Solicitors are turned back by the gate guards with no word on their condition.\n\nRumors are abound that the lord is suffering from a wasting sickness, and that the lady is so grief-stricken she has locked herself in his chambers.\n\nThese are truly dark times for Drustvar.', 148234, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll cut ya from stem to stern!', 'I\'ll cut ya from stem to stern!', 148233, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109565, 109566, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'ll pay for this...', 'You\'ll pay for this...', 148232, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109003, 109004, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ashvane... will prevail...', 'Ashvane... will prevail...', 148231, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 109001, 109002, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Damn it all...', 'Damn it all...', 148230, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 108999, 109000, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rats...', 'Rats...', 148229, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 108997, 108998, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
