('Who are you? Where is Lord Nimrod and Lady Dyana?', 'Who are you? Where is Lord Nimrod and Lady Dyana?', 121248, 0, 43384, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look, Marius here can see things that will scare you so stark you\'ll look like me.$b$bBut even he is getting all twitchy about this cave. Something about bad dreams and corrupted elves and whatever.$b$bBah! We tracked a powerful satyr to this cave and I\'ll be damned... more... if we don\'t at least try to enslave it.', '', 121247, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The spread has slowed, thanks to your bravery, $n.', 121246, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73036, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Now is not the time for a chat. Your temple is under attack!', 121245, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Nightmare spreads like a pox on the land! We might put a stop to it here before it continues to corrupt Val\'sharah!', 121244, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73037, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fine, fine! They went that way. Not that it matters, you will never catch up...', '', 121243, 0, 43861, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How did you get this invitation? Never mind, the hunt\'s already started!', '', 121242, 0, 43861, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mysterious whispers offer untold power for your services...', 'Mysterious whispers offer untold power for your services...', 121241, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Calm down, I\'m sure she will be here soon.', '', 121240, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The people are safe from hydras, at least for another season.', 121239, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73074, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It is near to birthing season for the hydras along Bradensbrook\'s coastline. We must prevent them from swelling to dangerous numbers so they don\'t pose a threat to the village.', 121238, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73075, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The coffee here is really strong!', 121237, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Some may think it heartless to slaughter the creatures, but the stalemate must be maintained lest one side will emerge the victor and swim to the mainland.', 121236, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73076, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'When is Phoe\'be getting here? She said she would be here over an hour ago!', 121235, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The island of Gloaming Reef is the site of a constant battle between murloc and makrura. At times, one side gains an advantage and we have to step in to keep the struggle going.', 121234, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73077, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'They put our druids to sleep in shark-infested waters? I am glad you arrived when you did.', 121233, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73038, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The druids who watch over Emerald Bay haven\'t returned from their patrol. Perhaps the sprites are up to something...', 121232, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73039, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Nightmare seeks to corrupt our entire forest!', 121231, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73040, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'A Dream Warden is under attack by the Nightmare! May Elune bless your path as you save the sacred dragon.', 121230, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73041, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We shall pick apart our enemies piece by piece, like a mana bun. Oh - now I am hungry.', 121229, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70521, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I have some high value targets for you. You would do well to call upon our more... unsavory allies.', 121228, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70520, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Nature\'s beauty still shines through even in these dire times.', 121227, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73042, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Some wisps have the extraordinary ability to encourage the rapid maturation of saplings into trees. Seek the Hidden Pools and bond with a wisp there.', 121226, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73043, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is $n seeing anyone? Do you think I\'d have a chance?', 'Is $n seeing anyone? Do you think I\'d have a chance?', 121225, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Looking smooth, $n! Real smooth!', 'Looking smooth, $n! Real smooth!', 121224, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'That squirrel invasion was nuts. Get it?', 121223, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73044, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look at $n! There goes a rogue with a true sense of style!', 'Look at $n! There goes a rogue with a true sense of style!', 121222, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'What the... What jokester spread so many acorns in Lorlathil? I realize this task is of the humble variety, but could you relocate some of those squirrels and crack a few nuts while you\'re at it?', 121221, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73045, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Thank you. It is easy to ignore such threats until it is too late to push them back.', 121220, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73046, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Naga have overrun the ruins of Kal\'delar. If they\'re allowed to gain a foothold, they could threaten the entire coastline.', 121219, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 73047, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Loan him Sharas\'dal, the Scepter of Tides.>', '<Loan him Sharas\'dal, the Scepter of Tides.>', 121218, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Move closer, bring your head close to his, and listen to the Oracle\'s ancient wisdom.>', '<Move closer, bring your head close to his, and listen to the Oracle\'s ancient wisdom.>', 121217, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Loan him the Doomhammer.>', '<Loan him the Doomhammer.>', 121216, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Thank him for his time.>', '<Thank him for his time.>', 121215, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Shake your head no.>', '<Shake your head no.>', 121214, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Nod affirmatively.>', '<Nod affirmatively.>', 121213, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Morgl looks very pleased with himself.>', '', 121212, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s bows deeply in gratitude.', '', 121211, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Urg blurgle murgle blek! Wurg $ct $n blergle-blerk. Wurgle, wurg.', '', 121210, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wurgle! Blerg arglebleg. Murgle urg blerk of Tides!', '', 121209, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Morgl is puzzled by your response. After composing himself, he continues:>\n\nUrgleblerg mra\'graggle berk urgleblag. Murgle urg grablurg urgle blerg ur Lake Minnetonka burgle bleg. Urg urkegle blerk murgle-gurgle, Azshara glurg\'ug. \n\nGurg blurgle urg-mulurk, \"Sharas\'dal\" gurp blergle urkle-klep. Blergle, $n?\n\n<The Oracle indicates the scepter you carry, then motions urgently for you to hand it to him.>', '', 121208, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blerk.', '', 121207, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Morgl is glad you feel that way. He looks toward the sky contemplatively.>\n\nWarg gurg blergargle mruk, mruk. $ct $n urgle blorglug mragle urk. Mrawgle urg 10,000 blerg \"Ra\" barg urglebleg, urg \"Ra-den\" blek Mogu berkblug.\n\n<His eager attention focuses back on you.>\n\nMrgle urg blurg\'urg gerblagle. Graggle merg blur Gurgle of the Storm. Wurgle! Berk blergle-berk urg grablag. $n: urg garble murk gerblerg? Urk?\n\n<The murloc oracle leans forward, motioning for you to come closer. He wants to whisper something to you. For you... and you alone.>', '', 121206, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s gurgles, happily.', '', 121205, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is clear that %s has no idea what he is doing.', '', 121204, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s begins smashing the Doomhammer around indiscriminately.', '', 121203, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Warg! Gra-blergle! BLEEERRGGHammer!', '', 121202, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Morgl nods, sadly. The old murloc turns away from you to contemplate the undulating grey sea, saying nothing more.>', '', 121201, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Herk! Blargleblag Doomhammer gurg blerklefirk glup urglegurbler.\n\nUrgle glugblag Orgrim, urgle glugblag Thrall, glup urgle glugblag \"$ct $n\" gruggleblurg murgleglub!\n\n<A thin tendril of spittle slowly snakes down from the corner of Morgl\'s mouth. He continues speaking, urgent and unrelentingly:>\n\nMraagggle urg blerg murgleurgleurgle gurk! Wurgleblerg murgle urg? Blerk! Glerg! Mwagle?\n\n<The Oracle gestures to the Doomhammer and beckons you to hand it over.>', '', 121200, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I can see a lot of potential in the surrounding area! I can now transport you to Suramar from Skyhold, $ct.', 121199, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'There\'s a small path through the trees here! I can now transport you to Val\'sharah from Skyhold, $ct.', 121198, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gurg urggle blerg\'urk urgle blark.\n\nBlerglearg urk $ct urgle blurg? Glerk! Gurg urggle ble\'blerg, erks ker-blerk, gurgler.\n\n<The wizened murloc softly chuckles to himself, then turns deadly serious:>\n\nGlergurg blergbergle, $n. Gulg ble\'blergle: gurg urggle kek, glup gurg urggle blarkleblag? Blerg?', '', 121197, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This area is well protected by the blue dragons. I can now transport you to Azsuna from Skyhold, $ct.', 121196, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I think you will spend quite a bit of time at Valdisdall, $ct. I can now transport you directly there from Skyhold.', 121195, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We\'ve come to end your reign, Illidan. My people, and all of Outland, shall be free!', '', 121194, 0, 0, 66, 94, 0, 11389, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hello there. Good news! My books have arrived at last, well most of them.\n\nYou still look confused, so let me explain again. You see, when we last teleported Dalaran, some of my books were damaged. And so this time I had them fly to our new location. Yes, fly.\n\nUnfortunately, they were halfway over Khaz Modan when we teleported again. Most just arrived last week and are settling back in around the city. A few of them are still on loan to some colleagues, and should return themselves soon. Actually, if they are out much longer I might have to go investigate.', '', 121193, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Quel\'vala thonos.  Nobility through tradition. I thank you, outlander.', 121192, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70917, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I will follow you through. Thank you for allowing me to accompany you.', 121191, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
