('Archmage Vargoth, what is the source of your power?', 'Archmage Vargoth, what is the source of your power?', 119737, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tidecaller, shield me!', '', 119736, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Scaleguard, freeze them to their bones!', '', 119735, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I believe I know a way I can help you, Conjurer.', '', 119734, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 69219, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I believe I know a way I can help you, small one.', '', 119733, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 69220, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Su\'esh begins to thrash nervously. Turn back before she throws you off!', 'Su\'esh begins to thrash nervously. Turn back before she throws you off!', 119732, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Free at last! I\'ve been a prisoner of their beliefs for far too long.', 'Free at last! I\'ve been a prisoner of their beliefs for far too long.', 119731, 0, 0, 603, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have given me a second chance. I will not waste it.', 'You have given me a second chance. I will not waste it.', 119730, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thank you, $n. I will not forget your kindness.', 'Thank you, $n. I will not forget your kindness.', 119729, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'ve shown me more mercy than I deserve.', 'You\'ve shown me more mercy than I deserve.', 119728, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Su\'esh roars happily at $n.', '', 119727, 0, 0, 53, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You be careful out there!', 'You be careful out there!', 119726, 7, 0, 396, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey! I wasn\'t finished yet.', 'Hey! I wasn\'t finished yet.', 119725, 7, 0, 396, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bring it back in one piece!', 'Bring it back in one piece!', 119724, 7, 0, 396, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Careful with that thing!', 'Careful with that thing!', 119723, 7, 0, 396, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re right, but how can we ever hope to tap into that safely? Our power will only...\n\n<Tyrosus pauses.>\n\nThe Ebon Blade.', '', 119722, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There cannot be Light without Shadow. We must strike a balance.', 'There cannot be Light without Shadow. We must strike a balance.', 119721, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I see.\n\nI trust your wisdom, Highlord, but I can\'t say that this sits well with me. \n\nHow can we ever be sure that the power within that thing won\'t... change you?', '', 119720, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve recovered a dark, but powerful crystal, Maxwell.\n\nIf we can harness its power it might prove useful against the Legion.', 'I\'ve recovered a dark, but powerful crystal, Maxwell. If we can harness its power it might prove useful against the Legion.', 119719, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you feel it as well, Highlord? Something isn\'t right.', '', 119718, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I feel a dark presence nearby...', '', 119717, 0, 0, 661, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not bad... not bad.  Green eyes though?  Mine were grey.', '', 119716, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 69313, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No. Lower caste. Won\'t do at all.', '', 119715, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 69312, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You know, I\'ve been rather missing having some skin on my bones.  Maybe there\'s something we can do about that?', '', 119714, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 69311, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Before I was devoured ever so slowly I did two things.\n\nThe first, as should be obvious, was putting my necromantic learnings to the test, sealing my soul within the phylactery you found. It did nothing for the pain of death... but it has served its purpose.\n\nAfterward, as I was already half-consumed by the creature, I hurled the crystal into the river beside you in hopes that someone might still put it to use against the forces of darkness.\n\n<The lich\'s face contorts into something of a smile.>\n\nIf you seek it, you will find it there.', '', 119713, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What happened to the crystal?', 'What happened to the crystal?', 119712, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I devised a way to fight the scourge using their own magic against them. It was a simple process, really - I had a veritable river of souls at my disposable from the Lich King\'s rampage.\n\nIn the end, I created a counterpart to the holy relic that fuels the Ashbringer\'s strength, but before I could properly seal it within a suitable blade I was found out by Isillien and his dogs.\n\nThe rest, as they say, was excruciatingly painful.', '', 119711, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All conduits are active. Can you amplify the feed?', 'All conduits are active. Can you amplify the feed?', 119710, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And what was that?', 'And what was that?', 119709, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Take the book.>', '<Take the book.>', 119708, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I suspect you know. We would not be meeting otherwise.\n\nMy story is simple. The original wielder of your blade proved unable to stand against the endless throngs of undead that threatened our world.\n\nI sought a different approach... one that could not fail.', '', 119707, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Are you mad? That\'s the farthest thing from nice I could imagine, short of ripping my beard out hair by luxuriant hair.', '', 119706, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What happened to you?', 'What happened to you?', 119705, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You will find no fight here, paladin. I can do you no harm, and bear no allegiance to the dark creatures you seek to destroy.', '', 119704, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, the Ashbringer yet lives. Curious.', '', 119703, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Go away. I\'ve no time to be patronized.', '', 119702, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What did you do then?', 'What did you do then?', 119701, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s terrible.', 'That\'s terrible.', 119700, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What did you write down?', 'What did you write down?', 119699, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wouldn\'t believe them?', 'I wouldn\'t believe them?', 119698, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s nice.', 'That\'s nice.', 119697, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What did you do?', 'What did you do?', 119696, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pah, no respect for your elders.', '', 119695, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I agree, $n.', '', 119694, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I bought this one back, but the rest were long gone. Paid a pretty penny for it too, golds where that blasted fool got coppers. I\'ve been searching high and low, but haven\'t been able to find more than rumors of the rest. These old bones aren\'t as up for adventuring as they were.', '', 119693, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wrote the story of this order. But that blasted apprentice lost all of them. All of them! It\'s ridiculous, I tell you. He sold them for mere coppers a page!', '', 119692, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I searched the world high and low for information! I wrote down everything. Even the inconsequential things. I\'ve seen things you would not believe, $Glad:lass;. Things you would not believe!', '', 119691, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Kids these days, no respect for archival. When I was an apprentice, why, I cared!', '', 119690, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I cannot afford to dispose of the wretch here; the attention it would draw if he were found would only further complicate my glorious work.\n\nNo... I have a better idea. I will bring him to death\'s very door and leave him in the Plaguelands. \n\nThere is a particularly vile slime on the river\'s edge that will ensure not a trace remains of the traitorous louse... if I can find the damned creature.', '', 119689, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Turn the page.>', '<Turn the page.>', 119688, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Victory to the Valarjar! Victory to the Battlelord!', '', 119687, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 69284, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<One of the sections in particular is slightly more worn than the others.>\n\n...the loathsome wizard is more resilient than I had first expected.\n\nStill, showing him the Light\'s wrath has been one of my great joys these past few weeks. The heathen deserves worse - who would dare try to create something so foul from the very shadows we seek to destroy?!\n\nI knew his kind were not to be trusted.', '', 119686, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let it be known! Today, thanks to the new Battlelord of the Valarjar we have won our first decisive victory against the Legion in one of their own worlds.', '', 119685, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 69283, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thorim... son! Hold them off! I shall send my champions to your aid.', '', 119684, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 68400, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'m afraid I don\'t know.\n\nOnly the crusaders that killed him know the truth, and none among their ranks live to reveal it.\n\nI would search their former holds for answers.', 119683, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I do not know.\n\nThey say that only the crusade knows the truth, and they have been all but eradicated.\n\nPerhaps you might find the answers you seek in one of their former holds.', '', 119682, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The halls of Ulduar have been overrun by the armies of the Legion. We are fighting bravely but their numbers are endless.', '', 119681, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 68399, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Father! Though we are oathbound to answer the call of the Gjallarhorn, we cannot.', '', 119680, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 68398, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Armies of Ulduar, heed Odyn\'s call!', '', 119679, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 68390, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you know anything more about what this wizard created to deserve such a fate?', 'Do you know anything more about what this wizard created to deserve such a fate?', 119678, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('She was a dwarf if I am not mistaken - and I am not often mistaken.\n\nShe came here with a copy of that very book, just as you have today, but had no proof of the black drake\'s death, and so my lips remained sealed. She was quite eager to learn about the Ashbringer\'s whereabouts.\n\nPerhaps if you found her, she might be able to enlighten you further.', '', 119677, 0, 924, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He was a Tauren if I am not mistaken - and I am not often mistaken.\n\nHe came here with a copy of that very book, just as you have today, but had no proof of the black drake\'s death, and so my lips remained sealed. He was quite eager to learn about the Ashbringer\'s whereabouts.\n\nPerhaps if you found him, he might be able to enlighten you further.', '', 119676, 0, 923, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Who else sought you out?', 'Who else sought you out?', 119675, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A human mage gave me a copy of that book many years ago. He kept trying to convince me to help him, going on about something to do with fighting fire with fire.\n\nI cannot leave this place, as you know, so that was the last I saw of the strange fellow. He went off to reunite with his allies, I presume.\n\nYou are not the first to inquire about this book, however. I wonder...', '', 119674, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What about this book? Can you tell me what it all means?', 'What about this book? Can you tell me what it all means?', 119673, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, yes. I had heard of Nefarian\'s demise, but it is indeed a treat to see his grisly end firsthand. Were I not stuck in these halls I might pay his lair a visit. \n\nPerhaps one day.\n\nAs for my end of our agreement, the tale of the Ashbringer is one of my favorites, of course.\n\n<The Prince glances at your weapon and smiles.>\n\nBut it would seem you are familiar with that particular tale.', '', 119672, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That was the last of them. I can use what little power I have left to escape. Farewell, friends.', '', 119671, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is the last of my power. Take it and destroy these traitors!', '', 119670, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What?! The Nightborne are upon us!', '', 119669, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That was close. I thought they\'d never stop coming.', '', 119668, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please, hero, we have no time to waste! Come!', '', 119667, 0, 0, 25, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Incoming!', '', 119666, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why not both, your highness? I will tell you the tale of the black drake Nefarian\'s fall, if you would tell me more about this book and the Ashbringer.', 'Why not both, your highness? I will tell you the tale of the black drake Nefarian\'s fall, if you would tell me more about this book and the Ashbringer.', 119665, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is only the beginning. The withered will be drawn to this much energy in one place.', '', 119664, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A single goblin glider kit will cost:', 'A single goblin glider kit will cost:', 119663, 0, 0, 3, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The elementals sense the disturbance here. Defend yourselves!', '', 119662, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Good choice!  Make sure to use it before you hit the ground.  It\'s not much help after that.', 119661, 0, 0, 3, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A smith with enough knowledge can see the details. The scratches on the blade, the wear of the haft tell of battle stresses and where it hits most often. See how easily you balance the heft. The comfort of your grip shows years of experience. While that cannot be forged, I can improve a new weapon in the right places so its wearer strikes more true and lives to earn those years.', '', 119660, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fine, though I have never seen a smith work in such a manner.', '', 119659, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A fine fight I saw! Master Saurfang, I believe $n chose correctly with you. Now, may I see you and your weapon together?', '', 119658, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sure, I\'ll take one.', 'Sure, I\'ll take one.', 119657, 0, 0, 3, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hello, peach!  Be careful if you\'re going to Dalaran Crater, it\'s quite a drop.\n\nI just so happen to have some gliders for sale if you need one though.\n\n10 gold.\n\nNo refunds.', 119656, 0, 0, 3, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Enough! You have proven your ability. I will grant your request.', '', 119655, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is good to see you, friend. I was able to hold them off but I fear more will be upon us soon.', '', 119654, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am here. Let us not waste time!', '', 119653, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Ye should see if ye can find anyone who might know more about this book. I think it\'s hintin\' at somethin\' far bigger than a day o\' fishin\'!', 119652, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Aha! Success!', 119651, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'How fascinatin\'. This Nat Pagle sounds like quite the adventurer!', 119650, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ll press a copy for our archives so ye can keep the finished book, Highlord.', 119649, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s meet back at the Hall of Shadows.', 'Let\'s meet back at the Hall of Shadows.', 119648, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It should only take a moment o\' two. Oh, this is so excitin\'!', 119647, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I must inform the Council of your news. Good luck, $n!', '', 119646, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We have a place for that. Make your way to the Circle of Glory. I will send a val\'kyr to bring this Saurfang.', '', 119645, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Welcome to Dalaran! I\'m happy to assist with anything you need.', '', 119644, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Tell Helgar of Saurfang and his request.>', '<Tell Helgar of Saurfang and his request.>', 119643, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You look pleased. You have found your warrior?', '', 119642, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why have I been brought back to fight for you?', '', 119641, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Of course.', 'Of course.', 119640, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '<Elda carefully thumbs through the pages, her eyes moving rapidly across the weathered text.>\n\nBy the Light, Highlord - I think you\'re right! This must be the one!\n\nI should be able tae piece it back together - allow me just a moment!', 119639, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 603, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I know of your exploits, but I must see them firsthand before I give you what you want. Let us duel.', '', 119638, 0, 924, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sister, could you take a look at these? They might be the missing pieces of the book!', 'Sister, could you take a look at these? They might be the missing pieces of the book!', 119637, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('While I am not interested in helping your Alliance become stronger, the Legion is a threat too great to not take every possible action against.', '', 119636, 0, 924, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ll open it at once. Then I must inform the ranger-general of my findings. Good luck!', 119635, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ve been readin\' about a book written by an expert tradesman that spoke at length about the Ashbringer. \n\nIt seems most copies were lost long ago, their tattered pages scattered tae the winds.\n\nI wonder if it\'s still out there somewhere? I\'m sure we could learn a thing o\' two if we could piece it back together!', 119634, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('King Anduin needs me to get to Dalaran. Can you open a portal?', 'King Anduin needs me to get to Dalaran. Can you open a portal?', 119633, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('When you are ready, send your messenger for me. I will come.', '', 119632, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have seen much battle as well, perhaps it is time to see how far you have come. Let us duel and I will aid your smith.', '', 119631, 0, 923, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I was doing research for Ranger-General Windrunner when all hell broke loose.$b$bWhat do you need?', 119630, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 396, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am honored you and he think so highly of me. It is true I have seen no small amount of battle.', '', 119629, 0, 923, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Tell Saurfang of Helgar\'s request.>', '<Tell Saurfang of Helgar\'s request.>', 119628, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I do not do what I do for praise. I\'m here to save Azeroth and the Horde. I sense you have a purpose here. What do you want?', '', 119627, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You are one of the greatest warriors the Horde has ever fielded. Your Arcanite Reaper is feared by all of your foes.', 'You are one of the greatest warriors the Horde has ever fielded. Your Arcanite Reaper is feared by all of your foes.', 119626, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Today I\'m here to fight the enemies of Azeroth. I\'ve no interest in wasting my strength with you. What do you want?', '', 119625, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That was to be expected. Ymiron was a cruel and evil ruler, but he always did fight with great ferocity.', '', 119624, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sometimes it is best to get out into the field and get a personal view of the war. The war could be going better.', '', 119623, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thank you.', 'Thank you.', 119622, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your sword is incredible, I wonder if there is an axe to match it.', '', 119621, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That may be, but what better punishment than to force him to serve you for the rest of time?', 'That may be, but what better punishment than to force him to serve you for the rest of time?', 119620, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Absolutely out of the question.$B$BKing Ymiron betrayed his people and doomed them to a cursed existence.$B$BHe might\'ve died while fighting valiantly but I abhor him and the feeling is mutual.', '', 119619, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want him to join our army.', 'I want him to join our army.', 119618, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Odyn laughs a deep booming laugh.>$B$BYou are a devious one, $n. You are right, that would amuse me. Let it be done!', '', 119617, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('King Ymiron has been defeated. He fought fiercely.', 'King Ymiron has been defeated. He fought fiercely.', 119616, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This might be the end for us, friends. But if we are going to die here today, we die fighting!', '', 119615, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 70822, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s head to Isle of Thunder and put this key to use.', 'I have the key, let\'s start the raid. [Queue for solo instance.]', 119614, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is that a key to Lei Shen\'s palace?  Wherever did you get that?\n\nI\'d be up for one more raid on the Thunder King\'s treasure troves, for old time\'s sake.  Just give me the word.', 'We are ready to launch the raid at a moment\'s notice. All we need is the key. Have you found one?', 119613, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There must be. All the powerful qualities of the Warbreaker, but the splitting strength of an axe. There must be something!', '', 119612, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is there an axe the equal to Strom\'kar?', 'Is there an axe the equal to Strom\'kar?', 119611, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your sword has made me wonder if it would be better as an axe. What would that axe look like? Is there one out there already?', '', 119610, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shatter their portals! Drive out the Legion!', '', 119609, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Demons in the throne room! Protect the king!', '', 119608, 0, 0, 0, 70, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is there anything else that you can tell me about Xe\'ra and the naaru before we go? [I PUT ON MY RED SHIRT AND WIZARD\'S HAT]', 'Is there anything else that you can tell me about Xe\'ra and the naaru before we go? [LOTS OF RP]', 119607, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m ready, Velen!', 'I\'m ready, Velen!', 119606, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Are you prepared to save O\'ros from Rakeesh and uncover the secrets held within Light\'s Heart?', '', 119605, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me when you are ready to rescue O\'ros and we will go.', '', 119604, 0, 0, 273, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gather your courage, hero. We must act quickly!', '', 119603, 0, 0, 25, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This invasion was a subterfuge. We were corralled here like cattle, exactly as they planned. Now they have found O\'ros - the last of the Light Mother\'s children!', '', 119602, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('HAH! It makes music when you beat it! What a delightful creature! I will enjoy ending its existence.', '', 119601, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 70832, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Her... progeny. O\'ros... NO!', '', 119600, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What you have brought to me is known as Light\'s Heart. It is the sentience core of the naaru prime: Xe\'ra.', '', 119599, 0, 0, 1, 64, 0, 70881, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will explain on the way there. Inform me when you are prepared to leave, but please hurry.', '', 119598, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 70887, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('$ct $n, we have to go. NOW!', '', 119597, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 70888, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mother of Light! I... I am sorry. I did not know.', '', 119596, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 70889, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'ll teach you. Only the strong survive!', '', 119595, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re such a weakling, only pandering to me to get out of a real fight.', '', 119594, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll get you some more wine, just please don\'t hurt me.', '', 119593, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Didn\'t see what?', '', 119592, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I-I-I\'m sorry. I didn\'t see...', '', 119591, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('You should never underestimate the little ones. We can be quite... tricky.', '', 119590, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sneak attack!', '', 119589, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, if it\'s going to come to that, I might as well...', '', 119588, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sorry. I didn\'t see you there. I was just...', '', 119587, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Just nothing! You\'ve got ten seconds to make this right before I beat you to the ground!', '', 119586, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What\'s your problem? You spilled arcwine all over me!', '', 119585, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am fairly alarmed here.', '', 119584, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 68258, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I hate being right all the time.', '', 119583, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 68257, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The plague will spread no further thanks to you.', 119582, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70149, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This keystone will ensure our success against the Magistrix. Your efforts will not be forgotten.', 119581, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70148, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We would have lost Arcanist Naran without your aid. Thank you. I am in your debt.', 119580, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70147, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I never believed the serpents could get so big! You\'ve saved us all.', 119579, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70146, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Arcway is one step closer to its former glory thanks to you.', 119578, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 70145, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would like to requisition some Rangers.', 'I would like to requisition some Rangers.', 119577, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would like to requisition some Trackers.', 'I would like to requisition some Trackers.', 119576, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
