('', 'What is your command?', 89253, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look, $n has arrived! This may be the stroke that turns the tide of this battle!', '', 89252, 0, 0, 25, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('$n has come to Stormshield! I\'ve never seen a finer $c in my day!', '', 89251, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is that $n? I can\'t believe $Ghe:she;\'s in Stormshield!', '', 89250, 0, 0, 5, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Fishing.', 'Train me in Fishing.', 89249, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am not a fighter myself, but I feel like even the most battle-minded of us should step away from time to time to enjoy some peace and quiet.\n\nFor me, there\'s no better way to do so then with a fishing rod in your hand and the gentle sounds of the ocean. \n\nWhat do you think, $C?', '', 89248, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The appearance of the Order of the Awakened vexes many of the Outcasts. Though they claim their intentions are pure, their kind has wronged us so many times before.\n\nWe hope they are true to their words, but for now we will wait and see.', '', 89247, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Our people appreciate the aid you have lent us against the Adherents of Rukhmar. \n\nWe will not forget your generosity.', '', 89246, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is good that you have come to Ashran, $C. You will likely be needed in the days to come.\n\nThe artifacts found on this island from the ancient ogre kingdom may be the determining factor in our battle against the Iron Horde. Unfortunately, the Horde has decided that they wish to take this knowledge for their own, in spite of our truce.\n\nWe must not let the Horde impede our efforts against our foe here on Draenor. Take the battle to them and pry the artifacts from their dead hands if you must!\n\nFor the Alliance!', '', 89245, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Slay the Burning Blade Initiate before they can reach Azuka!', 'Slay the Burning Blade Initiate before they can reach Azuka!', 89244, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Sanketsu! Unleash your power!', 89243, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 46336, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Come close heroes, and let me heal your wounds.', 89242, 0, 31197, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'No pets up to the challenge?  I don\'t have time for amateurs, come back when you have a few fights under your belt.', 89241, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Come close heroes, and let me heal your wounds.', 89240, 0, 36470, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'That Swann may not have been born a dwarf, but the heat of the forge runs through her veins. \n\nI could not ask for a finer apprentice.', 89239, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In my days with the rangari, I have learned many nuances of skinning the varied beasts of Draenor.\n\nNow that I am in Stormshield, however, I find it is much more enjoyable to pass these teachings onto others, than to toil in the fields with the skinning knife.\n\nWouldn\'t you agree?', '', 89238, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Iskar wanted to bring Terokk back with a body of his own. But would the Talon King have saved us, or lead us further into darkness?$B$BI was not willing to repeat the mistakes of our past.$B$BIn you, I saw a worthy steward of the Talon King\'s power. Ishaal agreed, and helped me to bind your essences together.$B$BIskar will not be happy about this, but what\'s done is done.', '', 89237, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|TInterface\\Icons\\Spell_Fire_Fireball02:20|t You are carrying |cFFFF0000|Hspell:160702|h[Blackrock Mortar Shells]|h|r. Hop in a Blackrock Turret to use them!', '|TInterface\\Icons\\Spell_Fire_Fireball02:20|t You are carrying |cFFFF0000|Hspell:160702|h[Blackrock Mortar Shells]|h|r. Hop in a Blackrock Turret to use them!', 89236, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Talon King\'s power belongs to the children of Skettis.$B$BReshad should never have shared it with an outsider...', '', 89235, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
