('Tell me about Herbalism.', 'Tell me about Herbalism.', 47142, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tailoring allows you to fashion armor, cloaks, clothing, bags, spellthread, and other similar items from various types of cloth, which can be purchased or taken from slain humanoid enemies. Additional necessary materials such as threads and dyes can be purchased from trade or Tailoring vendors.\n\nHighly skilled tailors can also upgrade their cloaks with magical embroidery.\n\nEnchanters are often tailors as well, since they can disenchant the magical items they create.', 'Tailoring allows you to fashion armor, cloaks, clothing, bags, spellthread, and other similar items from various types of cloth, which can be purchased or taken from slain humanoid enemies. Additional necessary materials such as threads and dyes can be purchased from trade or Tailoring vendors.\n\nHighly skilled tailors can also upgrade their cloaks with magical embroidery.\n\nEnchanters are often tailors as well, since they can disenchant the magical items they create.', 47141, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Leatherworking allows you to fashion armor, cloaks, armor-reinforcing kits, and other similar items from leather, hides, and scales. Other materials required for leatherworking can be purchased at trade and Leatherworking vendors.\n\nLeatherworking pairs well with Skinning as it allows you to gather your own raw materials; other necessary items, such as threads and dyes, can be purchased from trade or Leatherworking vendors.\n\nHighly skilled leatherworkers can also enforce their bracers and leg armor.', 'Leatherworking allows you to fashion armor, cloaks, armor-reinforcing kits, and other similar items from leather, hides, and scales. Other materials required for leatherworking can be purchased at trade and Leatherworking vendors.\n\nLeatherworking pairs well with Skinning as it allows you to gather your own raw materials; other necessary items, such as threads and dyes, can be purchased from trade or Leatherworking vendors.\n\nHighly skilled leatherworkers can also enforce their bracers and leg armor.', 47140, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Jewelcrafting allows you to fashion magical rings, amulets, and trinkets as well as cut gems.\n\nThe gems used in Jewelcrafting may be purchased or acquired via Prospecting from ore gathered by Mining; for this reason the two professions pair well.\n\nMost Jewelcrafting designs also require a Jeweler\'s Kit while more advanced creations require a Simple Grinder; these may be purchased from Jewelcrafting vendors.', 'Jewelcrafting allows you to fashion magical rings, amulets, and trinkets as well as cut gems.\n\nThe gems used in Jewelcrafting may be purchased or acquired via Prospecting from ore gathered by Mining; for this reason the two professions pair well.\n\nMost Jewelcrafting designs also require a Jeweler\'s Kit while more advanced creations require a Simple Grinder; these may be purchased from Jewelcrafting vendors.', 47139, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Inscription allows you to create magical scrolls, glyphs, off-hand tomes, Darkmoon cards, and even recipes for other professions.\n\nMany raw materials for Inscription come from milling herbs gathered by Herbalism, so the two professions pair well.\n\nYou\'ll need a Virtuoso Inking Set for inscribing things; this and other necessary materials, such as parchment, may be purchased from Inscription vendors.', 'Inscription allows you to create magical scrolls, glyphs, off-hand tomes, Darkmoon cards, and even recipes for other professions.\n\nMany raw materials for Inscription come from milling herbs gathered by Herbalism, so the two professions pair well.\n\nYou\'ll need a Virtuoso Inking Set for inscribing things; this and other necessary materials, such as parchment, may be purchased from Inscription vendors.', 47138, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Engineering allows you to construct a wide variety of useful, amazing, and just plain weird items like rifles and scopes, motorcycles, and mechanical squirrels. However, many of these are only usable by yourself or other engineers, such as special goggles, mechanical additions to belts, boots, gloves and cloaks, and flying machines.\n\nMost raw Engineering materials are metals gathered by Mining, so the two professions pair well.\n\nMany creations require the use of a Blacksmith Hammer; this and other necessary materials, such as gun stocks or flux, may be purchased from trade or Engineering vendors.', 'Engineering allows you to construct a wide variety of useful, amazing, and just plain weird items like rifles and scopes, motorcycles, and mechanical squirrels. However, many of these are only usable by yourself or other engineers, such as special goggles, mechanical additions to belts, boots, gloves and cloaks, and flying machines.\n\nMost raw Engineering materials are metals gathered by Mining, so the two professions pair well.\n\nMany creations require the use of a Blacksmith Hammer; this and other necessary materials, such as gun stocks or flux, may be purchased from trade or Engineering vendors.', 47137, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Enchanting allows you to enchant items with a wide variety of beneficial effects, as well as disenchant items and create magical wands and oils.\n\nHighly skilled enchanters can even enchant their own rings, which no one else may do.\n\nMost raw materials for Enchanting must be gathered via disenchanting, a process which destroys the disenchanted item. For this reason the profession pairs well with Tailoring, as you can disenchant the magical Tailoring items you create for raw materials.\n\nEnchanters may also place enchantments upon vellum, which allows the enchantment to be sold or saved for later use. Vellum and other useful Enchanting materials may be purchased from Enchanting vendors.', 'Enchanting allows you to enchant items with a wide variety of beneficial effects, as well as disenchant items and create magical wands and oils.\n\nHighly skilled enchanters can even enchant their own rings, which no one else may do.\n\nMost raw materials for Enchanting must be gathered via disenchanting, a process which destroys the disenchanted item. For this reason the profession pairs well with Tailoring, as you can disenchant the magical Tailoring items you create for raw materials.\n\nEnchanters may also place enchantments upon vellum, which allows the enchantment to be sold or saved for later use. Vellum and other useful Enchanting materials may be purchased from Enchanting vendors.', 47136, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dragonmaw attack! Protect the High Shaman.', 'Look out - Dragonmaw!', 47135, 7, 0, 274, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blacksmithing allows you to forge items from metals, minerals and stones: melee weapons, mail and plate heavy armor, raw materials used by other production professions, and upgrades to pieces of equipment such as sharpening stones and shield spikes.\n\nHighly skilled blacksmiths can add a gem slot to their own bracers and gloves, as well as to their own or others\' belts. These gem slots may then be filled with magical gems that make the gemmed item more powerful.\n\nBlacksmithing pairs well with Mining as it allows you to gather your own ore and minerals.', 'Blacksmithing allows you to forge items from metals, minerals and stones: melee weapons, mail and plate heavy armor, raw materials used by other production professions, and upgrades to pieces of equipment such as sharpening stones and shield spikes.\n\nHighly skilled blacksmiths can add a gem slot to their own bracers and gloves, as well as to their own or others\' belts. These gem slots may then be filled with magical gems that make the gemmed item more powerful.\n\nBlacksmithing pairs well with Mining as it allows you to gather your own ore and minerals.', 47134, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alchemy allows you to use herbs and other materials to create a wide variety of useful elixirs, potions, oils, flasks and cauldrons. You\'ll also gain greater, longer-lasting benefits when using your own elixirs and flasks.\n\nHighly skilled alchemists may also transmute elemental materials and certain minerals for use by other production professions.\n\nAlchemy pairs well with Herbalism as it allows you to gather your own herbs.', 'Alchemy allows you to use herbs and other materials to create a wide variety of useful elixirs, potions, oils, flasks and cauldrons. You\'ll also gain greater, longer-lasting benefits when using your own elixirs and flasks.\n\nHighly skilled alchemists may also transmute elemental materials and certain minerals for use by other production professions.\n\nAlchemy pairs well with Herbalism as it allows you to gather your own herbs.', 47133, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Skinning allows you to remove and prepare the hides from slain creatures. These can be sold at the auction house or used to support the Leatherworking profession.\n\nSkilled Skinners also become masters of anatomy, increasing their chances to critically hit a target.\n\nYou\'ll need a Skinning Knife in order to skin creatures; this can be purchased from trade or Leatherworking vendors.', 'Skinning allows you to remove and prepare the hides from slain creatures. These can be sold at the auction house or used to support the Leatherworking profession.\n\nSkilled Skinners also become masters of anatomy, increasing their chances to critically hit a target.\n\nYou\'ll need a Skinning Knife in order to skin creatures; this can be purchased from trade or Leatherworking vendors.', 47132, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mining allows you to locate and mine ore, minerals and stone from mining nodes in the wilderness and underground. These can be sold at the auction house or used to support the Blacksmithing, Engineering, or Jewelcrafting professions.\n\nSkilled miners also become tough and gain increased Stamina.\n\nYou\'ll need a Mining Pick in order to mine; this can be purchased from trade or Mining vendors.', 'Mining allows you to locate and mine ore, minerals and stone from mining nodes in the wilderness and underground. These can be sold at the auction house or used to support the Blacksmithing, Engineering, or Jewelcrafting professions.\n\nSkilled miners also become tough and gain increased Stamina.\n\nYou\'ll need a Mining Pick in order to mine; this can be purchased from trade or Mining vendors.', 47131, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Herbalism allows you to locate and gather herbs from the wild. These can be sold at the auction house or used to support the Alchemy or Inscription professions.\n\nSkilled herbalists can also use their knowledge of the earth to heal themselves.', 'Herbalism allows you to locate and gather herbs from the wild. These can be sold at the auction house or used to support the Alchemy or Inscription professions.\n\nSkilled herbalists can also use their knowledge of the earth to heal themselves.', 47130, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Production professions allow you to turn raw materials into items that you can use yourself, give to companions, or sell at an auction house.\n\nThey are often paired with a gathering profession so that you can gather your own raw materials, but it is possible to simply buy materials on the auction house.', 'Production professions allow you to turn raw materials into items that you can use yourself, give to companions, or sell at an auction house.\n\nThey are often paired with a gathering profession so that you can gather your own raw materials, but it is possible to simply buy materials on the auction house.', 47129, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The High Shaman is here - I can see the storm clouds. Crush him, that we may take his skull as a trophy!', 'The High Shaman is here - I can see the storm clouds. Crush him, that we may take his skull as a trophy!', 47128, 1, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I decided to keep shrinking the world until I could reach the clouds.$b$b|TInterface\\Icons\\inv_helmet_47.blp:32|t', '', 47127, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And then I\'ll throw you to Kalimdor!', '', 47126, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll find you in those clouds, you worm!', '', 47125, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('\"I\'ll find you in those clouds, you worm!\" I yelled.  \"And then I\'ll throw you to Kalimdor!\"', '', 47124, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Luckily, I had been tinkering with my world-shrinking device.', '', 47123, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The cowardly dragon must have seen me, because he turned away and flew into the clouds.', '', 47122, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('First of all, it wasn\'t sunny out.  It was cloudy when Deathwing appeared.', '', 47121, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hold your ground. We Wildhammer go down fighting to the end!', '', 47120, 7, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Engineering.', 'Train me in Engineering.', 47119, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Tailoring.', 'Train me in Tailoring.', 47118, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Skinning.', 'Train me in Skinning.', 47117, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Mining.', 'Train me in Mining.', 47116, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Leatherworking.', 'Train me in Leatherworking.', 47115, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Jewelcrafting.', 'Train me in Jewelcrafting.', 47114, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Inscription.', 'Train me in Inscription.', 47113, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Herbalism.', 'Train me in Herbalism.', 47112, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Enchanting.', 'Train me in Enchanting.', 47111, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Blacksmithing.', 'Train me in Blacksmithing.', 47110, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Train me in Alchemy.', 'Train me in Alchemy.', 47109, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gathering professions allow you to acquire raw materials used by production professions: gathering herbs; mining ore, stone, and jewels; or skinning beasts for their hides.\n\nYou can either support a related production profession with gathering, or simply sell the raw materials on the auction house.', 'Gathering professions allow you to acquire raw materials used by production professions: gathering herbs; mining ore, stone, and jewels; or skinning beasts for their hides.\n\nYou can either support a related production profession with gathering, or simply sell the raw materials on the auction house.', 47108, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me about production professions.', 'Tell me about production professions.', 47107, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me about gathering professions.', 'Tell me about gathering professions.', 47106, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can teach you the basics of any gathering or production profession, but that\'s all.\n\nTo learn more than an apprentice\'s skills, you\'ll need to visit a specialist dedicated to only one profession.\n\nYou can learn up to two professions: Two gathering, two production, or one of each.\n\nSecondary skills like Archaeology, Cooking, and Fishing don\'t count towards your two professions; you can learn as many of those as you like.', 'I can teach you the basics of any gathering or production profession, but that\'s all.\n\nTo learn more than an apprentice\'s skills, you\'ll need to visit a specialist dedicated to only one profession.\n\nYou can learn up to two professions: Two gathering, two production, or one of each.\n\nSecondary skills like Archaeology, Cooking, and Fishing don\'t count towards your two professions; you can learn as many of those as you like.', 47105, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get zhem!! Now! Go, go, go!', '', 47104, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We have to push forward if we\'re to put an end to him. Follow me, I\'ll open the courtyard so that you can spearhead our assault.', '', 47103, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Control yourselves! We\'re here for Godfrey\'s head above all else. Relish in the spoils of war later!', '', 47102, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 25, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Bloodfang Berserkers begin to salivate heavily.', '', 47101, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Keep moving forward. My men will dispose of this sorry bag of bones.', '', 47100, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pathetic. ', '', 47099, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('$n prepares a feast of Seafood Magnifique!', '$n prepares a feast of Seafood Magnifique!', 47098, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('$n prepares a feast of Broiled Dragon!', '$n prepares a feast of Broiled Dragon!', 47097, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Quick! Into the plane!', '', 47096, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Agreed.  So what do you want from me?', 'Agreed.  So what do you want from me?', 47095, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So not all of your people have allied with him?', 'So not all of your people have allied with him?', 47094, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why does he need you?', 'Why does he need you?', 47093, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Deathwing came here and didn\'t slay you all?', 'Deathwing came here and didn\'t slay you all?', 47092, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Who are you?', 'Who are you?', 47091, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Free me.$B$BFree me so that we may rally my people against Deathwing together.$B$BAnd if that\'s not reason enough, you will be rewarded with great riches.  I am still a prince after all.', '', 47090, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He\'s got one of the tribes on his side.  The Neferset.$B$BOrsis has made its defiance clear.$B$BRamkahen has tried to find a peaceful solution, but there is no peace possible with Deathwing and his allies.', '', 47089, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We are keepers of the secrets of Uldum.  Beneath the sand... under the pyramids... there exists great power.$B$BThe power to make and break an entire world.$B$BHe cannot access this power without us, however.', '', 47088, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He offered all of us a chance to regain our former glory... to be true tol\'vir again.$B$BBut only... if we swore allegiance to him.', '', 47087, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am Prince Nadun of Ramkahehn.  My people are tol\'vir... or descended from the tol\'vir to be precise.$B$BThe people of Neferset were like us, made of flesh and blood...$B$BUntil Deathwing came.', '', 47086, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am Prince Nadun of Ramkahen.  The Neferset tribe has turned against the other tol\'vir.$B$BHelp me escape so that I may lobby my brother, the king, to wage war against these traitors!', '', 47085, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Chuck the Bear Cub!', '', 47084, 0, 10810, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Climb to the Tree Top', '', 47083, 0, 10809, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Grab a Bear Cub', '', 47082, 0, 10808, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Find a Tree to Climb', '', 47081, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I took Helgrum under my wing when I arrived in Stonard. Under my harsh glare, he became an even greater tracker than before... and my only companion.$B$BI thought myself strong. I thought no suffering could break my spirit. When I saw the humans sink their swords into Helgrum... into my mate... I found out how wrong I was.', 47080, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'All the oceans shall be ours, and then we shall look beyond.', 47079, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 21804, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get back up there and get into the fight!', 'Get back up there and get into the fight!', 47078, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<The enormous ancient remains wary of you, but speaks to you as an ally.>', '', 47077, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Cenarius has fallen!', '', 47076, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21639, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('An inconspicuous stone slab.', '', 47075, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Place the statue down on the slab.', 'Place the statue down on the slab.', 47074, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('An inconspicuous marble slab.', '', 47073, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I see no reason to deny our trust.', '', 47072, 0, 10401, 0, 65, 0, 21766, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This champion has proved intent and capable.', '', 47071, 0, 10401, 0, 65, 0, 21765, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('At least enough so that you can prove yourself.', '', 47070, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 21762, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They should show you a degree of trust.', '', 47069, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 21761, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hah! Too easy!', '', 47068, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ho, ho! That had to hurt!', '', 47067, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get back up! I DARE YE!', '', 47066, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'ll learn ye!', '', 47065, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You die in vain!', '', 47064, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It was inevitable!', '', 47063, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'No mercy for the weak!', 47062, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hail to the queen!', 47061, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Those filthy mutts forced me out of Fenris Keep, I won\'t be forced out of my camp as well!', '', 47060, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sintharia, your master owes me a great debt -- one that I intend to extract from his consort\'s hide!', '', 47059, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21590, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Heroes, you are not alone in this dark place!', '', 47058, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 21588, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Foolish mortals!  You toy with arcane powers beyond your understanding!  I will put an end to this mockery of magic!', '', 47057, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All I wanted was a little peace and quiet!', '', 47056, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Blackhorn gazes out across the distant inferno, then turns his attention back to you.>', '', 47055, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Madness. Chaos. Much as I thrill to see the titans\' work undone, I do wish to remain alive when the master returns. I will help you.', '', 47054, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dad always told me the big fellas hit hard, but that they\'re slow...$b$bI\'m pretty sure dad never met this guy!', '', 47053, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It\'s lovely here, don\'t you think?$b$bA bit hot, perhaps, but it\'s a dry heat...', 47052, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes...', '', 47051, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey, look!  It\'s flying!', '', 47050, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('...thank you, Prophet. You have given both of us great comfort. I will continue my work, in faith and memory of Magtoor.', '', 47049, 0, 0, 273, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Prophet Velen!', '', 47048, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('Even now, nothing. Why? Why would the Light forsake the innocent?', '', 47047, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Remember, Avuun. Not all who wander are lost.', '', 47046, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Then may the Light save you and raise you up.', '', 47045, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Magtoor, you have endured your plight bravely. Are you ready to return to the embrace of the Light?', '', 47044, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Even now, the true battle between the forces of Light and Darkness approaches. We will all be called to join, and in the face of this conflict, all mortal suffering will be meaningless.', '', 47043, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Light wishes suffering on none, my child. But it does not reign unopposed in our realm.', '', 47042, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Some have spent decades meditating upon this mystery, Avuun. I do not wish the same fate upon you.', '', 47041, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Twilight Dragonkin must be stopped! Rescue the other Red Dragonflight and we shall assist you!', '', 47040, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please champions, rescue my brethren from the Twilight\'s Hammer!', '', 47039, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|TInterface\\Icons\\INV_POTION_162.BLP:20|tMaloriak throws a |cFF33FF00green|r vial into the cauldron!', '', 47038, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|TInterface\\Icons\\INV_POTION_20.BLP:20|tMaloriak throws a |cFF809FFEblue|r vial into the cauldron!', '', 47037, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|TInterface\\Icons\\INV_POTION_24.BLP:20|tMaloriak throws a |cFFFF0000red|r vial into the cauldron!', '', 47036, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Meet the brawn to my brains! Prime subjects, devour them!', '', 47035, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19859, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Too early, but no choice... They must be tested! Face now my prime subjects!', '', 47034, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19858, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My failings will be your downfall!', '', 47033, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19857, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What they lack in intelligence they make up for in ferocity!', '', 47032, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19856, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There will never be another like me...', '', 47031, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19850, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Strip the flesh, harvest the organs!', '', 47030, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19849, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nothing goes to waste... ', '', 47029, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19848, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There can be no disruptions! Mustn\'t keep the master waiting! Mustn\'t fail again!', '', 47028, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 19847, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '<A dream-like vision of Ysera floats before you, her attention divided. After a moment, she addresses you.>$B$BFor many years, Aviana fluttered at the periphery of my dreams. I wondered if she should ever return to us. I fear her spirit has darkened with the passage of time...$B$BBut we have more immediate concerns if we hope to save this mountain.', 47027, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The guardian of the skies has taken flight again! This is encouraging news, $n. But much remains undone, and we must turn our attention elsewhere...', 47026, 0, 0, 273, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'So Tortolla has risen to fight at our side. You are wise, $n; it is difficult to earn that ancient\'s trust. He will be a stalwart companion.', 47025, 0, 0, 273, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The gryphon screams with glee as you break it free.', '', 47024, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '<Ysera\'s image flutters before your eyes, as if in a dream. Nobody else sees her here, yet the vision senses your presence.>', 47023, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '$n, you have unleashed the wolf ancient and defeated his shadow. Your actions already reverberate across the dream - thank you. But more remains to be done...', 47022, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'A vision of Ysera materializes before you.', 47021, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The gryphon looks at you with genuine appreciation.', '', 47020, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'My suffering is eternal!', 47019, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yo you got through the gauntlet! I\'m out!\n', '', 47018, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The gryphon muscles tense and eyes tighten as soon as the bark is extended towards it.', '', 47017, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let the gryphon smell the piece of charred highland birch.', 'Let the gryphon smell the piece of charred highland birch.', 47016, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have 3 Holy Power!', '', 47015, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have 2 Holy Power!', '', 47014, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have 1 Holy Power!', '', 47013, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The gryphon appears to be trapped. It looks like it would be easily possible to break its bonds though.', '', 47012, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The gryphon looks at you intently, clearly smelling a familiar scent on your clothing.', '', 47011, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The gryphon appears to be injured. Perhaps healing or first aid could get it back on its feet.', '', 47010, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Take us to the Stockades, Andromath.', '', 47009, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We\'re taking him into custody in the name of King Varian Wrynn.', '', 47008, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This beast leads the Riverpaw gnoll gang and may be the key to ending gnoll aggression in Elwynn.', '', 47007, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wow!', 'Wow!', 47006, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('General Hammond Clay!', 'General Hammond Clay!', 47005, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hold your blade, adventurer!', '', 47004, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The cultists have not stopped their attacks. Spread the word: double the guard and arrest anyone suspicious. These orders come from the warchief himself!', '', 47003, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Grunts, $n has lead Orgrimmar\'s fight against the doomsday cultists.', '', 47002, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We obey, blood guard. For the Horde!', 'We obey, blood guard. For the Horde!', 47001, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No hurt Hogger!', '', 47000, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I DON\'T BELIEVE IT! WE HAVE A NEW CHAMPION OF CARNAGE!!! Our big, bad beefy challenger has been defeated by a ragtag crew of nobodies! Incredible finish!', '', 46999, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('W-W-W-WINNER! We have a winner! Good job and stuff!', '', 46998, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Twilight\'s Hammer: happy to serve local nefarious schemes anytime, anywhere. And today is no exception! Our final combatant hails from the not so distant Bastion of Twilight! Or is it the Twilight Bastion... bah, who cares!', '', 46997, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hailing from the semi-distant wreck of a landscape that was once Gilneas, our champion arises! Keep your pants up $n, you don\'t want to show this guy a full moon!', '', 46996, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You know what they say... if you can\'t beat \'em, join \'em! And in this case, you won\'t have the choice! Cruicible of Carnage, I adore you so.', '', 46995, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Imagine my surprise when I was approached by the genius forsaken, Calder Gray, and propsitioned with a combatant made of all the best features of our previous champions... LITERALLY! Who could refuse a chance to challenge CALDER\'S CREATION?!', '', 46994, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This match is sure to be SHORT! Okay, okay, I\'m done. Let the bloodbath begin!', '', 46993, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve got a LITTLE somethin\' special for ya this time, folks! You aren\'t half the man of this half-man! $n vs. the vicious Wildhammer... SULLY KNEECAPPER!!!', '', 46992, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The battle is about to begin! $n vs. the vicious Dragonmaw, Torg Drakeflayer! I THINK he\'s vicious anyway - hard to tell. I just let him because they let us take over their old arena here. Here\'s hoping for some blood!', '', 46991, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Whatever, let the fight begin!', '', 46990, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Here we are once again, ladies and gentlemen. The epic struggle between life and death in the Crucible of Carnage! For this round we have $n versus... a really fat ogre? Wait, seriously?! That\'s all we could come up with on short notice? What am I paying you for? ', '', 46989, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The grand Crucible of Carnage awaits, $n. Remember, once a battle starts you have to stay in the arena. WIN OR DIE!', '', 46988, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What Deathwing has set in motion... (...no man can stop.) No man! Least of all you wretches. (Show them. Show them their end!)', '', 46987, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Hammer of Twilight. (The Hammer of Twilight!) Commissioned by the Aspect of Death. It is the breaker of worlds. It is not yours to wield. (Kill the intruders!) Kill them all!', '', 46986, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look, mortal, upon the instrument of your undoing. (The Hammer, hand of the Gods Below.) Forged of molten blood... (...gift of the master. His gift!) Shaped upon the Last Altar of Storm.', '', 46985, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Back, vermin! (Insects! Weak and small!)', '', 46984, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('THERE IS NO MERCY!  YOU WILL BURN FOR THIS, DRAGON!', '', 46983, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mercy?!', '', 46982, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Yes.  Just... just show mercy to the egg.', 46981, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Are you ready to die, dragon?', '', 46980, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You impetuous little whelp... I know exactly what you and the mortal are up to.', '', 46979, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'No... it\'s... it\'s you!  NO!', 46977, 0, 0, 431, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'How\'s my little baby doing?', 46976, 0, 0, 4, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Now to get the egg...', 46975, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ll just leave this right here.', 46974, 0, 0, 432, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This land shall be purged in the Twilight\'s Flame! ', '', 46973, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why hello chaps, I have a not so surprising surprise for you this eve.', '', 46972, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Calder said that if I kill you, I get to have your parts!', '', 46971, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My little sister could best the lot of ya. This ain\'t no arena. This is a nursery!', '', 46970, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All of the highlands belong to the Dragonmaw, even this pit!', '', 46969, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Avoid the lava waves!', '', 46968, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You look like you could make us some money. How about a spin inside the Crucible of Carnage, pal?', '', 46967, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '...', 46966, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is my time, Avuun. Nobody is to blame...', '', 46965, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I have failed you, my friend. I am so sorry.', '', 46964, 0, 10790, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 378, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I came here long ago to study our cursed brothers, in search of a way to cure their affliction.$B$BMagtoor welcomed me with open arms. Living here, he became my closest friend.$B$BAnd now, before my eyes, he is dying...', '', 46963, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Use the Mech Control Scrambler to disable Twizzleflux\'s vehicle!', '', 46962, 0, 10785, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re certainly not local. Matters to me little though. I\'ll put my life on the line for anyone here as long as they pull their weight.', '', 46961, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They took us unaware... attacked all of the highlands all at once, burstin\' forth from the ground, swoopin\' from the air. Most of the gryphon wings were scattered, and far too many good dwarves lost their lives.$B$BThere\'d be little hope at all if Keegan hadn\'t rallied us together. I owe that man my life. At least now we have a chance.', '', 46960, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If I\'m not mistaken, this belongs to you.', 'If I\'m not mistaken, this belongs to you.', 46959, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I believe these are yours, Meara.', 'I believe these are yours, Meara.', 46958, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hahahah!', '', 46957, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I found this in the ruins. Cailin told me it was yours...', 'I found this in the ruins. Cailin told me it was yours...', 46956, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What\'s happening to me?', '', 46955, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'For the Bilgewater Cartel! For the Shattered Hand! FOR THE HORDE!', 46954, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 71, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No... nooooo!', '', 46953, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My family hammer?! What could have possibly possessed you... never mind, I don\'t care.  You\'ll always be welcome in our home - we\'ll save a place for you at the table.  Thank you.', '', 46952, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What the-??', '', 46951, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pleasure to meet ya, young $gman:lady;.', '', 46950, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Wha... my roses?! Did Cailin tell you?  I really can\'t thank you enough. I thought I\'d never smell home again...', 46949, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You\'re definitely not Wildhammer. What brings you here? Your timing is pretty horrid, that\'s for sure.', 46948, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Oh my gosh! Thank you SO much! You have no idea how much this means to me. You\'re the sweetest thing!', 46947, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hi! You\'re new. Did you lose your home too? You can sit with me if you want.', 46946, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And you... are next!', '', 46945, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fools!  It is too late for them  And it is too late for all of you! You will join us and together we will unearth secrets that will unravel this world!', '', 46944, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What the-????   AGGHGHhh...', '', 46943, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Twizzleflux!  What insanity are you up to?  We brought the additional crew you requested, but there is no... research going on here.  Only madness!', '', 46942, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gah!!!  What... how did you..?', '', 46941, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
