('Decontamination complete. Standby for delivery.', '', 46324, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Commencing decontamination sequence... ', '', 46323, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be wary of taking to the sky above these ruins, $glad:lass;. The Twilight drakes have a taste for things that fly.', '', 46320, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There\'s an artifact, a weapon, being forged with the power of an Old God. We don\'t know exactly what it is, but we need to get to it before it\'s completed by Cho\'gall.$B$BEverything else is secondary. Everyone is expendable, including you and I.', '', 46319, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 396, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Let\'s get something straight, $r. I\'m here for just one thing: to kill Cho\'gall!$B$BYour job is to keep him from finishing the creation of his ultimate weapon. It\'s an artifact that\'s supposedly being created with the power of an Old God.', 46318, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 396, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wouldn\'t say that it\'s your fault, Tarenar.  But don\'t let that stop you from saving Gidwin.', '', 46317, 0, 0, 397, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is all my fault.  I\'ve got to go find him, to set things right.', '', 46316, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Perhaps he felt he needed to prove that he was as talented as you.', '', 46315, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What do you mean?', '', 46314, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Perhaps that\'s why he left without you.', '', 46313, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ve watched both of you fight, Tarenar.  You\'ve got natural talent - more than Gidwin ever will.', 46312, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '...yet it was you that continually kept up with him.  Without practice.', 46311, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Me, skilled?  No, no, Gidwin was the good paladin.  He\'s the one who stayed up for hours every night practicing... ', '', 46310, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You\'re not alone, Tarenar.  You\'ve made allies along the way.  And besides, you\'re a skilled paladin in your own right.', 46309, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m not sure I\'m ready to go in there alone.', '', 46308, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Both are places of great evil.  This is the leg of my journey that I shun the most.', '', 46307, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If we\'re to find him, we\'re headed in the right direction.  It\'s likely that he was taken to Stratholme, or potentially to the Plaguewood.', '', 46306, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Well, actually, that\'s pretty bad news, but considering the alternatives... ', 46305, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Really?  That\'s great news!', 46304, 0, 0, 4, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s likely that he\'s being held somewhere, awaiting a death ritual.', '', 46303, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A paladin like Gidwin makes a fine death knight.  Any member of the Scourge powerful enough to defeat him would know that.', '', 46302, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Even more reason to believe that he\'s still alive.', '', 46301, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He was always studying, always trying to get better.', '', 46300, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No, he\'d never just leave his prayer book behind!  He was always nose-deep in that book, studying.', '', 46299, 0, 0, 274, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We can\'t be certain that he was killed.  Maybe he just ran off somewhere.', '', 46298, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It\'s not your fault, Tarenar.  He ran off on his own will.  None of us could stop him.', 46297, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can\'t believe I let Gidwin run off like that!', '', 46296, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Walking, eh...?', '', 46295, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Light\'s Hope isn\'t far, young paladin.  Might I suggest walking?', '', 46294, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('NOOOOOOO!  Stopped again!', '', 46293, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Of course I\'m not just going to drop you off, Master Highbeacon.  We\'ll be happy to wait for you.', 46292, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ma\'am, would you mind dropping me off at Light\'s Shield Tower, just up ahead?  I have to stop here.', '', 46291, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Whoah... he lets you call him Max?', '', 46290, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Certainly.  I don\'t make it out to Light\'s Hope very often anymore, but when you arrive, tell Max Tyrosus that I sent you.', '', 46289, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('Think you can put in the good word for us?  We\'re looking to join the order.', '', 46288, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So you\'re part of the Argent Crusade, eh?', '', 46287, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('By the way, if any of you need anything repaired, let me know.  I am at your service.', '', 46286, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I find it satisfying.  I enjoy working with my hands.', '', 46285, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Noble work.', '', 46284, 0, 0, 273, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Without proper upkeep, buildings within the plaguelands tend to... waste away.', '', 46283, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I service the five Argent towers.  Mostly repairs and maintenance, and some minor magical work.', '', 46282, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you don\'t mind my askin\', what do you do that requires walking so much?', '', 46281, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, I do, though it was easier when I was younger.  These days, I have to be more careful.', '', 46280, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Do you normally walk these roads alone?', 46279, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ahem!  I, ah, appreciate the ride, Madam Fiona.  It\'s nice to get off my feet for once.', '', 46278, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do not!', '', 46277, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh shut up, you dolt.  YOU probably want to kiss her a hundred times.', '', 46276, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fiona, I must warn you: Gidwin only wants to sit in front because he wants to kiss you.', '', 46275, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I know I promised you the front seat, Giddy, but we have an elderly guest.  I\'m sorry.', 46274, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey!  I oughtta bounce one of these trunks off of your head, Tarenar.', '', 46273, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Because you\'re short.', '', 46272, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Because you\'re the bravest, dear.', 46271, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why do I have to sit up top with all the stuff?!', '', 46270, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This hardly seems fair!!', '', 46269, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Reforge', 'Reforge', 46268, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you\'re looking for an Arcane Reforger, there is a highborne mage inside the enchanting shop just outside the Mage District.', 'If you\'re looking for an Arcane Reforger, there is a highborne mage inside the enchanting shop just outside the Mage District.', 46267, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Arcane Reforgers can modify the magical effects of a item; this magically complex process is known simply as reforging.$B$BThrough reforging, a secondary attribute of any piece of weaponry, armor, or jewelry may be reduced in order to add an additional secondary attribute. In this manner one may customize their equipment to best match their role and skills.$B$BFor example, if an item afforded you a bonus to strike your enemies but you\'d rather it made you attack more quickly, an Arcane Reforger could, for a price, reforge the item to have less Hit but increase your Haste.', 'Arcane Reforgers can modify the magical effects of a item; this magically complex process is known simply as reforging.$B$BThrough reforging, a secondary attribute of any piece of weaponry, armor, or jewelry may be reduced in order to add an additional secondary attribute. In this manner one may customize their equipment to best match their role and skills.$B$BFor example, if an item afforded you a bonus to strike your enemies but you\'d rather it made you attack more quickly, an Arcane Reforger could, for a price, reforge the item to have less Hit but increase your Haste.', 46266, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What is reforging?', 'What is reforging?', 46265, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Reforge an item.', 'Reforge an item.', 46264, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Highborne have returned, and with them spellcraft lost to the world for centuries.$B$BDo you have something for me to examine?', 'The Highborne have returned, and with them spellcraft lost to the world for centuries.$B$BDo you have something for me to examine?', 46263, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('With Stormwind\'s park district destroyed by Deathwing\'s pass over the city, we\'re returning to Darnassus for a time.', '', 46262, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s move out quickly, $n. Up the ramp and straight to Garona.', '', 46261, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Horde scum! I was once like you. (Our old masters, small and hungry.) You cling to your mortal shells... (Bags of blood and bone and tears). ...trying to deny your insignificance.', '', 46260, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pathetic flesh!', '', 46259, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('(Finish it! Finish them all!)', '', 46258, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Accompany Lady Sylvanas Windrunner across the Battlefront.', 46257, 0, 0, 0, 64, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hakkar is known by many names. Some call him the Blood God, others simply refer to him as The Soulflayer. Titles aside, he is an entity of enormous power with malicious intentions for our world.$B$BMy flight discovered this temple early on and sank it beneath the Swamp of Sorrows. Unfortunately, we only seemed to aid the Atal\'ai by ensuring their efforts to summon Hakkar went on undisturbed. Many of the dragons tasked with guarding the temple have been corrupted, and the Soulflayer\'s presence grows with each passing day.$B$BI cannot stop them alone. Together, though, we might have enough time to stop this madness.', '', 46256, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The world will be reborn in flames!', 46255, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 21634, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'A sacrifice for you, master.', 46254, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 21635, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Witness the power bestowed upon me by Deathwing! Feel the fury of earth!', 46253, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 21628, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Minions, followers, children of the Worldbreaker, I call to you now! The hallowed halls of our father have been befouled! Kill the intruders!', 46252, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 21627, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'For my death, countless more will fall. The burden is now yours to bear.', 46251, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 21633, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A protector has fallen. The World\'s Heart lies exposed!', '', 46250, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21922, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Break yourselves upon my body. Feel the strength of the earth!', '', 46249, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21921, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The cycle is complete.', '', 46248, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21920, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('None may pass into the World\'s Heart!', '', 46247, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21919, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Even in these bright days after the reign of Kel\'thuzad, after the fall of the Lich King: the Brotherhood lives on.', 46246, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 273, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Kill him!', '', 46245, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Cho\'gall!', '', 46244, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alliance soldiers! So bold, so cavalier. (Scurry, scurry, scurry, mortals.) Your numbers are small, and you are too late. (Helpless and hopeless, helpless and hopeless.)', '', 46243, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now... witness the full power of Millhouse Manastorm!', 'Now... witness the full power of Millhouse Manastorm!', 46242, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21788, 21788, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah-ha! I\'ve got you right where I want you!', 'Ah-ha! I\'ve got you right where I want you!', 46241, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21787, 21787, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Prison taught me one very important lesson, well, two if you count how to hold your soap, but yes! SURVIVAL!', '', 46240, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21789, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t say I didn\'t warn ya!', '', 46239, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21786, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re gonna be sorry!', '', 46238, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21785, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s time for a tactical retreat!', '', 46235, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21784, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Follow me if you dare!', '', 46234, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 21783, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Burn! BURN AND SUFFER!', '', 46233, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Murderous scum! Treacherous filth!', '', 46231, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You cannot escape the highlands, orcs!', '', 46230, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Filthy, filthy orcs! Unhand those whelps!', '', 46229, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My people have enjoyed a good relationship with the Wildhammer for quite some time now.$B$BA few of us have settled here... those who have found this land to be a home worth defending.', '', 46228, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We will never stop fighting for Lordaeron. Never...', 46227, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I know now - beyond a shadow of a doubt - that the val\'kyr are our future.', 46226, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'And as I drifted towards nothingness, a brilliant light appeared, then another, and another... My dear val\'kyr.', 46225, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I saw... only darkness.', 46224, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Then let it be done.', 46223, 0, 0, 457, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It is our sacred duty. The pact was sealed, the bargain made...', 46222, 0, 0, 457, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It will destroy us, sister...', 46221, 0, 0, 457, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We are bound to her, sisters...', 46220, 0, 0, 457, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fix her... FIX HER!', '', 46219, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This land will quiver and shake in the wake of our destruction!', '', 46218, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('FALL BACK, BROTHERS! TO SHADOWFANG!', '', 46217, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('NOW JOIN YOUR MISTRESS IN DEATH!', '', 46216, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gilneas belongs to me, and so soon will the rest of Lordaeron!', '', 46215, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Something that should have been done a long time ago, you filthy animal.\n', '', 46214, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('WHAT HAVE YOU DONE, GODFREY!', '', 46213, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '%s dies.', 46212, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'SOLDIERS OF THE HORDE! WE ARE VICTORIOUS! LORDAERON IS W...', 46211, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Forgive me, daughter...', '', 46210, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Lordaeron belongs to the Forsaken.', 46209, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Now leave here, Crowley, and never return.', 46208, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Of course, mistress.', '', 46207, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Release her, Godfrey.', 46206, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You can\'t be serious, Crowley. You miserable bastard!', '', 46205, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lorna... I... Release her. I will sound the retreat.', '', 46204, 0, 0, 20, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('GODFREY! You deceitful maggot!', '', 46203, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hello, old friend!', '', 46202, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Bring her, Godfrey!', 46200, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Choose your next words wisely, Crowley. Deny me and she will serve me in undeath - forever.', 46199, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I offer you the life of Lorna for your unconditional surrender.', 46198, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I now present you with a choice - a choice that I was never given.', 46197, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Nothing, yet...', 46196, 0, 0, 274, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('LORNA? What... Where is she!? What have you done to her!?', '', 46195, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'And your daughter? You could have saved her... You could have offered her your blood, yet you did not. Why?', 46194, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We will die trying!', '', 46193, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Is Gilneas worth the lives that have been lost? The lives that will be lost? You cannot win.', 46191, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You frivolously throw away the lives of your people while your own king sits atop his throne of lies, nary lifting a finger to help.', 46190, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s not over, Sylvanas. Not yet.', '', 46189, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Crowley, your forces have fallen before my mighty army. You have lost!', 46188, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wait! Do you hear something?', '', 46187, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('COME, HUMANS! LICK THE STAINLESS STEEL BOOTS OF YOUR NEW GOD!', '', 46186, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Deploy mobile rocket platform pods! .... Oh yes.', '', 46185, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s actually pretty good by Bilgewater standards. ', '', 46184, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Deathblade ... activated! System integrity check: 57 percent nominal.', '', 46183, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We should move out, $n. Up the ramp and then straight to Master Shaw.', '', 46182, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We did it! Let\'s fire this masterpiece up...', 'We did it! Let\'s fire this masterpiece up...', 46181, 0, 0, 4, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, stuff it. This thing is busted beyond hope. I\'m outta here!', 'Well, stuff it. This thing is busted beyond hope. I\'m outta here!', 46180, 0, 0, 274, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Throm-Ka, $n. We snuck a few more in while you were preparing the Gates for attack.$B$BI\'ll show you where we\'re to meet with Garona.$B$B<The squad leader produces a map of the Twilight Citadel and points to the spot.>$B$BLet me know when you\'re ready, and we\'ll go together.', '', 46179, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This shredder looks like it can be repaired. You fire off a signal...', '', 46178, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Cover my butt in case we\'re ambushed.', 'Cover my butt in case we\'re ambushed.', 46177, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Here we go, $gbub:toots;. Watch how things get done.', 'Woohoo, $gsweet-thing:lady;! Step aside and watch the magic.', 46176, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The trees here in the Highlands are made of stout wood. And some of them... stone. I don\'t pretend to understand.$B$BWe\'ve got diamond-bladed shredders to harvest the stuff, but the Alliance keeps whacking them.', '', 46175, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Who needs this hunk of metal more, Rok\'tar? You? ...Or the highest bidder?', '', 46174, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nobody ever made money by keeping themselves alive, Rok\'tar.', '', 46173, 0, 0, 274, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Time is money, friend!', '', 46172, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gnugat, if your goblins strip any more of this ship\'s supports, it\'ll plunge into the surf!', '', 46171, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gnugat, does it seem wise to you to tear apart a ship underneath your own feet?', '', 46170, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gnugat... Can you wait until we are OFF of the boat before you take it apart?', '', 46168, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The flare launcher has been emptied.', '', 46167, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It looks like your predecessor had time to set the flares up, but they have not yet been launched.$b$bThis is your time to shine, $n.', '', 46166, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The hieroglyphs on your tablets indicate that there\'s a way to get this mechanism working again.$b$bWe just need to figure out how...', '', 46165, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Remember: Hellscream\'s eyes are upon you, $n!', '', 46164, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Admiral was killed during our last naval engagement. I\'ve turned this ship into a fortress.$B$BWe\'re improvising here, $c.', '', 46163, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t get many visitors this deep in the Plaguewood.  Abominations, mostly.$b$bCan I help you with something?', '', 46162, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For the Horde!', '', 46161, 1, 10604, 66, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For the Horde!', '', 46160, 1, 10604, 66, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For da Horde!', '', 46159, 1, 10604, 66, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let everything you do be done for the Horde.', '', 46158, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Then it is done.', '', 46157, 1, 10604, 273, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will not fail you, Warchief.  I will lead as well as I can, and I will consult with the advisors you suggest.  I know what a tremendous honor you do me, and I will strive to be worthy of it.', '', 46156, 1, 10604, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They will help you Garrosh.  And I will help you.  I will find the answers that we need to assuage the fears of the people and soothe the elements.', '', 46155, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now you are thinking like a ruler, Garrosh.  You must look at all sides of a problem.  Consult with your advisors and act with confidence.', '', 46154, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But even we are not sure of all that is happening.  Should we capture these cultists and force their silence?  But that may anger the rest of the people... Still, we cannot allow the cult to spread fear and lies...', '', 46153, 1, 10604, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A good first test may be dealin\' with dese cultists.  Da people be scared.  Dey aren\'t sure what\'s goin\'on.', '', 46152, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And though I am leaving soon, I can also instruct you.', '', 46151, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You will not be alone.  You will have advisors: Cairne, Eitrigg, Vol\'jin.  They will help guide you.', '', 46150, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am honored, warchief.  But I feel unprepared for the life of a ruler.', '', 46149, 1, 10604, 2, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In my absence, I am instructing you, Garrosh Hellscream, to lead the Horde.  You have the strength and courage that our people need to survive in these trying times.', '', 46148, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It may take time to learn what I must.  I trust I will not be gone too long, but it could be weeks - even months.', '', 46147, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How long you gonna be gone?', '', 46146, 1, 10604, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, I leave for Nagrand to learn from the elements there.  They have suffered and seen many of these same symptoms.', '', 46145, 1, 10604, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'To the Greymane Wall! We will force their hand.', 46144, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Look at them, $p. They scurry like rats, veering headlong to their doom. Surely Crowley and Bloodfang can see the futility in this!', 46143, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Lay down your arms and surrender!', 46142, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I will leave your cities in dust and your lives in ruin!', 46141, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not now, $gpal:lady;.$B$BI gotta re-tune the boss\' shredder.$B$BShe don\'t like movin\' around the city on foot like any old chump, ESPECIALLY if she\'s gotta go deal with the warchief.', '', 46140, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Onward, $n! We will beat back the Alliance dogs and secure Lordaeron for the Forsaken! For the Horde!', 46139, 0, 0, 15, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Greetings, $n.', '', 46138, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s good to have traveling companions.  The road gets lonely out here.', '', 46137, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Look around... business is BOOMIN\'!$B$BWhile Gallywix is wastin\' time pickin\' custom wallpaper for his Pompous Palace in the Azsharan boondocks, I\'m makin\' twice the coin movin\' and shakin\' for Big G.$B$BYou heard me: Counting houses, trade halls, construction and maintenance, the war-works, supply lines...$B$BDon\'t even get me STARTED on transit! Orcs can fight, but they can\'t move goods; my boys ship it twice as fast for half the cost! Well... when it doesn\'t blow up along the way, hee.$B$BAnyhow! Take a load off, huh? Enjoy yourself, spend some coin... we\'ve got everything from money changers and laundry services to exotic drinks and fishing trainers.', 46136, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 11, 0, 0, 4, 0, 39653),
('', 'Relax, spend some coin... we\'ve got everything from money changers and laundry services to exotic drinks.$B$BAnd if anyone gives you any trouble? You just let ME know, and I\'ll handle it.$B$BI\'m Mida... the boss.$B$BOh, the renovations? Yeah, I\'m always willing to help our new allies for the right price!', 46135, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The creature is gaining power from the ancestral Grimtotem!  We must put them to rest if we are to defeat this beast!\n', '', 46134, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fire in the hole!', '', 46133, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blast \'em!', '', 46132, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let \'em have it!', '', 46131, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fire!', '', 46130, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m ready, commander, let\'s head up.', 'I\'m ready, commander, let\'s head up.', 46129, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good to see you again, $n. We snuck some more of us in here while you were prepping the Gates for the attack.$B$BI\'ll show you where we\'re to rendezvous with Master Shaw.$B$B<The squad leader produces a map of the Twilight Citadel and points to the spot.>$B$BLet me know when you\'re ready, and we\'ll all head up together.', '', 46128, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The creature is gaining power from the ancestral Grimtotem!  We must put them to rest if we are to defeat this beast!', 46127, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You will be punished for this transgression, thief!', '', 46126, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Engage secondary targets!', 46125, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The T.A.D. units have the priority targets!', 46124, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Geomancers, bury them in stone and flame!', '', 46123, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Reavers, at my side!', '', 46122, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stompers, defend your Chieftan!', '', 46121, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey boss.  You need someone to help drive the caravan, you just let ol\' Beezil know.', '', 46120, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You know, if you\'re looking for a place to hide out, you\'re free to join us in our caravan.', 'You know, if you\'re looking for a place to hide out, you\'re free to join us in our caravan.', 46119, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You present an interesting option, $r.  I\'ll take that into consideration.$b$bAlright, I\'ve considered it.  Sure, I\'ll join you.  I\'ve probably stayed in Light\'s Hope Chapel for too long anyhow.  Like a gnome at a urinal, I\'m gonna have to stay on my toes!  Heh heh!', '', 46118, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, ahh... hello there, good traveler!  What can this fine goblin do for you today?$b$bI\'ll assure you that I\'m here in Light\'s Hope Chapel solely due to my hatred of the Scourge which I share with these Argent Crusaders, and definitely not because I\'m running away from any sort of embarrassing zeppelin crash!$b$bI\'ll stop talking now, before I implicate myself any further!', '', 46117, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If one such as I can be captured by that lumbering oaf, then you must be brave indeed to venture here.\n\nIf you can distract Halfus and break the chains binding me then I will fight alongside you.\n\nMy ability to engulf an enemy in a furious tempest will impair Halfus\' efforts to unleash Shadow Novas.', '', 46116, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If one such as I can be captured by that lumbering oaf, then you must be brave indeed to venture here.\n\nIf you can distract Halfus and break the chains binding me then I will fight alongside you.\n\nMy ability to temporarily paralyze an enemy\'s body will grant you respite from Halfus\' Malevolent Strikes.', '', 46115, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If one such as I can be captured by that lumbering oaf, then you must be brave indeed to venture here.\n\nIf you can distract Halfus and break the chains binding me then I will fight alongside you.\n\nMy ability to blind the eyes of an enemy will help you withstand Halfus\' Frenzied Assault.', '', 46114, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We must avenge our mother!\n\nDistract the monster who slew her, free us from this cage, and we will fight by your side.\n\nOur ability to reduce the damage an enemy inflicts will help you survive the Proto-Behemoth\'s Scorching Breath.', '', 46113, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gidwin is nearby... I know it.  Paladin\'s intuition.', '', 46112, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll throw my hammer upside his head if he makes us wait any longer.', '', 46111, 0, 10652, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tyrosus himself sent us to Northdale!  So why are we wasting our time with upstart nerubians?!', '', 46110, 0, 10652, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t know why I put up with his nonsense.  He never takes anything seriously.', '', 46109, 0, 10652, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That useless blood elf!  We have a DUTY to perform, and he wastes our time!', '', 46108, 0, 10652, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Take the scout\'s spectacles.', 'Take the scout\'s spectacles.', 46107, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Incoming mortar barrage!', '', 46106, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('$R! Your corpse will feed the sea.', '', 46105, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alright, Gidwin... deep breaths...', '', 46104, 0, 10651, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What\'s the holdup, Fiona?', '', 46103, 0, 10651, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why haven\'t we left yet?  I\'m ready to head off on my own if we don\'t get going.', '', 46101, 0, 10651, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can\'t BELIEVE that we\'re stopping!  We\'ve got a duty to do here!', '', 46100, 0, 10651, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Well, well... look who\'s here!', 46099, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hey, $n!  You here to visit, or did you want to buy something?', 46098, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Good to see you again, $n!', 46097, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '<Fiona is rather upset.  She doesn\'t seem to be in the mood to talk.>', 46096, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Promise me you\'ll find him, $n.', 46095, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Why would he run off like that?!', 46094, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I hope you\'ve made yourself welcome to the items inside my caravan.  If we\'re not using them, you might as well borrow them.', 46093, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The boys and I have only traveled together for a little while, but I already can\'t imagine life without either one of them.', 46092, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'d like to set up shop in Light\'s Hope Chapel someday.  I\'m not much of a fighter, but that doesn\'t mean I can\'t help the cause.', 46091, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'By the way, you\'re welcome to borrow any supplies you find inside the caravan... as long as you bring them back when you\'re done!', 46090, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Looks like they found their way back home.  I\'m relieved.$b$bYou came back, too!  Are you interested in joining us?', 46089, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Spirits of Deepholm, grant me your strength!', '', 46088, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Spirits of Skywall, heed my call!', '', 46087, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We will always remember Kargath Bladefist for what he once was to the Horde. He was one of the finest warriors to ever live, even the Alliance recognizes this.$B$BThe Kargath Expeditionary force was named in his honor, and I plan to ensure we live up to his name. We will drive out the Dark Iron Dwarves and claim Blackrock Mountain, and all of the surrounding areas, for the Horde as they so rightfully belong.$B$BYou will be the Warchief\'s blade against Thaurissan. Wear that honor proudly.', '', 46086, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Spirits of the Firelands, fill me with your rage!', '', 46085, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Quickly! We must head back to the Forsaken Front before we are discovered!', '', 46084, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hold the line!', '', 46083, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This stronghold is fortified, but our enemies close in from all sides. We would be wise to secure our position on the coast before advancing farther inland. ', 46082, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You won\'t be able to open the back door yourself to escape once you\'ve started the chaos. You\'ll have to either get the guards to open it by killing bar patrons, get Private Rocknot drunk so he causes property damage, or see if Spazzring has the key on him!', 46081, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '%s falls unconscious.', 46080, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'HAH! You\'ll have to kill me! DIE!', 46079, 0, 0, 11, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now lay down your arms and surrender. We are not here to kill you. Not yet.', '', 46078, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your father and Greymane saw to that... No, Gilneas died when they allowed murderous beasts to reign free. Unchecked.', '', 46077, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My kingdom? My kingdom is no more.', '', 46076, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You would betray your kingdom out of spite?', 46075, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Godfrey? So the rumors are true.', 46074, 0, 0, 397, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lorna, is that how you greet old friends? ', '', 46073, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'So the Banshee Queen has sent assassins?', 46072, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I asked for reinforcements to help us hold the beach. And the Horde sent these tiny little men and their small metal tubes.$B$B<Gralok eyes the nearby goblins with disdain.>', '', 46071, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s hard to explain to the Dragonmaw concepts like, \"Fields of Fire\" or \"Suppressive Barrage.\"$B$BFortunately, they have a firm grasp of \"Kill Zones\" and ... uh, \"Murder.\"', '', 46070, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Charge!', '', 46069, 0, 0, 480, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I beg to differ.', '', 46068, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Just the two of you?  You\'ll never stand a chance.', 46067, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re wrong, banshee.  We\'ve come to take Gidwin back.', '', 46066, 0, 0, 397, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Oh really?  What exactly will you do, dwarf?  There\'s nobody to save you here.', 46065, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'ll never get away with this, you ugly, stinkin\' witch!', '', 46064, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('ASSASSINS! I\'ll take chunks out o\' you!', '', 46063, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ve been watching the Dark Iron for a long time...plotting, hoping, wishing for the chance to drive them away and take back my land.$B$BThey can keep Blackrock Mountain. I hope it erupts again and takes them all with it. I want what is now called the Burning Steppes, my part of the Redridge Mountains that their fiery overlord destroyed.$B$B$C, I\'m going to show the world the potential left in my land. I\'ll build a kingdom of peace and justice atop the death and trickery they leave behind them. My vigil is over. I\'m here to fight for what\'s rightfully mine.$B$BAnd I\'m willing to die for it.', 46062, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('KEEP FIGHTING! I\'M GOING UP TOP TO SPEAK WITH CHO\'GALL!', '', 46061, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('THERE\'S NOTHING HERE EXCEPT FOR THIS FOG!', '', 46060, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('WHAT WAS THAT?!', '', 46059, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('1...', '', 46058, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('2...', '', 46057, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('3...', '', 46056, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Deathwing has returned. He\'s seized Grim Batol and much of the highlands, and I feel near powerless to stop him.$B$BSoon, our queen shall arrive, and together we shall put the once Earthwarder in his place.', '', 46055, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You won\'t be able to open the back door yourself to escape once you\'ve started the chaos. You\'ll have to either get the guards to open it by killing bar patrons, get Private Rocknot drunk so he causes property damage, or see if Spazzring has the key on him!', 46054, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You always were a spineless coward, Dempsey.', '', 46053, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I welcome you into an eternity of service, thief.', '', 46052, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Once a thief, I am now a servant of the Stars.', '', 46051, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Those who behold the starlight must forever protect it!', '', 46050, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You... You saved me? I\'m a damned monster! YOU\'RE A DAMNED MONSTER! LOOK AT YOURSELF!', '', 46049, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We have sworn to serve, intruder. And so shall you.', '', 46048, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You tread on sacred ground! You must be purified!', '', 46045, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your theft is forbidden, trespasser!', '', 46044, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('HAH! Don\'t you recognize us, Dempsey? It\'s Godfrey. I have here Lord Walden and Baron Ashbury. We\'ve \"saved\" you and this is the thanks that we get?', '', 46043, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('HELP! HELP! I\'ve been captured by monsters!', '', 46042, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wha? What happened to me? WHO ARE YOU PEOPLE?', '', 46041, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am more than Forsaken... more than a man... I am something new. Something... else.', '', 46040, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Vengeance will be ours!', '', 46039, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rage is the only emotion I have left.', '', 46038, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m losing my mind. Can\'t keep my thoughts together...', '', 46037, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Keep the conversations curt. I am in no mood for whining or rambling.', '', 46036, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I always loved Silverpine -- until the Lich King let loose his rampaging Scourge armies and turned the land into a massive rotting corpse pit. Now the sight of it boils my green blood.', '', 46035, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is undoubtedly Godfrey\'s fault.', '', 46034, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And perhaps the best part, I now have a hungering for the flesh of other humanoids. Cannibalizing their rotting corpses grants me power. Yes, DE-LI-CIOUS...', '', 46033, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, and I am now able to shrug off mind controlling effects - BECAUSE I LACK A BRAIN!', '', 46032, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Being Forsaken has its benefits. Let me see... I am able to practically live underwater. I can stay submerged 233%% longer than any fleshy mortal. Yes, count it, 233%%.', '', 46031, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They should have burned my damned corpse.', '', 46030, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('I did not bring this wretched affliction upon myself, Godfrey. It was a \"gift,\" remember? Now kindly enjoy the \"gift\" and shut up.', '', 46029, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For pity\'s sake, Ashbury, cover yourself. Your leg bones are popping out.', '', 46028, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gilneas was an impossible dream. Only a man of true vision could have seen it through... but Greymane? Never...', '', 46027, 0, 0, 274, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We used to burn the worgen when we killed them - to be sure that they were dead.', '', 46026, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('\"It\'s over, Godfrey...\" That\'s what he told me right before I jumped off of the cliff. NOTHING IS OVER, GREYMANE! I LIVE AGAIN!', '', 46025, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Never did I dream that our \"king\" would betray us as he did. To think that he had been a worgen in secret while he ruled over us. Sickening...', '', 46024, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Just do as I say and this war will end without incident. Unless you count the death of every worgen in Lordaeron as an incident.', '', 46023, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bloodfang? When the attacks upon Gilneas first occurred, it was Bloodfang\'s worgen that lead the charge. This monster and his pack have been terrorizing these lands for years.', '', 46022, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Crowley? I knew him. He was nothing more than a criminal before the curse took hold of our land. Now he\'s a great worgen hero? Sickening...', '', 46021, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I feel slightly unhinged. I am not taking well to this... condition.', '', 46020, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Firelord will bring about the end of Azeroth at long last! You will burn in his fury, fools!', 46019, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Dragonmaw stand proudly with the Horde. The Twilight Citadel will fall, $n!', 46018, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You see, Cozwynn, I told you that we could rely upon $n.', 46017, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'These Twilight scum can\'t hold out much longer. The Dragonmaw Clan has waited a long time for this, $n.', 46016, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Good to see you again, $n. I look forward to fighting by your side once more.', 46015, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s my $g boy : girl;! How goes the fight, $n?', '', 46014, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We Wildhammer are a proud bunch. I trust that you have as much pride in the Alliance, $n?', '', 46013, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('See, Cassius. I told you that we could depend upon $n.', '', 46012, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good! I\'m glad you\'re here, $n. We have much to discuss.', '', 46011, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|TInterface\\Icons\\ability_warrior_shieldreflection.blp:20|tOzruk casts |cFFFF0000|Hspell:78939|h[Elementium Bulwark]|h|r!', '', 46010, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('|TInterface\\Icons\\ability_warrior_charge.blp:20|tGeneral Umbriss sets his eyes on |cFFFF0000$n|r and begins to cast |cFFFF0000|Hspell:74670|h[Blitz]|h|r!', '', 46009, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Drinking a healing potion!  I won\'t be able to use another one for a while!', '', 46008, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Lady Windrunner herself sent me to serve as the Horde liaison to Zaela and the Dragonmaw clan. She and the new Warchief, Garrosh, are attempting to mend their broken fences, it would seem.$B$BIn any case, we must put an end to the Twilight threat once and for all. Most importantly, though, we must keep Cho\'gall from creating his ultimate weapon.', 46007, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey, why not you say so? Give dem Twilight\'s the ol\' one-two, den ya comin\' back here an\' we party!$B$BI gots me a sweet lil\' place down on dey beach with me lady. You comin\' by!', '', 46006, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Drinking a healing potion!  I won\'t be able to use another one for a while!', 46005, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Jon-Jon, I\'m here to lead your wind rider squad and drop off the Kor\'kron assassins.', 'Jon-Jon, I\'m here to lead your wind rider squad and drop off the Kor\'kron assassins.', 46004, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dere\'s nothin\' bettah dan flyin\' ovah ya enemies an\' droppin\' dey boom-boom bombs on dem!$B$BDat, or droppin\' two-hundred, fifty pound orcs on dere heads. Right, mon?', '', 46003, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 11, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be seein\' ya back at Crushblow.', 'Be seein\' ya back at Crushblow.', 46002, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You kill dese ettins so we be comin\' back ta finish dey job, mon!', 'You kill dese ettins so we be comin\' back ta finish dey job, mon!', 46001, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bye-bye now!', 'Bye-bye now!', 46000, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Okey dokey. We outta here, mon!', 'Okey dokey. We outta here, mon!', 45999, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why we gotta taxi you? Canna ya just sneak in dere, mon?', 'Why we gotta taxi you? Canna ya just sneak in dere, mon?', 45998, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Assassins? What we need ta do is drop some firebombs on dem!', 'Assassins? What we need ta do is drop some firebombs on dem!', 45997, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s get ta dey drop point!', 'Let\'s get ta dey drop point!', 45996, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Someone needs ta lose some weight, mon.', 'Someone needs ta lose some weight, mon.', 45995, 0, 0, 273, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Kill dem for me!', 'Kill dem for me!', 45994, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Twilight scum!', 'Twilight scum!', 45993, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dey were too many, mon!', 'Dey were too many, mon!', 45992, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get ta dey drop point!', 'Get ta dey drop point!', 45991, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stinkin\' ettins!', 'Stinkin\' ettins!', 45990, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For dey Horde!', 'For dey Horde!', 45989, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dey came at us from everywhere, mon!', 'Dey came at us from everywhere, mon!', 45988, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Aaaeeeiiii!', 'Aaaeeeiiii!', 45987, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('See you back at Victor\'s Point!', 'See you back at Victor\'s Point!', 45986, 0, 0, 3, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Kill these ettins so that we can come back and finish the job.', 'Kill these ettins so that we can come back and finish the job.', 45985, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thanks for the company!', 'Thanks for the company!', 45984, 0, 0, 3, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We\'re out of here. Good luck!', 'We\'re out of here. Good luck!', 45983, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We must stop Cho\'gall from creating his ultimate weapon at all costs, even if that means sacrificing ourselves.', '', 45982, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For Kurdran!', 'For Kurdran!', 45981, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Twilight\'s Hammer pukes!', 'Twilight\'s Hammer pukes!', 45980, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Aaaagghhh!', 'Aaaagghhh!', 45978, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stinking ettins!', 'Stinking ettins!', 45977, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Reduced to ashes... Soon nothing will be left of Gilneas or the worgen taint.', '', 45976, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Through fire we purge this land of its impurities.', '', 45975, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Some people only want to watch the world burn. Others want to be the ones responsible for burning it...', '', 45974, 0, 0, 11, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s get something straight... we\'re not your taxi service!', 'Let\'s get something straight... we\'re not your taxi service!', 45973, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hang on tight. It\'s going to get bumpy!', 'Hang on tight. It\'s going to get bumpy!', 45971, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We need to lighten the load here.', 'We need to lighten the load here.', 45970, 0, 0, 1, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s get these humans to the drop point.', 'Let\'s get these humans to the drop point.', 45969, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wildhammers!', 'Wildhammers!', 45968, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get to the drop point!', 'Get to the drop point!', 45967, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They came out of nowhere!', 'They came out of nowhere!', 45966, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There were... too many!', 'There were... too many!', 45964, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('After a quick assessment, you determine that this fellow has expired within the last several hours.', '', 45963, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve done it!$b$bUsing sapphire from the chamber\'s adornments, I have fashioned a pair of goggles. With them, I am able to see things...Amazing things!$b$bWith luck, my next entry will find me a newly rich man!', '', 45962, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Report!', '', 45961, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It has taken me all day to wrestle the cipher from these hieroglyphs:$b$b$b   Through eyes of blue is starlight$b              revealed.$b$b   Ten shards, one rod, and the veil$b             disappears.$b$b$bForget Schnottz and his empty promises!$b$bIf I can just unravel this riddle, its secrets shall be mine!', '', 45960, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A most productive day, today!$b$bThe chamber is indeed of ancient origin, and houses a magnificent mechanism which seems to be in disrepair.$b$bI will investigate further tomorrow.$b$bThis discovery will surely force Schnottz to take notice of me!$b$bHow could he deny me a promotion after something like this?', '', 45959, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Take your lies and leave me in peace, cultist. You\'ve already done enough damage here!', 'Take your lies and leave me in peace, cultist. You\'ve already done enough damage here!', 45958, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You will own this peninsula, $c.$B$BYou will be a weapon.$B$BYou will be a minister of death, praying for war.', '', 45957, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Worthless maggot.', '', 45956, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Cowards don\'t get to return home.', '', 45955, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is a mercy killing.', '', 45954, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('$g He:She; died in battle. Bow your heads...', '', 45953, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get out of my sight before I execute you!', '', 45952, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('These cowering troopers should die in shame. This is an embarassment.', '', 45951, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would have burned this whole place down with them in it...', '', 45950, 0, 0, 273, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Haven\'t you poisoned the minds of enough men with your lies? Stay away from me!', 'Haven\'t you poisoned the minds of enough men with your lies? Stay away from me!', 45949, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Dark Lady lets these mongrels live? Useless...', '', 45948, 0, 0, 6, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Cowardly dog. Run back to your mommy and hide.', '', 45947, 0, 0, 5, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Take your vile message away from this city! You will steal no more citizens away with your fake \'prophecies\'!', 'Take your vile message away from this city! You will steal no more citizens away with your fake \'prophecies\'!', 45946, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Begone! Isn\'t it enough that you have taken my husband? What more do you want?', 'Begone! Isn\'t it enough that you have taken my husband? What more do you want?', 45945, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We overheard their orders... no survivors...', 'We overheard their orders... no survivors...', 45944, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They\'re EVERYWHERE! WATCH OUT!', 'They\'re EVERYWHERE! WATCH OUT!', 45943, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You filthy cultists have taken my husband from me! He just left us behind and went to follow all this \'end of the world\' nonsense you\'re spouting!', 'You filthy cultists have taken my husband from me! He just left us behind and went to follow all this \'end of the world\' nonsense you\'re spouting!', 45942, 0, 0, 25, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You must be the hero that everyone is talking about. Thank you.', 'You must be the hero that everyone is talking about. Thank you.', 45941, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I thought I was done for!', 'I thought I was done for!', 45940, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They struck from the shadows. We didn\'t stand a chance.', 'They struck from the shadows. We didn\'t stand a chance.', 45939, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Are... are they all dead?', 'Are... are they all dead?', 45938, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is it safe?', 'Is it safe?', 45937, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We have our best people looking into these issues.', '', 45936, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We take these missing person reports very seriously, ma\'am.', '', 45935, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We are investigating the cultists activities as we speak.', '', 45934, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We have the situation under control.', '', 45933, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We are doing everything we can.', '', 45932, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('As soon as we have some news we will let you know.', '', 45931, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We are looking into the missing person reports you filed.', '', 45930, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We are looking into these cultists groups.', '', 45929, 0, 0, 396, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t let anybody tell you that the Scourge is defeated.  Look... do they not still roam the Plaguewood?  They cling to their corrupted land like a child\'s blanket.$b$bI have no choice but to fight.  Until my last breath, I will fight them.', '', 45928, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, why didn\'t you say so? Give those Twilight cultists a good one from me, will ya?', '', 45927, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Angus, I\'m here to lead the Wildhammer squad and drop off the SI:7 agents.', 'Angus, I\'m here to lead the Wildhammer squad and drop off the SI:7 agents.', 45926, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There\'s nothing more exciting than to soar through the air.$B$BWell, maybe to fight while soaring through the air, and a good tankard of ale afterward!', '', 45925, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The portal has been opened! Thanks to your efforts, we can now quickly travel from Stormwind to Twilight Highlands.', 45924, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'By wind and wave, by earth and fire... To Stormwind we go, $n!', 45923, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please... Make it stop.', 'Please... Make it stop.', 45922, 0, 0, 20, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why is this happening?', 'Why is this happening?', 45921, 0, 0, 18, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t want to die!', 'I don\'t want to die!', 45920, 0, 0, 18, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve found an incredible site!$b$bThe whole area pulsates with the hum of ancient architecture.$b$bIf it were not so late in the day, I would investigate the chamber immediately!$b$bSleeping, tonight, will be a struggle...', '', 45919, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We are doomed!', 'We are doomed!', 45918, 0, 0, 430, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Earthquake!', 'Earthquake!', 45917, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
