('Ogre Pinata', 'Ogre Pinata', 34849, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Path of Cenarius', 'Path of Cenarius', 34848, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fields of Honor', 'Fields of Honor', 34847, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You might have gone feral, but Gilnean blood still pumps through your veins.  Defend our homelands agains the Horde!', '', 34846, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gilneas needs you!  Now is not the time to retreat to the woods like a pack of wild animals!  Face the enemy and live or die as Gilneans not as beasts!', '', 34845, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do not give in to the curse!  You were men and women of Gilneas once... you can be men and women of Gilneas again!', '', 34844, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The savior of the forest! Were it not for your actions, Astranaar and then the rest of Ashenvale surely would have fallen to the Burning Legion.$B$BI hope that this day finds you well, $n!', '', 34843, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 34, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good day to you, $r.', '', 34842, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 33, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What is it, $r? Time is money!', '', 34841, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, look out behind you, $n!', '', 34840, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bolyun, is Kariva still about?', 'Bolyun, is Kariva still about?', 34839, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Beware, $n!', '', 34838, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Ahahahaha, you\'ve fallen into my trap, $n!', 34837, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wahoo!!', '', 34836, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s smiles at you knowingly as it approaches.', '', 34835, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s approaches the moonwell slowly, a familiar, thoughtful look upon its face.', '', 34834, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s rests on the side of the moonwell in peaceful contemplation.', '', 34833, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s fades into existence as you approach, nodding a subtle greeting.', '', 34832, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Just a pinch...', '', 34831, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s put this stuff to the test...', '', 34830, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can\'t wait any longer. I\'m going to set it off! Muahahahahahaha!', '', 34829, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Someone get me somebody stupid enough to move this thing into Stonetalon!', '', 34828, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Somebody set us up The Bomb!', '', 34827, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is The Bomb to end all bombs!', '', 34826, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Harder, better, faster, stronger!', '', 34825, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do it!', '', 34824, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Make it!', '', 34823, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Work it!', '', 34822, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Incredible shooting! I\'ll try to calm the animals down. Report to Thork, he will want to know of this attack.', '', 34821, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Shade of the Kaldorei closes its eyes and fades away.', '', 34820, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s stares into the moonwell, lost in distant memories.', '', 34819, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There she is. Mount up!', '', 34818, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bring it on, Rocco.', 'Bring it on, Rocco.', 34817, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Are you ready to do this, $n?', '', 34816, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('None know what to expect next, but with Malfurion and Tyrande reunited, a new hope dawns on the Kaldorei.', '', 34815, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Though a small corruption lingers, desperately longing to be cleansed, the boughs of Teldrassil itself seem changed.  Growth has begun anew.', '', 34814, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And with his return came Alexstrasza and Ysera, to at long last offer their blessings upon Teldrassil.', '', 34813, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But in his place, Shan\'do Stormrage awoke from the dream and returned to his beloved Tyrande Whisperwind.', '', 34812, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We break from this haze to find that Fandral Staghelm and many of his closest followers have disappeared without a word.', '', 34811, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In weeks past, all of those living atop Teldrassil have found their memories blurry, as if time itself seized a portion of their lives.', '', 34810, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fandral Staghelm carries the burden of our sins and our follies, and in so doing deserves the respect of us all.', '', 34809, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But many druids of the Cenarion Circle stand firm that he wants only what is best for all of the Kaldorei, and serve him unerringly towards that end.', '', 34808, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Others cite rumors of his escalating conflicts with Tyrande Whisperwind, the shining light of our people, our leader in Darnassus.', '', 34807, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Some pose that he blames us, his people, for the loss of his son, long ago during the War of the Shifting Sands.', '', 34806, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Over time, Staghelm only grew more disconnected from our people.', '', 34805, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Staghelm retreated to his enclave in Darnassus, ever seeking a new direction by which to bless Teldrassil, and restore the immortality of our people.', '', 34804, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In agreement, Alexstrasza also refused Staghelm, and without her blessing, Teldrassil\'s growth has been flawed and unpredictable.', '', 34803, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But Nozdormu, Lord of Time, refused to give his blessing, chiding the druid for his arrogance.', '', 34802, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Archdruid approached the dragons for their blessings, as the dragons had placed on Nordrassil in ancient times.', '', 34801, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Though we have our new home, our immortal lives have not been restored.', '', 34800, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In an effort to regain immortality for our people, and with the approval of the Circle, Staghelm and the most powerful druids grew Teldrassil, upon whose boughs you now stand.', '', 34799, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Archdruid Fandral Staghelm roused the druids and convinced the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore that it was time for our people to rebuild.', '', 34798, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('With Malfurion Stormrage gone, the druids were left in disarray and in desperate need of a new leader.', '', 34797, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A dark time for all.', '', 34796, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Betrayer was freed from his prison, and Shand\'do Stormrage disappeared into the emerald dream.', '', 34795, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Our immortality-the very essence of our beings!-was lost.', '', 34794, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nordrassil lies a pale shadow of what it once was, its power used to defeat Archimonde and drive back the Burning Legion.', '', 34793, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Much has changed for our people since the Battle of Mount Hyjal.', '', 34792, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Used to be hauling gear and food from Orgrimmar to Crossroads was peon-work. Nowadays my neck\'s always on the line.', '', 34791, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ho, $n! My brother Balgor tells me you\'re quite the shot from the back of a kodo. Great work getting that caravan here from Far Watch in one piece.$B$BListen, there\'s plenty of work for you here in Grol\'dom... but I could use your trigger fingers for the rest of the ride to Crossroads.$B$BCome see me when you\'re ready!', '', 34790, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 3, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No Pennant', 'No Pennant', 34789, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I know all is not well in Shadowglen, but coming back to these woods is always like coming back home.$B$BEver peaceful. Ever pure.', 34788, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not again!', '', 34787, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey! Just what do you think you\'re doing?', '', 34786, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I lied. Your miserable food stinks, but not as much as this town is going to stink!', '', 34785, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s the idea.', '', 34784, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I know, sister. I know. We\'ll return to fighting one day. For now, though, maybe it\'s best to spread the word to others... give them the hope you have.', '', 34783, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mmmm... There\'s nothing like good, home-cooked human food.', '', 34782, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Still... there is balance in all things, even death. I simply hate the concept that such destruction and darkness might be necessary.', '', 34781, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I know I\'m counseling patience, Aponi, but I don\'t like remaining here any more than you do. Times are bleak, and failing to act only makes me worry that my idle hand may have been the one to turn the tide.', '', 34780, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m thinking about the front to the north. The one you\'re so eager to return to.', '', 34779, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sorry, sister. It\'s nothing to worry about.', '', 34778, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'And through that hope, strengthen our side in the fight?', 34777, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'But I\'d still rather be there on the front lines helping it happen rather than trying to placate myself with belief. We can\'t just sit around and hope it happens.', 34776, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Even on the glacier itself, the sun manages to peek through the gloom. I have hope, Tahu. I think we\'ll make it through this, no matter how dire it looks.', 34775, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '%s smiles and gestures to the north.', 34774, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'There\'s a phrase... \"It\'s always darkest before the dawn.\" The dawn will come, though, Tahu. The sun will rise. The balance will shift back to where it should be.', 34773, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'What about it?', 34772, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'But something is on your mind, right?', 34771, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I see that thoughtful frown, Tahu.', 34770, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I suppose so. It\'s not silly, though, what you said.', 34769, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'So are you going to bring this up to the elder?', 34768, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Do you think his teachings are wrong?', 34767, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I hear the \"but\" in your voice...', 34766, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Where are you going with this?', 34765, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Like Mu\'sha.', 34764, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Not much.', 34763, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Talk to me, Tahu. Something. Anything! I\'m going stir-crazy.', 34762, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Another new face? It\'s so good to meet you. I\'m Dellylah.', 34761, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The revitalized kodo rises to its feet, shaking off the dust.', '', 34760, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nom nom nom nom nom...', '', 34759, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This is awful! I shouldn\'t be sitting here, useless, when there\'s so much to be done! If only my arm hadn\'t gotten injured up in Northrend... No use dwelling on it, though! Tahu will have me patched up and cured eventually, and we\'ll still help around here in the meantime.\n\nJust because we\'re not at the front doesn\'t mean we can\'t help out somehow.', 34758, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Surely you\'ve been a student once in your life, $c. You learned from an instructor, and you gained respect for them in some way, yes? Maybe not as a person, but at the least, as one who knew more than you and was willing to teach you. If not, use your imagination...$b$bWhat would you do if you came to realize your instructor may not know as much as you thought, and that you may have found a better path?', '', 34757, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, it isn\'t exactly a new thought, sister.', '', 34756, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No, no. No need for him to trouble about a student\'s idle philosophizing while he entertains a friend.', '', 34755, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And while we, as druids, are guardians of nature, I wonder if we\'ve overlooked a key aspect of balance in all things.', '', 34754, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But we\'re nothing if not people who strive for balance. Our warriors fight only when there is need. Our hunters take only what the tribes require to live, and use all they can when they do. The shaman stand as guide and mediator to the elemental spirits.', '', 34753, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Freya drains the essence of Eonar\'s Gift, healing nearby allies!', 'Freya drains the essence of Eonar\'s Gift, healing nearby allies!', 34752, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No! No, nothing like that. He is an elder for good reason, sister. Mu\'sha is one of the Earthmother\'s eyes, and she watches over us. That isn\'t sinister. ', '', 34751, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('...but what Hamuul teaches is what the elves know. The night elves. They put such stock in their moon goddess, as creatures of the night.', '', 34750, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wonder. Hamuul has guided us well, and I\'ve learned so much from him. The legends say that our people were druids when time began...', '', 34749, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Just like her. The parallels I\'ve heard are interesting. And it\'s no secret all druids, Shu\'halo and elf alike, can call upon Mu\'sha\'s light.', '', 34748, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The elves speak of a moon goddess, did you know? They put great stock in the light given by the moon.', '', 34747, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All right, Aponi. I\'ve enough on my mind to share. Have you ever spoken to the elves of Moonglade?', '', 34746, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s laughs softly.', '', 34745, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We Razormane ... must ... survive ...', '', 34744, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tortusk barks, grunts, and snorts angry instructions to his followers.', '', 34743, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('These lands will be ours!', '', 34742, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Haha - <snort> ha - heee! <snort> Haha no stop haha <SNORT> <wheeze> Hee hee! Battlemaster Tortusk never prepared us for this!', '', 34741, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
