('Lumbering in from the south, the smell of Carnage precedes him!', '', 32758, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Circling Valhalas, Sigrid Iceborn approaches to seek her revenge!', '', 32757, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You both have my thanks and that of the village, though many will never know of your deeds.', '', 32756, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('With my help, $n travelled back in time to your battle, and ensured that history was set right. The North Wind\'s fate was sealed, and your story restored.', '', 32755, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It would\'ve succeeded if $n and I hadn\'t tracked the North Wind\'s historical corruptions to their source: your ancient battle.', '', 32754, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Khit\'rix the Dark Master skitters into Valhalas from the southeast!', '', 32753, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The wind used its minions to distort the history of this place, changing the stories your people told, destroying the spirits of the honored dead.', '', 32752, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But the North Wind did not silently accept defeat. Instead, it gathered power and bided its time, deciding the best revenge was to destroy your memory, and with it, your village.', '', 32751, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your battle with the wind was hundreds of years ago, Stormhoof. You weakened it so much that it has been silent all these years.', '', 32750, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The North Wind? It still troubles my people?', '', 32749, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And it very nearly didn\'t remember you. $n fought bravely against the North Wind to protect your story.', '', 32748, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is Camp Tunka\'lo, the village ruled by my brother, but I... I don\'t remember you.', '', 32747, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The bronze dragonflight. They snatched me from the brink of death and took me before their master, Nozdormu. He said they had been watching me and wanted me to continue my hunt. He granted me immortality as a watcher, tasked to bear witness to the history of Azeroth as one of his agents.$B$BI am Xarantaur the Witness, and it is my duty to preserve the true history of Azeroth lest it be forgotten.', '', 32746, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They?', 'They?', 32745, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wandered for the rest of my natural life in search of knowledge, seeing more wonder and meeting more strange and mysterious races than any of my people before me. I travelled across the length and breadth of ancient Kalimdor until there was no more to see, no new lands across the horizon.$B$BYet... there was still so much I did not know as I felt my final journey approaching and I wept for the things I would never know.$B$BAs I fell, my life at an end, that is when they found me.', '', 32744, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please, go on.', 'Please, go on.', 32743, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I was one of the first tauren druids, of the last generation taught by Shan\'do Cenarius, before the Legion, before the Sundering, when the world was still young. Before everything changed.$B$BWhile my brethren hunted great beasts, I hunted stories. I had been drawn to the druidic arts by this hunger, this lust for knowledge. For a time, that hunger was sated as I learned to talk to the trees, rocks, and beasts, and heard their stories.$B$BBut then, the time came when Cenarius walked among us no more and my brethren began to forget what he had taught us. I could not forget, though, and I still needed to learn more about our world.$B$BSo I said my farewells and travelled beyond the lands of my people.', '', 32742, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me of yourself, Xarantaur. Why are you called the Witness?', 'Tell me of yourself, Xarantaur. Why are you called the Witness?', 32741, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
