('Sorry, but Chromie said that I couldn\'t reveal anything about your future to you. She said that if I did, I would cease to exist.', 'Sorry, but Chromie said that I couldn\'t reveal anything about your future to you. She said that if I did, I would cease to exist.', 27311, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oy mon! I know you?$b$bAhh yeah, Prigmon not forget a face.$b$bYou... followin\' me, mon? Cuz whatver it be, Prigmon never done it!', '', 27310, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oy, mon!$b$bThis not be what it looks like. Well, maybe...$b$bIt be complicated.', '', 27309, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mack belches loudly...', '', 27308, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wow, I\'d forgotten how inexperienced I used to be.', 'Wow, I\'d forgotten how inexperienced I used to be.', 27307, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No matter what, you can\'t die, because that would mean that I would cease to exist, right? But, I was here before when I was you. I\'m so confused!', 'No matter what, you can\'t die, because that would mean that I would cease to exist, right? But, I was here before when I was you. I\'m so confused!', 27306, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What? Am I here alone. We both have a stake in this, you know!', 'What? Am I here alone. We both have a stake in this, you know!', 27305, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look at you fight; no wonder I turned to drinking.', 'Look at you fight; no wonder I turned to drinking.', 27304, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Harry said I could take his bomber to Bael\'gun\'s. I\'m ready to go!', 'Harry said I could take his bomber to Bael\'gun\'s. I\'m ready to go!', 27303, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This is the only way Harry will even talk to me! I have to keep this stupid mask on all the time...', 27302, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can\'t believe that I used to wear that.', 'I can\'t believe that I used to wear that.', 27301, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My business partner slays things; I drain a portion of their essence... a pittance, really; the slightest of slivers. It won\'t be missed.$B$BStill, to fulfil my portion of the contract, I pay in Ethereal Credits.$B$BOne may redeem these credits for items I sell at any time. I\'m bound to have something that will interest you...', '', 27300, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Show me what you have to trade.', 'Show me what you have to trade.', 27299, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How does this work?', 'How does this work?', 27298, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How may this one help you, $gsir:madame;?', '', 27296, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I have arrived. Shall we set to work, then?', '', 27295, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Admiral Keller sent me, Emilune. Please send me to Westguard Keep!', 'Admiral Keller sent me, Emilune. Please send me to Westguard Keep!', 27294, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Elune watch over you, $r.', 27293, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s it! Far as I got... Whatd\'ya think?', '', 27292, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('...on an open fire.....', '', 27291, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shcourged trooolls roashting....', '', 27290, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is from this throne that I issue the command of Hellscream. His word is life and his word is death.', '', 27289, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There ya go, mon. Try ta be more careful with this one, won\'t ya?$b$bNow head down ta Drak\'Zin Ruins and drink it near the pedestal!', '', 27288, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Farewell, $n. Keep us alive and get some better equipment!', 'Farewell, $n. Keep us alive and get some better equipment!', 27287, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I need another of your elixirs, Drakuru.', 'I need another of your elixirs, Drakuru.', 27286, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ey, mon!$b$bGood to be seein\' ya again... $n, right? Yes, yes, of course.$b$bYou and I gunna be real good friends. Drakuru know dese things.$b$b<A grin slowly spreads across the troll\'s painted face.>', '', 27285, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Time was when I\'d pull yer heart out ya just ta see da look on yer face....', '', 27284, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shake Drakuru\'s outstretched hand.', 'Shake Drakuru\'s outstretched hand.', 27283, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Drakuru extends his bleeding hand through the cage and looks at you with anticipation.>', '', 27282, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('AAAAHHH!!', 'AAAAHHH!!', 27281, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('YEEOOWCH!', 'YEEOOWCH!', 27280, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('AYYYIEEE!!', 'AYYYIEEE!!', 27279, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('OWWWW!', 'OWWWW!', 27278, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bah! You\'re as dumb as a rock! I hope the worms eat all of you.', '', 27277, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s waves dismissively.', '', 27276, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look, $n, the hourglass has revealed Nozdormu!', 'Look, $n, the hourglass has revealed Nozdormu!', 27275, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Greenskin... I know why you\'ve come. You will not find allies in my kind for we do not trust you.', '', 27274, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('YAAARRRRR! Here we be, matey! Scalawag Point!', '', 27273, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hang on to your hat, $n! To Scalawag we go!', '', 27272, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Good luck, and be safe. Here comes Uther and Jaina now.', 27271, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Very well, Chromie.', 'Very well, Chromie.', 27270, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Well, you\'re not going to sign recruitment papers or anything, but you are going to fight alongside him.$B$BYou need to make sure Arthas culls Stratholme and defeats Mal\'Ganis. Without Uther and Jaina around, he\'ll need all the help he can get.$B$BIf you talk to Arthas, he\'ll put you to work destroying the forces of Mal\'Ganis. Follow along until I can figure out what\'s going on with the Infinites.', 27269, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You want me to do what?', 'You want me to do what?', 27268, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I don\'t know, and that worries me. I\'ll do everything I can to find the Infinites.$B$BWhat I need you to do now is stay close to Arthas by joining his army.', 27267, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What do you think they\'re up to?', 'What do you think they\'re up to?', 27266, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Good work! Arthas now knows about the plagued grain in Stratholme, and is about to begin the culling.$B$BSomething is still not quite right, though. I sense a foreign presence in this timeline besides us, and that must mean the Infinite Dragonflight are here somewhere.', 27265, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('Once again, all soldiers of Lordaeron are ordered to immediately report to the entrance of Stratholme, and await further instructions from Prince Arthas.', '', 27264, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All soldiers of Lordaeron should immediately report to the entrance of Stratholme, and await further orders from Prince Arthas.', '', 27263, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Unstable Mur\'ghoul is about to explode!', '', 27262, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh darn. You\'re our only hope. Survive!', 'Oh darn. You\'re our only hope. Survive!', 27261, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The %s claws at the ground.', '', 27260, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I guess I\'ll go find the authorities. If I\'m lucky they\'ll tell me it\'s the plague and that we\'re all going to die.', '', 27259, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, come on! My cart broke, my horse lost a shoe, and now the cargo goes bad!', '', 27258, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, guess I should load everything back into the cart.', '', 27257, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wasn\'t even supposed to be here today!', '', 27256, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m going to lose my on time bonus because of this!', '', 27255, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This grain shipment has been nothing but trouble!', '', 27254, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I knew I should have secured the wagon lock better when I was in Andorhal.', '', 27253, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wait a second. Grain isn\'t supposed to smell like THAT! I better go find a guard.', '', 27252, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Heads up... here they come. I\'ll help as much as I can. Let\'s just keep them off of the hourglass!', 'Heads up... here they come. I\'ll help as much as I can. Let\'s just keep them off of the hourglass!', 27251, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, close call. It\'s just the grain here.', '', 27250, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can\'t be me, I took a bath 3 days ago!', '', 27249, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wait, what\'s that smell?', '', 27248, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ok, enough work for now. Time for refreshments and a little conversation in the inn.', '', 27247, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Have you heard of the taunka? They are supposedly related to tauren in some way. Can you imagine such a thing?', 27246, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'What was that! Did you see that?', 27245, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I thought for sure that I would die like all the others!', 27244, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'How will we overcome the mist?', 27243, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Infinite Dragonflight has destroyed the %s!', '', 27242, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is no good, Scruffy. Stay here and guard the house, I need to go find a soldier.', '', 27241, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What did you find, boy?', '', 27240, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey there, $n, don\'t be alarmed. It\'s me... you... from the future.  I\'m here to help.', 'Hey there, $n, don\'t be alarmed. It\'s me... you... from the future.  I\'m here to help.', 27239, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What\'s wrong, pal?', '', 27238, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s begins to growl...', '', 27237, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Looks like a storm\'s coming in, Scruffy...', '', 27236, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Oh, my.', 27235, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pardon me, $r, but I am on official business and cannot be disturbed.$b$bPlease excuse me.', '', 27234, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My warmages are inbound and will arrive presently.$b$bSpeak to me again when they have returned,', '', 27233, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Oh hello, Jena. Of course you can borrow some grain. Help yourself.', 27232, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Martha, something\'s wrong with this grain! Some of the Prince\'s soldiers were looking for this. I\'m going to go look for one.', 27231, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Oh, dear.', 27230, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Thanks, Martha! I owe you one.', 27229, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Here ya go, friend! Icehammer is right inside that vrykul building! Give \'em hell!', 'Here ya go, friend! Icehammer is right inside that vrykul building! Give \'em hell!', 27228, 7, 7239, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Keep a close eye on your surroundings. The route I\'m taking is the same route you can use to get back to Valgarde.', 'Keep a close eye on your surroundings. The route I\'m taking is the same route you can use to get back to Valgarde.', 27227, 7, 7239, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pay attention, friend! We\'re headin\' into hostile territory with both vrykul and Horde all over the place!', 'Pay attention, friend! We\'re headin\' into hostile territory with both vrykul and Horde all over the place!', 27226, 7, 7239, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Off we go!', 'Off we go!', 27225, 7, 7239, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Martha, I\'m out of flour for bread. You wouldn\'t happen to have any grain from that recent shipment, would you?', 27224, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Ah, I\'ll make him some fresh bread! I need to get some flour from Martha!', 27223, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Strawberries! Oh wait, they\'re not in season.', 27222, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I need to make something healthy for him, he\'s still not recovered from that illness from last week.', 27221, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ve got plenty of cured bacon, but he had some for breakfast.', 27220, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Let\'s see, we had chicken last night.', 27219, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Who... Who am I?\n', '', 27218, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('O\' my head... Wh... Where am I?\n', '', 27217, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We\'ll see about that, Perelli. We\'ll see about that.', '', 27216, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now, I call out to the spirits of this place. I will give anything or pay any price, if only you will help me save my people.\n', '', 27215, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Damn the men! Nothing shall prevent me from having my revenge, old friend. Not even you.\n', '', 27214, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have to believe me, I\'m innocent!', '', 27213, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Leave it be, Arthas. Forget this business and lead your men home.\n', '', 27212, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would gladly bear any curse to save my homeland.\n', '', 27211, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m confiscating this suspicious grain, Perelli. We were looking for signs of tampered food, and it would be in your best interest to stay put while Prince Arthas checks this out.', '', 27210, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hold, lad. There\'s an inscription on the dais. It\'s a warning. It says, \"Whomsoever takes up this blade shall wield power eternal. Just as the blade rends flesh, so must power scar the spirit.\" Oh, I should\'ve known. The blade is cursed! Let\'s get the hell out of here!\n', '', 27209, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What are you talking about, Sergeant!', '', 27208, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Behold, Muradin, our salvation, Frostmourne.\n', '', 27207, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wait, what is this? You\'ve been holding out on me, Perelli!', '', 27206, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You don\'t mind me checking out your merchandise for signs of tampering, do you?', '', 27205, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Xink\'s Shredder collapses and sputters to a stop.', '', 27204, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Absolutely.', '', 27203, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, Sergeant Morigan.', '', 27202, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, sir.', '', 27201, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nope.', '', 27200, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No, sir.', '', 27199, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No, Sergeant.', '', 27198, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mr. Perelli, if you happen across any signs of Scourge activity or shady dealings in your travels, let the nearest Lordaeron soldier know.', '', 27197, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The walls of Frostmourne Cavern shudder and shake.', 'The walls of Frostmourne Cavern shudder and shake.', 27196, 0, 7238, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You wouldn\'t happen to have any canned turtle soup from Hillsbrad, would you?', '', 27195, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mr. Perelli, have these goods been under your supervision at all times?', '', 27194, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you plan on leaving the area soon if we have further questions?', '', 27193, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mr. Perelli, I know you travel around quite a bit hawking your goods. Surely you\'ve heard rumors or information about the Scourge?', '', 27192, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mr. Perelli, have you seen any signs of the undead? Any information you can provide would be appreciated by Prince Arthas.', '', 27191, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mr. Perelli, have you seen any suspicious activity by men wearing dark robes in the last few weeks?', '', 27190, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I left a war once to tend to the troubles back home in Westfall. That seems like a lifetime ago. Thank the Light that the Defias are no longer a threat.$B$BWe\'re a long way from home up here, but if we don\'t win this battle, there may not be a Westfall to return to.', '', 27189, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I think he likes Old Blanchy.', '', 27188, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I know just the soldier for that horse!', '', 27187, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m gonna train that one myself.', '', 27186, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Keep bringin\' ones like that!', '', 27185, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s a mighty fine mustang ya got there.', '', 27184, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wow, that\'s a nice one!', '', 27183, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now, be free and join the battle! Let us end this together!', '', 27182, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have saved Wintergarde! With Thel\'zan\'s filth washed away, the 7th Legion will easily clean up the remaining Scourge. When you are done here, report to Angrathar!', '', 27181, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Victory for the Alliance!', '', 27180, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lord Fordragon!', 'Lord Fordragon!', 27179, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s the Highlord!', 'It\'s the Highlord!', 27178, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good to see you still alive and kicking, $n. Don\'t think that I\'d forgetten what you did for me in Stormwind, oh so long ago.', '', 27177, 0, 7237, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('THIS WILL BE THE LAST TIME YOU UTTER THAT NAME, PALADIN! Breathe your dying breath!', '', 27176, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So how, then, did Father Inigo Montoy, bastion of virtue for the Argent Dawn, become the embodiment of that which he hated most?', '', 27175, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You dedicated your whole life to fighting the Scourge. You saw what they did to our beloved Lordaeron. The Lich King took everything from you!', '', 27174, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Honor, courage, compassion and justice! These were once the virtues you fought for as a cleric of the Argent Dawn, Thel\'zan.', '', 27173, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Time to make another Patchy.', '', 27172, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s sighs in irritation.', '', 27171, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There you are, you little miscreant.', '', 27170, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Patchy?', '', 27169, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Where did that cat go?', '', 27168, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Careful with it. It\'s unstable and loses its potency quickly. Use it soon! And... preferably within eyesight, yes...', '', 27167, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 396, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All right, I\'ll take this mixture of yours.', 'All right, I\'ll take this mixture of yours.', 27166, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blight, Blight, Blight... that\'s all I hear about around here. I miss the diversity!$b$bHere, here. You have pets, yes? Of course you do. Of course. Little pets. I have a mixture for them. It will make them ca-- ah, clever and strong creatures, yes. Yes. Strong.$b$bTry it!', '', 27165, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 396, 5, 397, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rise, my minions! Your master commands it!', '', 27164, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Just as our lord saved me, so too shall I save you!\n', '', 27163, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But enough talk... You have fought hard and come from the distant reaches of this world to face the Duskbringer. I shall not disappoint...\n', '', 27162, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So serve him I did... Were it not for me the glorious dread citadel of Naxxramas may never have returned to Northrend.', '', 27161, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('\"Serve me in life and I will promise to rend the weakness from your soul. To erase it from existence!\" To be chosen... blessed by the Lich King in such a way.', '', 27160, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Our lord, Arthas, saw in me the frailty of man.', '', 27159, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('LEGION, STEADY YOURSELVES!', '', 27158, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I was... once like you. Mortal. Soft. Only flesh and bone. WEAK AND TIMID!', '', 27157, 0, 7236, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is this phylactery - Thel\'zan\'s phylactery - that is the key to victory!', '', 27156, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Steel yourselves, soldiers. $n has provided us with the final piece of this puzzle. The dread lich, Thel\'zan, will soon come out of hiding, only to be rendered powerless against us!', '', 27155, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '$n, good to see you!$B$BOr is this the first time that we\'ve met?$B$BI\'m in so many places and times right now, I sometimes have a hard time keeping track of all of it.', 27154, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have saved me from those vicious monsters. Thank you.', '', 27153, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s casts Frost Tomb on $n.', '', 27152, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Death comes for us all eventually, but sometimes it comes a little faster than anticipated. Today we call that blind heroics... Tomorrow someone may call it stupidity. \n', 'Death comes for us all eventually, but sometimes it comes a little faster than anticipated. Today we call that blind heroics... Tomorrow someone may call it stupidity. \n', 27150, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Come on... Let\'s get this over with!\n', 'Come on... Let\'s get this over with!\n', 27149, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let it be known that it has been an honor and a privilege fighting alongside all of you.\n', 'Let it be known that it has been an honor and a privilege fighting alongside all of you.\n', 27148, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m getting a little worried. Where is this hero that is supposed to lead us into battle?', 'I\'m getting a little worried. Where is this hero that is supposed to lead us into battle?', 27147, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is this the end? If we stop this monster now, is victory assured at the Wrathgate?', 'Is this the end? If we stop this monster now, is victory assured at the Wrathgate?', 27146, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If I don\'t make it back to Wintergarde, let my family know that I did my best and that I love them...', 'If I don\'t make it back to Wintergarde, let my family know that I did my best and that I love them...', 27145, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It looks like a gateway to hell!', 'It looks like a gateway to hell!', 27144, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What is it?', 'What is it?', 27143, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey, $n!  I hope you\'ve been enjoying our club!', 'Hey, $n!  I hope you\'ve been enjoying our club!', 27141, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey, $n, how\'s life been treating you?  Are you here to hang out with other club members?', 'Hey, $n, how\'s life been treating you?  Are you here to hang out with other club members?', 27140, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good seein\' you again, $n.  I hope our club be treatin\' ya right.', 'Good seein\' you again, $n.  I hope our club be treatin\' ya right.', 27139, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How things be treatin\' ya, $n?  Here to hang out with other members of da club?', 'How things be treatin\' ya, $n?  Here to hang out with other members of da club?', 27138, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wyrmbait, eh? Welp, go fetch us Icestorm!', 'Wyrmbait, eh? Welp, go fetch us Icestorm!', 27137, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get out there before I clock you. Clock. Get it?', '', 27136, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Top of the hour, boys. Go.', '', 27135, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'re on, rats.', '', 27134, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you want to jump to your death this time, I won\'t stop you.', '', 27133, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do your job, scum.', '', 27132, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get out there.', '', 27131, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey, I see ya got some Brewfest tokens.  If ya want, I still got a few Brewfest goods to sell.', 'Hey, I see ya got some Brewfest tokens.  If ya want, I still got a few Brewfest goods to sell.', 27130, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bat gizzards again for the gnomes tonight...', '', 27129, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wonder how many reinforcements need to suffer injury before they allow us to chop down these idiotic trees. They\'re costing us a fortune in bats. Maybe I\'ll rig a harness or two...', '', 27128, 33, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What do they expect, making the bats come in at that angle? Broken necks and gamey bat stew, that\'s what they get.', '', 27127, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('\'We like the trees, Fenrick. They provide cover.\' They won\'t let me chop them down, either.', '', 27126, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thel\'zan\'s phylactery drops to the ground beneath Icestorm.', '', 27125, 0, 7233, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Welcome to Granite Springs, friend.$b$bIf you manage to catch any of these ice trolls alive, be sure to let me know. We\'re paying well for \'em.', '', 27124, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('FIRE! FIRE! BRING HER DOWN!', '', 27123, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Awaiting orders!', '', 27122, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 66, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ticket Exchange', 'Ticket Exchange', 27121, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll flush her out, $n! You just be ready for her when she comes in!', 'I\'ll flush her out, $n! You just be ready for her when she comes in!', 27120, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Darling, those shoes are to die for!  I mean that literally.  Who did you kill for them?', 27119, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Darling, you simply can\'t complete your look without the right shoes.  Don\'t you agree?', 'Darling, you simply can\'t complete your look without the right shoes.  Don\'t you agree?', 27118, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A crack begins to open beneath your feet.', '', 27117, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s good to see you again, $n.$B$BCome for a refresher in Scourge tactics?', '', 27116, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, $c, what is it?', '', 27115, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, $c, what can I do for you?$B$BIf you\'re here for a lesson on Naxxramas, there\'s plenty of room.', '', 27114, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<The commander stops his lesson and turns, his eyes appraising you, sizing you up.>$B$BI have use for one such as yourself, $c.', '', 27113, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 1000, 0, 0, 39653),
('No, please!  Don\'t!', '', 27112, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Now don\'t move if you ever want to walk again!', 27111, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You... half-idiot!  You really did it this time.  I\'m going to have to make it look like your leg\'s broken.', 27110, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'What were you thinking, provoking her like that?', 27109, 0, 7217, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Let me take care of it, sister.', 27108, 0, 7217, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Alliance has maintained this remote lodge for a while.  It\'s seen some use by our hunters and woodsmen.$B$BWith the war going on, you\'d better believe the military is in charge here now, though.', '', 27107, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be sure to go through the southern canyon when entering and exiting the shrine, $n. You will know the canyons where the battle is waged by the abominations that guard them... keep your distance.', '', 27106, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do not stray too far down the pass, $n. Stay with the captain and his men... you\'re no use to us dead.', '', 27105, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In years past, the warlock Nekros Skullcrusher abused a powerful artifact to enslave Alexstrasza and much of the red dragonflight.  Zuluhed and Nekros are dead, but the debt we owe to the reds is far from repaid.', '', 27104, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I don\'t think we can afford to pass an opportunity to ingratiate ourselves with the red flight. With the battles ahead, having them as allies would be invaluable.', 27103, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Infinites are attempting something unusually subtle for them. They are trying to hide the evidence that will lead to Arthas deciding to cull Stratholme.$B$BTheir agents have used illusionary magic on the plagued grain shipments in the nearby countryside to make them appear normal.$B$BI need you to find the hidden grain, and use this Arcane Disruptor on the shipments. Arthas\' men are looking for plagued grain, and should find it quickly with the illusion gone.', 27102, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, he\'d better keep the moonshine flowing if he wants my men to stop their research to serve the military\'s purposes!', '', 27101, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He wants me to do WHAT?', '', 27100, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Show me what you have for sale, trapper.', 'Show me what you have for sale, trapper.', 27099, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s a good thing you came along, ally! We were done for!', 'It\'s a good thing you came along, ally! We were done for!', 27098, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I was almost ghoul bait! Thanks for the rescue!', 'I was almost ghoul bait! Thanks for the rescue!', 27097, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wow, I thought I was a goner! Thanks, friend!', 'Wow, I thought I was a goner! Thanks, friend!', 27096, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thanks for the cover fire! It\'s a MADHOUSE down there! ', 'Thanks for the cover fire! It\'s a MADHOUSE down there! ', 27095, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So how does the Infinite Dragonflight plan to interfere?', 'So how does the Infinite Dragonflight plan to interfere?', 27094, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Arthas gave the order to cull Stratholme, killing every single human within its walls.$B$BHe discovered evidence that the Scourge had infected the city with their insidious plague, and the disease doesn\'t just kill people.$B$BThose who die to this plague rise up as mindless zombies, further fueling the Scourge\'s war machine.', 27093, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What was this decision?', 'What was this decision?', 27092, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Infinite Dragonflight is attempting to alter the destiny of Prince Arthas Menethil.$B$BYou know him now as the Lich King, but here and now he was still a Prince of Lordaeron trying to do what was best for his kingdom.$B$BArthas makes a very fateful choice today, leading to something we Keepers of Time call an inflection point in the timeline.', 27091, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why have I been sent back to this particular place and time?', 'Why have I been sent back to this particular place and time?', 27090, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rifleman, cease fire! Our soldier is within range! GET HIM OUT OF THERE!', 'Rifleman, cease fire! Our soldier is within range! GET HIM OUT OF THERE!', 27089, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rifleman he\'s close enough now to rescue! GO GET HIM!', 'Rifleman he\'s close enough now to rescue! GO GET HIM!', 27088, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rifleman, get our soldier out of there! NOW NOW NOW!', 'Rifleman, get our soldier out of there! NOW NOW NOW!', 27087, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Pssst. Naohain. Why does Modoru still wear those ridiculous robes? He looks like some interdimensional bumpkin who stumbled out of Ammen Vale not six hours past.', 27086, 2, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '%s peers at Modoru\'s Draenic robes.', 27085, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Soldier, run to me! I\'ll clear a path with the chain gun!', 'Soldier, run to me! I\'ll clear a path with the chain gun!', 27084, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Come out, soldier! I\'ll cover you!', 'Come out, soldier! I\'ll cover you!', 27083, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In the Plaguelands, Kel\'thuzad was again defeated by the agents of the Argent Dawn. However, his phylactery was delivered to a false agent of the Brotherhood. We have yet to discover who stole his phylactery or why. ', '', 27082, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Kel\'thuzad has survived trials that would have long since shattered the souls of even the greatest of the Brotherhood. He readily gave his life at Arthas\'s hand, later to be brought back - reborn in the power of the Sunwell. ', '', 27081, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The lich, Kel\'Thuzad. He serves the Lich King without question, a necromancer of great prowess in life, turned into a master of necromancy after his death. It is said he is the most loyal of the Lich King\'s subjects.', '', 27080, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sapphiron. Once a noble blue dragon within the mountains of Northrend, Sapphiron was slain by Arthas during his campaign through the frozen north. Resurrected to serve him, Sapphiron guards Kel\'thuzad\'s lair eternally, awaiting those who would dare tresspass upon his master.', '', 27079, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thaddius, built from the flesh of women and children, it is said that their souls are fused together - eternally bound within that foul prison of flesh. ', '', 27078, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gluth, the foul plague-dog of Naxxramas, was said to have an appetite so voracious that even the living were not enough to satisfy his hunger. Feugen was said to feed him an army of zombies daily, recycling the remains of undead too weak to use in combat.', '', 27077, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes?', '', 27076, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Grobbulus, the first of what was to be an army of flesh giants. It carried the plague slime of Naxxramas within its body, injecting the living ooze into the bodies of its foe. The recipient of this foul injection would usually flee to his allies, bringing them down with him.', '', 27075, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Behold, Patchwerk. When word of his existence first reached the ears of the Brotherhood, none believed the tales of an abomination with such immense speed and strength. Fewer still believed it when he fell the first time...', '', 27074, 0, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Maexxna, born deep within the mountains of Northrend many ages ago, she was captured within the dread citadel Naxxramas, where she gives birth to her brood, feeding them the corpses of all who dare venture too deeply into Naxxramas.', '', 27073, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Grekk holds them.$b$bMaybe he\'ll give you one if you help him out. The next time you\'re up north at Blue Sky logging Grounds be sure to talk to him.', '', 27072, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Where can I get a Refurbished Shredder Key?', 'Where can I get a Refurbished Shredder Key?', 27071, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Grand Widow Faerlina, a botanist in life, breeder and caretaker of arachnids in death, she overseers the spider wing, developing the most potent of poisons for the Lich King. ', '', 27070, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('At first we repaired them to harvest the forests here, but ever since the alliance arrived and the fighting broke out we\'ve been using them as war machines.$b$bBelieve me, $c. If you\'ve got a key, you\'d be crazy not to use it.', '', 27069, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why would I want to ride a shredder?', 'Why would I want to ride a shredder?', 27068, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Listen, $r.$b$bIf you\'re lookin\' for a shredder to ride, you\'ll need to head up into the hills just north there.$b$bThis one\'s out of commission.', '', 27067, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Anub\'Rekhan, one of the finest Spider Lords of Azjol\'Nerub, was brought under the control of the Scourge when he and his former commander, Anub\'arak, were finally defeated by Lich King many years ago. It is said that he was the most loyal of Anub\'arak\'s commanders.', '', 27066, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The final death knight, Lord Mograine, was the finest warrior that the death knights had ever seen. However, after the events in Azeroth, he vanished without a trace. It is yet to be seen who Kel\'Thuzad has appointed in his place.', '', 27065, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sir Zeliek, a paladin in life, so strong in his faith, that even in undeath, the power of the light still heeds his call, smiting his foes in battle.', '', 27064, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The next, Lady Blaumeux, calls forth the power of shadows, drawing the souls of the living into the voracious embrace.', '', 27063, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The most powerful death knights within Naxxramas are the four horsemen. They represent the pinnacle of Kel\'Thuzad\'s guard. The first, Thane Korth\'azz, holds the power of flame. ', '', 27062, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gothik, the Harvester. A master of necromancy and conjuration, Gothik is said to be able to beckon forth legions of the undead at a moment\'s notice. It is with his guidance that even the weakest of Death Knights can raise the dead.', '', 27061, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Pay attention. This is Instructor Razuvious, Kel\'Thuzad\'s appointed trainer of all death knights. It is said that his own technique is so potent, only a disciple of his could possibly withstand his might.', '', 27060, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I shall leave this image on display for your perusal. Study your opponents\' strengths, for a creature\'s strength can also be its weakness.', '', 27059, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Loatheb. The hideous result of fusing the living plague of the Plaguelands with the bog beasts of Azeroth, Loatheb is said to control the power of healing itself. ', '', 27058, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is said that Heigan has rigged the very walls and floors of Naxxramas itself with a vast array of traps, which he can trigger at will.', '', 27057, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Observe, Heigan the Unclean. The mastermind behind the plague cauldrons that turned the wilderness of Azeroth into the Plaguelands. ', '', 27056, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Behold, Noth the Plaguebringer. Responsible for the creation of the process that distills the souls of the living and places them within the cold cage of undeath, Noth was observed to be refining this process even now. ', '', 27055, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Next, I shall speak of the most powerful entities within the pinnacle of Naxxramas. Truly, these are two of the greatest threats to all of Northrend.', '', 27054, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Next, I shall speak of the death knight wing of Naxxramas. Within its corrupted halls, the echo of battle rings day and night, as our finest warriors are corrupted and twisted into the Scourge\'s greatest warriors.', '', 27053, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Next, I shall speak of the blighted abomination wing of Naxxramas. There, the Scourge develop the strongest and most hideous aberrations of their armies.', '', 27052, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Next, I shall speak of the accursed spider wing of Naxxramas. It is there the Scourge breed even more poisonous and dangerous versions of their kin.', '', 27051, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Next, I shall speak of the dread plague wing of Naxxramas, where the Scourge seek to improve upon the deadly blight which they spread across Lordaeron.', '', 27050, 7, 7259, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Does being in the presence of a Black Dragon make you nervous?$B$BGood. It should. It makes these dragons nervous too. They cling to their ancient virtues though - they wouldn\'t dare attack me here.$B$BFools.', 27049, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can you spare a drake to take me to Lord Devrestrasz in the middle of the temple?', 'Can you spare a drake to take me to Lord Devrestrasz in the middle of the temple?', 27048, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Official postings by Wintergarde citizenry and officials.', '', 27047, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can I get a ride back to ground level, Lord Devrestrasz?', 'Can I get a ride back to ground level, Lord Devrestrasz?', 27046, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thel\'zan needs to die, if only to stop the incessant yammering!', '', 27045, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Welcome, adventurer. You\'ve come just in the nick of time.', 27044, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My lord, I need to get to the top of the temple.', 'My lord, I need to get to the top of the temple.', 27043, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would like to go to Lord Devrestrasz in the middle of the temple.', 'I would like to go to Lord Devrestrasz in the middle of the temple.', 27042, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to exchange my Emerald Essence for Ruby Essence.', 'I want to exchange my Emerald Essence for Ruby Essence.', 27041, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to exchange my Amber Essence for Ruby Essence.', 'I want to exchange my Amber Essence for Ruby Essence.', 27040, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to exchange my Ruby Essence for Amber Essence.', 'I want to exchange my Ruby Essence for Amber Essence.', 27039, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to exchange my Emerald Essence for Amber Essence.', 'I want to exchange my Emerald Essence for Amber Essence.', 27038, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Listen here, now. When you\'re looking for answers nothing beats a good explosion - the bigger, the better!$b$bBut that\'s probably enough with the questions for now, $r.$b$bMy warheads are classified material, and the element 115 that I created to power them is even more classified!$b$bIn fact, it\'s best that you just return to your everyday life and pretend we never met.', '', 27037, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rocket propelled warheads? Isn\'t that a bit aggressive?', 'Rocket propelled warheads? Isn\'t that a bit aggressive?', 27036, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to exchange my Amber Essence for Emerald Essence.', 'I want to exchange my Amber Essence for Emerald Essence.', 27035, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to exchange my Ruby Essence for Emerald Essence.', 'I want to exchange my Ruby Essence for Emerald Essence.', 27034, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Why... why sister?  Why did it have to come to this?', 27033, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ladies and gentlemen!  Well... let\'s just say you don\'t want to miss this one!', '', 27032, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Enough talk.  By the time I\'m through with you, not even the worgs are going to want to go near your corpse.', 27031, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You went behind my back.  You neglected my orders.  You will pay the price.', 27030, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Good one, sister.  What about your pet?  Where is $n?', 27029, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'We\'ll see about that.', 27028, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I used good judgment when you showed none.  I don\'t want to see you lead us into ruin, Krenna!', 27027, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It doesn\'t have to end this way, you know?', 27026, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I see you\'ve brought your pets.', 27025, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Here for a ride, $r?$B$BOr, is something else bothering you?', 27024, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Forgive me, but I am spent and cannot use my magic to send you back Theramore. You have the look of a worldly adventurer about you; surely you know of another way to reach Theramore in time.', '', 27023, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Explosion brought to you by Smokywood Pastures!', '', 27022, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Come back next year for a new surprise!', '', 27021, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Straight out of Thor Modan and made of 100 percent authentic... metal... here is Rustblood, the lightning-powered iron golem!', '', 27020, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Gather round, folks!  Grab a warm drink and find a good seat for you\'re about to witness a showdown between $r and machine!', '', 27019, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Just when you think you\'ve seen it all!  $n will square off with an authentic Grizzly Hills crazed furbolg in front of your very eyes here at the Conquest Pit!  Place your bets, folks!', '', 27018, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ladies and gentlemen, gather round the Conquest Pit!  Witness the battle of $r versus bear and place your bets with confidence!', '', 27017, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In the other corner, a serial killer, mass defenestrator, sentenced to death multiple times by noose and by blunt instrument!  Horgrenn... Hellcleave!  Ladies and gentlemen... place your bets!', '', 27016, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In one corner we have... $n, truly a world class $c.  Slayer of reptiles, mammals, mechanical constructs and the odd dragon...kin.  You\'ve never seen another $r like $g him : her;.', '', 27015, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ladies and gentlemen... gather round the pit!', '', 27014, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hrm. It appears to be functioning normally again...', '', 27013, 35, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('If I ever catch whoever keeps damaging this holo-emitter...', '', 27012, 35, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Every time I fix this mailbox, it\'s vandalized again within a day.', '', 27011, 35, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Who keeps breaking this thing?!', '', 27010, 35, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'d like to exchange the tickets in my inventory for the new tokens.', 'I\'d like to exchange the tickets in my inventory for the new tokens.', 27009, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Brewfest has undergone some changes since its first year. We now issue Brewfest tokens instead of tickets. If you have old tickets, I can exchange them for you.', 'Brewfest has undergone some changes since its first year. We now issue Brewfest tokens instead of tickets. If you have old tickets, I can exchange them for you.', 27008, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You need to learn to appreciate your surroundings, Cersei!', '', 27007, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Sinu a\'manore. If you seek to learn how to conjure a portal to Theramore, I can show you.', 27006, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'My teachings are only of use to mages. I cannot help you, $c.', 27005, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'d give my pestle away for some earplugs.', '', 27004, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m not sure which one\'s crazier.', '', 27003, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shut up.', '', 27002, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Remember how quiet it was before the elves came here? I miss that.', '', 27001, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be quiet.', '', 27000, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hrm? Oh. Pardon me if I seem distracted; I fear for the men of Northwatch. I should have sent some of my students to aid them...', 'Hrm? Oh. Pardon me if I seem distracted; I fear for the men of Northwatch. I should have sent some of my students to aid them...', 26999, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hrm? Oh. Pardon me if I seem distracted; I fear for the men of Northwatch. I should have sent some of my students to aid them. Now, how may I help you?', 'Hrm? Oh. Pardon me if I seem distracted; I fear for the men of Northwatch. I should have sent some of my students to aid them. Now, how may I help you?', 26998, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('To this day, I ponder why I, myself, was chosen for this particular station. I can only imagine my superior felt I was uniquely suited to the task and would quickly become accustomed to the quaint culture of the Horde found herein, but I heard a truly mean-spirited rumor that it may be because I talk too much.', '', 26997, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Before I was stationed out here, I\'d only heard about the rejuvenating effects a mudbath can have on skin. When I first tripped over a tree root, I was exposed to the full benefits! Amazing what nature can do, even without a bit of magic to help it along.', '', 26996, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Here I am, in a rough-hewn stone tower squatting on marshy, muddy ground while clouds of midges fly unchecked through the open doorways, standing amongst hunched, greenskin figures of dubious hygiene and coarse manners. I\'ve never been happier.', '', 26995, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is a shame, a dreadful shame, that my brethren cannot see what benefits come from truly steeping oneself in a culture.', '', 26994, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('While visitors complain about the exceptionally humid air, I find it helps my complexion! Dry skin is unflattering.', '', 26993, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, I love the smell of Stonard! It smells like... like... orc sweat. And rot. Still, combined, the effect can be quite pleasant! It\'s an acquired scent.', '', 26992, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Most of my brethren are disdainful of the Horde\'s \"barbaric\" ways, and I once counted myself among them. When I was first ordered to this somewhat humid and... fragrant place, I cursed my lot in life.$b$bDuring my studies, however, I grew to appreciate my surroundings. It has a certain charm, don\'t you think?$b$b...you wouldn\'t be interested in my studies, of course, not being a mage yourself.', '', 26991, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Most of my brethren are disdainful of the Horde\'s \"barbaric\" ways, and I once counted myself among them. When I was first ordered to this somewhat humid and... fragrant place, I cursed my lot in life.$b$bDuring my studies, however, I grew to appreciate my surroundings. It has a certain charm, don\'t you think?$b$bAh, and my studies, of course, were to allow other mages to return here with a spell. Shall I teach you?', '', 26990, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Happy Winter\'s Veil!', '', 26989, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why !', '', 26988, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please!  Stop the burning!', '', 26987, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It burns!', '', 26986, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I hope I\'m alive to see Arthas get what\'s coming to him.', 'I hope I\'m alive to see Arthas get what\'s coming to him.', 26985, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Where are all the corpses? What have they done to our people?', 'Where are all the corpses? What have they done to our people?', 26984, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look at this mess... The Scourge will pay for this!', 'Look at this mess... The Scourge will pay for this!', 26983, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So does anyone know anything about Thel\'zan? Who is he? How did he come to leading the Scourge armies on the ground?', 'So does anyone know anything about Thel\'zan? Who is he? How did he come to leading the Scourge armies on the ground?', 26982, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Driver, I hear you single handedly airlifted our villagers out of this hell-hole. Is that true?', 'Driver, I hear you single handedly airlifted our villagers out of this hell-hole. Is that true?', 26981, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The smell of death covers every inch of this place.', 'The smell of death covers every inch of this place.', 26980, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Keep the chatter down, people. We need to stay alert!', 'Keep the chatter down, people. We need to stay alert!', 26979, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve never seen destruction like this...', 'I\'ve never seen destruction like this...', 26978, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I used to know a dwarf that claimed gnomes evolved from beneath the earth. That we all started out as sand gnomes. What a load of nonsense! Sand gnomes? PUH-LEASE!', 'I used to know a dwarf that claimed gnomes evolved from beneath the earth. That we all started out as sand gnomes. What a load of nonsense! Sand gnomes? PUH-LEASE!', 26977, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Something straight up stinks in here! It\'s definitely not me. Gnomes smell like butter and sunshine. Not like those dwarves that smell like they were born from a trogg\'s armpit! None of you are dwarves, are you?', 'Something straight up stinks in here! It\'s definitely not me. Gnomes smell like butter and sunshine. Not like those dwarves that smell like they were born from a trogg\'s armpit! None of you are dwarves, are you?', 26976, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey, do any of you know McGoyver over at Valgarde? He\'s my uncle. You know what his title is? Pro. Yea, just \"Pro.\" I want to be a pro too.', 'Hey, do any of you know McGoyver over at Valgarde? He\'s my uncle. You know what his title is? Pro. Yea, just \"Pro.\" I want to be a pro too.', 26975, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wonder if we\'ll ever solve the mystery of the strange ore. There\'s gotta be some use for it!', 'I wonder if we\'ll ever solve the mystery of the strange ore. There\'s gotta be some use for it!', 26974, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It doesn\'t make any sense. Why don\'t they just fly Naxxramas over Wintergarde Keep and blow it up? I mean, that\'s what I would do if I were Kel\'Thuzad.', 'It doesn\'t make any sense. Why don\'t they just fly Naxxramas over Wintergarde Keep and blow it up? I mean, that\'s what I would do if I were Kel\'Thuzad.', 26973, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Did I ever tell you soldiers about the time I destroyed the Thandol Span? Yep, weren\'t no dark irons destroyed that bridge! Was me!', 'Did I ever tell you soldiers about the time I destroyed the Thandol Span? Yep, weren\'t no dark irons destroyed that bridge! Was me!', 26972, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I think I see one of their plague wagons!', 'I think I see one of their plague wagons!', 26971, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In all of my centuries, I never dreamed that it would come to this.', '', 26970, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have my leave.', '', 26969, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes. Do your best to return in one piece.', '', 26968, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is regrettable, but necessary.', '', 26967, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thank you, my friend. Go.', '', 26966, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Defend the temple at all costs.', '', 26965, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do what must be done.', '', 26964, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What have we come to?', '', 26963, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is unconscionable that Malygos would have his forces attack the temple! With your permission, my lord, I will defend us with my life.', 'It is unconscionable that Malygos would have his forces attack the temple! With your permission, my lord, I will defend us with my life.', 26962, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve heard that the azure dragonshrine is being invested with the direct power of a ley line. I will defend the temple as best I can.', 'I\'ve heard that the azure dragonshrine is being invested with the direct power of a ley line. I will defend the temple as best I can.', 26961, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Their dragonshrine may have empowered them, but the blues will not wrest the temple from us this day!', 'Their dragonshrine may have empowered them, but the blues will not wrest the temple from us this day!', 26960, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('By your leave, I will do what I can.', 'By your leave, I will do what I can.', 26959, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If the blues dare to attack the temple, then they have a deathwish.', 'If the blues dare to attack the temple, then they have a deathwish.', 26958, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For the queen. For Wyrmrest Temple!', 'For the queen. For Wyrmrest Temple!', 26957, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lord Devrestrasz, with your leave, I wish to defend the temple.', 'Lord Devrestrasz, with your leave, I wish to defend the temple.', 26956, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My lord, I am ready to go.', 'My lord, I am ready to go.', 26955, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Reporting for duty, sir!', 'Reporting for duty, sir!', 26954, 7, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to fly on the wings of the bronze flight.', 'I want to fly on the wings of the bronze flight.', 26953, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Belgaristrasz speaks the truth; time is running out!\n\nI can grant you the power to call upon a drake from the bronze flight.  Speak to Belgaristrasz or Verdisa if you prefer to draw on the power of the red or the green.', '', 26952, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to fly on the wings of the red flight.', 'I want to fly on the wings of the red flight.', 26951, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Varos Cloudstrider and his ring guardians protect the second ring.  Your drakes are more than a match for the ring guardians, but Varos stands behind an impenetrable shield created from the energy of the Oculus itself.  Ten centrifuge constructs power the shield from the ring and platforms above.  Destroy them and Varos will be vulnerable.\n\nI can grant you the power to call upon a drake from the red flight.  Speak to Eternos or Verdisa if you prefer to draw on the power of the bronze or the green.', '', 26950, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Belgaristrasz speaks the truth; the situation is grave indeed.  \n\nI can grant you the power to call upon a drake from the green flight.  Speak to Belgaristrasz or Eternos if you prefer to draw on the power of the red or the bronze.', 26949, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to fly on the wings of the green flight.', 'I want to fly on the wings of the green flight.', 26948, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('S.T.O.U.T. is more than just a target for throwing steins, it\'s a valuable training asset.  If you can hit S.T.O.U.T. you can probably hit anything!$b$bJust try not to hit me.', '', 26947, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'d like to use the stables.', 'I\'d like to use the stables.', 26946, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Welcome to Camp Oneqwah.', '', 26945, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Remnant of Dahlia Suntouch fades away...', 26944, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Dahlia spits on the ground at the thought of the name.', 26943, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'And thank you... thank you for freeing me from the shackles of the damned.  You are a hero... I know you will go on to great deeds.', 26942, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'My time is done... I offered myself to Alexstrasza in life, but I have nothing left to offer in death.  She will need a new keeper for her shrine.', 26941, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Lich King is stretching his hand far now... fearlessly treading on the most sacred lands of all of the flights.  He intends to force us to action.', 26940, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'ve lived here and kept this shrine with the blessing of the Alexstrasza for longer than I can remember.  In its darkest hour, I\'ve failed... I fell at the feet of that damned death knight...  Bloodbane.', 26939, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m sorry, $r, but I just called to a defender for you.$B$BYou will have to wait a short time before I will do so again.', 'I\'m sorry, $r, but I just called to a defender for you.$B$BYou will have to wait a short time before I will do so again.', 26938, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thank you for freeing us, mortals.  Beware, the blue flight is alerted to your presence.  Even now, Malygos sends Varos Cloudstrider and his ring guardians to defend the Oculus.  You will need our help to stand a chance.', '', 26937, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Greetings, $r.$B$BIf you are interested in helping with the defense of the temple, please speak with Lord Devrestrasz  inside.', 'Greetings, $r.$B$BIf you are interested in helping with the defense of the temple, please speak with Lord Devrestrasz  inside.', 26936, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'d like to use the stables.', 'I\'d like to use the stables.', 26935, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hello. Squire Walter and I are responsible for taking care of Old Blanchy here, along with the rest of the mounts.', '', 26934, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bolster my defenses! Hurry, curse you!', '', 26933, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
