('Intruders have breached the factory!  Engage emergency defense protocol immediately!', 'Intruders have breached the factory!  Engage emergency defense protocol immediately!', 17366, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ezekiel said that you might have a certain book...', 'Ezekiel said that you might have a certain book...', 17365, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Beat it, kid. I got business to attend to...', '', 17364, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s falls unconscious.', '', 17363, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Unbelievable!  Anyone else want to attack?', '', 17362, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alright, we give up! Don\'t hurt us!', '', 17361, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh, come on!  First the mana wraith and now revenge from a stalker?!  No, you\'re not getting your mojo back!', '', 17360, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Can you believe this ethereal technology?!$B$BI\'m sure glad they let me stay out here with them.  I\'m gonna learn a lot... and maybe get some of it for myself, too!', 17359, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 11, 0, 0, 500, 0, 39653),
('%s cracks his knuckles.', '', 17358, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Time to meet your maker!', '', 17357, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('2...', '', 17356, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('1...', '', 17355, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now I\'m gonna give you to the count of \'3\' to get out of here before I sick the dogs on you.', '', 17354, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Time to teach you a lesson in manners, little $g boy:girl;!', '', 17353, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you become a friend of the Lower City, perhaps we can do business?', '', 17352, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Welcome, friend of the free people of the Lower City, but do not tarry long.$B$BThere are sounds of battle coming from within.  My compatriots could use your assistance!', '', 17351, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Help!  A mana wraith!  It\'s come to avenge its brethren and steal back their essences!', '', 17350, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Did you think me weak? Soft? Who is the weak one now?', '', 17349, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not again! Not again...', '', 17348, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Legion will consume you all!', '', 17347, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I... am... unleashed!', '', 17346, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('When Rocket-Chief Fuselage was asking for volunteers to help out with building the X-52 Nether-Rocket, I submitted my resume for the security division.$B$BUnfortunately, the only position that was left was chief engineer.  Lucky for me, I have Xyrol here to look over my shoulder.', '', 17345, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My blood will be the end of you!', '', 17344, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How long do you believe your pathetic sorcery can hold me?', '', 17343, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Away, you mindless parasites! My blood is my own!', '', 17342, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Illidan is an arrogant fool! I will crush him and reclaim Outland as my own!', '', 17341, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Vermin! Leeches! Take my blood and choke on it!', '', 17340, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wretched, meddling insects! Release me, and perhaps I will grant you a merciful death!', '', 17339, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s becomes unstable and begins to disintegrate!', '%s becomes unstable and begins to disintegrate!', 17338, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lambs! Lemmings! All of them!', '', 17337, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will not be taken so easily! Let the walls of this prison tremble... and fall!', '', 17336, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Psst, hey, $n.  Up here on the platform.  Hurry!', '', 17335, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'ll have to prove yourself to us before you\'re welcome here, $n.', 'You\'ll have to prove yourself to us before you\'re welcome here, $n.', 17334, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It would be to your benefit for you to stay away from our holy grounds, $n.', 'It would be to your benefit for you to stay away from our holy grounds, $n.', 17333, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would not venture further if I were you, $n.  You are not permitted above.', 'I would not venture further if I were you, $n.  You are not permitted above.', 17332, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('May the Light guide you, $n.', 'May the Light guide you, $n.', 17331, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Aldor welcome you, $n.', 'The Aldor welcome you, $n.', 17330, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is good to see you again, $n.', 'It is good to see you again, $n.', 17329, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s rummages through the bones.', '', 17328, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why? WHY! Why was I \"gifted\" such a burden?', '', 17327, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The dead are not supposed to speak. Now be silent!', '', 17326, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I broke a covenant? I BROKE A COVENANT? What about that fool exarch and his avatar?', '', 17325, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No, spirit, I am afraid that they are all trapped inside - FOREVER! Now leave me be...', '', 17324, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll show them... I\'ll show them all!', '', 17323, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Throw me out of the priory, will they?', '', 17322, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be silent! Damn you, spirits!', '', 17321, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Mommy won\'t let anyone harm you, sweetheart.', 17320, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Mommy is going to make sure you\'re ok, baby.', 17319, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'In the end, we will all be together, sweetheart.', 17318, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I know it will be ok, baby.', 17317, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Oh sweetheart, grandpoppy has passed. It will be ok.', 17316, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '%s wipes the tears away.', 17315, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mommy, Greatfather told me that he will watch over us and make sure we\'re ok.', '', 17314, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t cry, Mommy. Greatfather says not to worry.', '', 17313, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mommy, Greatfather says everything will be ok.', '', 17312, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s tugs on Clarissa\'s robe.', '', 17311, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will, Greatfather.', '', 17310, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ok!', '', 17309, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You promise?', '', 17308, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll tell her, Greatfather.', '', 17307, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s laughs.', '', 17306, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s smiles.', '', 17305, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s nods.', '', 17304, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s giggles.', '', 17303, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Please, father, I do not have your strength. I cannot do this on my own. Please help me...', 17302, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Give me a sign... anything...', 17301, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Father, give me strength to go on.', 17300, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I wouldn\'t venture into the Scryer\'s Terrace if I were you, $n.  You are not welcome there.', 'I wouldn\'t venture into the Scryer\'s Terrace if I were you, $n.  You are not welcome there.', 17299, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Welcome back, $n.', 'Welcome back, $n.', 17298, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Please leave me to my sadness.', 17297, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Keep it down!  I don\'t want them to see me over here.$B$BOoh, this really burns me up!  Who do these ethereals think they are?$B$BThis is MY claim!', '', 17296, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The night Kael\'thas leveled the village, I could do nothing to help. His magic had already sealed me in the tower, exacerbating my torment by forcing me to witness the deaths of my fellows.$B$BAnd still their voices are calling from far away, waking me up in the middle of the night. ', '', 17295, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Archmage Vargoth favors you with a wry smile.>$B$BPlenty of room at the cursed Violet Tower.$B$BAny time of year, you can find me here.', '', 17294, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you\'ve been sent to kill me, please take a number and wait your turn.', '', 17293, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The orb behind me was once capable of glimpsing into the happenings on Azeroth.$B$BKael\'thas\'s curse changed all that, of course, but during our years of isolation many of the mages found solace in its images.$B$BSome scried to remember; some scried to forget. ', '', 17292, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will have my revenge on Kael\'thas for this outrage against the Kirin Tor! He once walked among us as a brother, but we are brothers no more.$B$BThere will be a reckoning.$B$B<The archmage nods grimly, not relishing the prospect.>$B$BKael\'thas is more than a mere rogue mage. Once I am free from my tower, Ravandwyr and I will assist anyone who opposes him.', '', 17291, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<The archmage\'s image seems to look through you, rather than at you.>$B$BRibbons and currents of arcane energy ebb and flow here as if the area is awash in a sea of magical power. Not even the first cataclysm caused this kind of damage.', '', 17290, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The land is in worse shape than I could\'ve imagined. If the damage continues at this rate, Farahlon -- err, Netherstorm will be nothing but cosmic gravel very soon.$B$BWhere will it stop, I wonder? Perhaps the better question is, \'will it stop?\'', '', 17289, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<The image\'s head blurs as it turns to take in its surroundings.>$B$BIf you had seen the Plains of Farahlon, you wouldn\'t believe this is the same place. Mere months ago, these fields would not have looked out of place in Westfall.$B$BAll that is gone now, but how and why?', '', 17288, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We\'re rather selective of who we befriend, $n.  You think you have what it takes?', 'We\'re rather selective of who we befriend, $n.  You think you have what it takes?', 17287, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Light be with you, $n.  And welcome to Shattrath.', 'Light be with you, $n.  And welcome to Shattrath.', 17286, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Are you joking?  I\'m a Scryer, I always watch what I say.  More enemies than allies in this city, it seems.', 17285, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be mindful of what you say, this one\'s being shown around by Khadgar\'s pet.', '', 17284, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Khadgar himself is showing you around?  You must have made a good impression, $n.', '', 17283, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'A newcomer to Shattrath!  Make sure to drop by later.  We can always use a hand with the injured.', 17282, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good luck stranger, and welcome to Shattrath City.', '', 17281, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Such is their animosity that they vie for the honor of being sent to assist the naaru there. Each day, that decision is made here by A\'dal.  The armies gather here to receive A\'dal\'s blessing before heading to Shadowmoon.', '', 17280, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There he continues to wage war on Illidan with the assistance of the Aldor and the Scryers.  The two factions have not given up on their old feuds, though.', '', 17279, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Aldor\'s most holy temple and its surrounding dwellings lie on the terrace above.  As a holy site, only the initiated are welcome inside.\n', '', 17278, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Many of the priesthood had been slain by the same magisters who now vowed to serve the naaru.  They were not happy to share the city with their former enemies.', '', 17277, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The naaru accepted the defectors, who would be known as the Scryers; their dwelling lies in the platform above.  Only those initiated with the Scryers are allowed there.', '', 17276, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('As the naaru approached him, Voren\'thal kneeled before him and uttered the following words: \"I\'ve seen you in a vision, naaru. My race\'s only hope for survival lies with you. My followers and I are here to serve you.\"', '', 17275, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('As the regiment of blood elves crossed this very bridge, the Aldor\'s exarchs and vindicators lined up to defend the Terrace of Light.  But then the unexpected happened.\n', '', 17274, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The priesthood, known as the Aldor, quickly regained its strength as word spread that the naaru had returned and reconstruction soon began.  The ruined temple is now used as an infirmary for injured refugees.', '', 17272, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They were drawn to the ruins of Shattrath City where a small remnant of the draenei priesthood conducted its rites inside a ruined temple on this very spot.\n', '', 17271, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let us go into the Lower City.  I will warn you that as one of the only safe havens in Outland, Shattrath has attracted droves of refugees from all wars, current and past.', '', 17270, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The city was left in ruins and darkness... until the Sha\'tar arrived.', '', 17269, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('When the Burning Legion turned the orcs against the draenei, the fiercest battle was fought here. The draenei fought tooth and nail, but in the end the city fell.', '', 17268, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Show our guest around Shattrath, will you?  Keep an eye out for pickpockets in the Lower City.', '', 17266, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thanks and good luck!', '', 17265, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He was right, you know. I\'ll have to take that tag-line for my own... It\'s not like he\'ll have a use for it anymore!', '', 17264, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh really? And what might that be?', '', 17263, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Khadgar should be ready to see you again.  Just remember that to serve the Sha\'tar you will most likely have to ally with the Aldor or the Scryers. And seeking the favor of one group will cause the others\' dislike.\n', '', 17262, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ok break time is OVER. Let\'s go!', '', 17261, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Are you ready to go?', '', 17260, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We\'re close to the exit. I\'ll let you rest for about thirty seconds, but then we\'re out of here.', '', 17258, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The attacks against Shattrath continued, but the city did not fall, as you can see. On the contrary, the naaru known as Xi\'ri led a successful incursion into Shadowmoon Valley - Illidan\'s doorstep.', '', 17257, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What do we have here? I thought you said the area was secure? This is now the third attack? If we make it out of here, I will definitely be deducting this from your reward. Now don\'t just stand there, destroy them so I can get to that collector.', '', 17256, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There can\'t be too many more of these collectors. Just keep me safe as I do my job.', '', 17255, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, there it is. Follow me, fleshling.', '', 17254, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Aldor are followers of the Light and forgiveness and redemption are values they understand. However, they found hard to forget the deeds of the blood elves while under Kael\'s command.', '', 17253, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hrm, now where is the next collector?', '', 17252, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That should do it...', '', 17251, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The defection of Voren\'thal and his followers was the largest loss ever incurred by Kael\'s forces. And these weren\'t just any blood elves.  Many of the best and brightest amongst Kael\'s scholars and magisters had been swayed by Voren\'thal\'s influence.\n', '', 17250, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Looking at these energy levels, Shaffar was set to make a killing!', '', 17249, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fantastic! Let\'s move on, shall we?', '', 17248, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The blood elves laid down their weapons in front of the city\'s defenders; their leader, a blood elf elder known as Voren\'thal, stormed into the Terrace of Light and demanded to speak to A\'dal.', '', 17247, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This should\'t take very long. Just watch my back as I empty these nether collectors.', '', 17246, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It wouldn\'t be long, however, before the city came under attack once again.  This time, the attack came from Illidan\'s armies. A large regiment of blood elves had been sent by Illidan\'s ally, Kael\'thas Sunstrider, to lay waste to the city.', '', 17245, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Never underestimate the other ethereal\'s greed!', '', 17244, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Your plan was a good one, Sha\'heen, and you would have gotten away with it if not for one thing...', '', 17243, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Sha\'tar, or \"born from light\" are the naaru that came to Outland to fight the demons of the Burning Legion.', '', 17242, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bravo! Bravo! Good show... I couldn\'t convince you to work for me, could I? No, I suppose the needless slaughter of my employees might negatively impact your employment application.', '', 17241, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shattrath was once the draenei capital of this world. Its name means \"dwelling of light.\"', '', 17240, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Follow me, stranger.  This won\'t take long.', '', 17239, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do not burden A\'dal with mundane questions, $r.  This being\'s will is all that keeps our enemies from crushing this city.', '', 17238, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What manner of creature is that?  Looks like a purple goblin.', '', 17237, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look at those crazy kids running around.  Not a care in the world.', '', 17236, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The market sure looks busy today.', '', 17235, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '', 17234, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Push a random button.>', '<Push a random button.>', 17233, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The control panel shifts and rotates on its axis.', '', 17232, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let\'s not waste any time! Take anything that isn\'t nailed down to the floor and teleport directly to Stormspire! Chop chop!', '', 17231, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s expertly manipulates the control panel.', '', 17230, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You made it! Well done, $r. Now if you\'ll excuse me, I have to get the rest of our crew inside.', '', 17229, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s checks to make sure his body is intact.', '', 17228, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('At ease, men.', '', 17227, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m close to the edge, Morphalius. Another screw up and it\'ll be you running through that portal for Kaftiz\'s tests.', '', 17226, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t pay you engineers exorbitant amounts of gold so that I can hear the words \"no\" or \"can\'t\" exit your wrappings. Bring that barrier down or you\'ll find yourselves working the energy reclamation line on X-17.', '', 17225, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t give a damn what Shaffar\'s ethereals have placed over the entrance to the Mana-Tombs. You will work until those wards are removed and the Consortium can move in safely and take what\'s rightfully ours!', '', 17224, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That Shaffar is a clever one. He\'s rigged the entrance with some sort of ward to prevent other ethereal groups from entering. We\'re working on breaking through his defenses so we can get in there and take what\'s ours. I\'ve got top ethereals working on this around the clock. We\'ll have it open any minute now. I can feel it...', '', 17223, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Show me what you have for sale, \"Slim.\"', 'Show me what you have for sale, \"Slim.\"', 17222, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, I see you are a friend to the Consortium. Perhaps you would be interested in making a purchase?', '', 17221, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m neither slim nor shady. As a matter of fact, I find both references insulting.$B$BNow, get out of my sight before I plant my staff up your backside.', '', 17220, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What\'s an \"Ologist?\" A better question might be what isn\'t an \"Ologist.\" It means I study everything! In fact, I\'m so well versed in \"everything\" that I\'m guaranteed to be the most intelligent ethereal you\'ll ever meet - or your money back.$B$BApologies. That\'s the dealer in me talking...', '', 17219, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thankfully, there\'s a steady stream of these fools champing at the bit to get in here.', '', 17218, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nice going, you incompetent morons! Another one of our engineers vaporized!', '', 17217, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Damnit. How are we ever going to get through their security measures?', '', 17216, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I didn\'t like him much anyway. Too much talk, not enough \"do.\"', '', 17215, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh well, back to the drawing board.', '', 17214, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s shakes his head in disapproval.', '', 17213, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s shrugs.', '', 17212, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s runs his hands across his body to make sure everything is intact.', '', 17211, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alright, it looks safe. Get in there, engineer!', '', 17210, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I made it! I made it!', '', 17209, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If I make it through, I expect a pay raise.', '', 17208, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is gonna leave a mark...', '', 17207, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Here goes nothing!', '', 17206, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I don\'t get paid enough for this nonsense.', '', 17205, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can\'t believe you imbeciles went to school for this! Does anybody here know what they\'re doing?', '', 17204, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You know, we could easily replace you with goblins. Is that what you want???', '', 17203, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is it done yet? What is taking so damned long?', '', 17202, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Is that damned thing safe to go through yet?', '', 17201, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve had just about enough of your incessant whining, captain. What are you even a captain of? I mean, the nerve!', '', 17200, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why don\'t you pick up a hammer and start banging on these structures instead of asking us if it\'s done every 5 minutes?', '', 17199, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Will you stop asking that?', '', 17198, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can\'t bang on this device any faster, captain! My wrapping is already beginning to unravel!', '', 17197, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m giving her all that I\'ve got, captain. I don\'t think she can take much more of this!', '', 17196, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What does that mean anyway? Ready? Can it ever be ready?', '', 17195, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is if I\'m not the one that\'s going to be sent in to test it... Otherwise, no.', '', 17194, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Not really.', '', 17193, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bribe who you must, but I need some inside information this week if I\'m to make a profit and keep your lot employed.  Off with you!', '', 17192, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nothing surprising there.  Come back with some real news, will you?', '', 17191, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('As expected.  Very well, dismissed.', '', 17190, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Word from Netherstorm, sir.  Stop all bloodgem imports; client has reneged payments.$B$BThe nexus-prince will buy out our stock at full price as compensation.', '', 17189, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Xarodi sector markets have reopened, sir.  Sapphires of all sort are up.  Silver is down.  Gold is up.  Diamonds remain stable.$B$BOh, and your brother asks that you return the holocubes you borrowed last week.', '', 17188, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No word from the nexus-prince as of yet.  Rumors of a dispute with our clients in Netherstorm have begun to circulate.  Our Sodaraami backers speak of divesting.  We\'ve dispatched our top negotiators to dissuade them, sir.', '', 17187, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Heraazi exports are on the rise, sir.  We\'ve already bribed the appropriate taxation officers and contraband will begin to arrive within days.', '', 17186, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('By your leave, sir.', '', 17185, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hail, Gezhe!  Seventeen more orders have been placed in the Hara\'samid Sector.  The markets of heavy veldarite have all but collapsed, as you predicted.', '', 17184, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What is it that you want, $r?', '', 17183, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This thing kind of reminds me of a Zed Power Nodule I once took half of Papa Wheeler\'s old garage out with.', '', 17182, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('...victory.', '...victory.', 17181, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It smells like...', 'It smells like...', 17180, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I love the smell of nether in the morning.', 'I love the smell of nether in the morning.', 17179, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hmm...Frost, Fire, and Arcane defenses respond faster than Batch 7, but Nature defenses remain passive.', 'Hmm...Frost, Fire, and Arcane defenses respond faster than Batch 7, but Nature defenses remain passive.', 17178, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I have returned, Greatmother. Garrosh has found his heart and his fury.', '', 17175, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It is for them, or rather for what they represent, that we fight.$B$BOutside these walls, these people\'s lives are forfeit.  The world as they know it... as we all know it, is threatened by Kael\'thas, Illidan and the Burning Legion.$B$BWithin these walls you will find the few that are willing to fight for that world.', '', 17174, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You need not thank me, Garrosh. Your father was a brother to me. I would do anything for you and the Mag\'har. I must now return to the Greatmother.', '', 17173, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s places a hand on Garrosh\'s shoulder.', '', 17172, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thank you, son of Durotan.', '', 17171, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('News spread quickly of Shattrath City\'s victories.  Refugees from all previous wars and from the one that had begun anew begun to pour into the city.$B$BThe entire lower third of the city is inhabited by them now.  No one who seeks respite from Illidan is turned away, so you might run into an unsavory character or two there.  But for the most part, they\'re just ordinary people who had lost all hope and have now been given a new lease on life.', '', 17170, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am Garrosh Hellscream, son of Grom, chieftain of the Mag\'har! Let the battle call of Hellscream give you courage and strength! Be lifted by my rallying cry.', '', 17169, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('On this day, a great burden has been lifted from my chest. My heart swells with pride. And for the first time, I can proudly proclaim who I am. I can finally unleash the fury in my heart.', '', 17168, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You have shown me truths that I would have never known. You and your allies have gifted me with something that cannot bear a price: Redemption. Thrall, redeemer of the Mag\'har, you honor me as none ever have...', '', 17167, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I hated him for what he had done. I hated him for the burden he left me. But now...', '', 17166, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shattrath did not fall, as you can see.  To the contrary, the naaru known as Xi\'ri, led a successful incursion into Shadowmoon Valley - Illidan\'s doorstep.$B$BThere he continues to wage war on Illidan\'s armies with the assitance of the Aldor and the Scryers.$B$BThe two factions have not given up on their old feuds, however. Such is their animosity that they vie for the honor of being the ones sent to assist the naaru there.  Each day, that decision is made by A\'dal right here in Shattrath.', '', 17165, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For my entire life I have thought my bloodline cursed. I have lived beneath the shadow of my father\'s greatest failure.', '', 17164, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s collapses.', '', 17163, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fierce retaliation for the defections were to follow.  Shattrath City came under unrelenting attack from Illidan and Kael\'thas.$B$BArmies of blood elves, naga and Broken, would pour into the city; only to be repelled by the might of the Sha\'tar.$B$BOne thing became clear to the naaru.  If they were to pursue the Legion, they would have to defeat Illidan first.', '', 17162, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Khadgar grins to himself>$B$BI convinced A\'dal and his brethren to return here with me. I believe that only their power can drive the Legion from this universe. But as you will no doubt find - their power must first live in our hearts.$B$BTo combat the darkness, we must become beacons of their eternal Light.', '', 17161, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('While my comrades held the line against the encroaching darkness, I used my magic to reach out into the Great Dark Beyond.  There, I sensed beings of immense Light - of unfathomable purity.$B$BIt was A\'dal and his naaru I had found. It was nothing short of a... miracle.', '', 17160, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Trapped in this broken wasteland, we did our best to survive. Over time we sensed that a new evil was closing in around us from the Twisting Nether.  More foul than the dark orcs - it was the Burning Legion itself that sought to take hold of this... Outland.', '', 17159, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My comrades and I called ourselves the Sons of Lothar - in honor of the greatest, most selfless man we ever knew.  We gave our all to defeat Ner\'zhul and end his madness.$B$BAs this doomed world fell apart around us, we shattered the Dark Portal to prevent any further harm befalling our beloved Azeroth.', '', 17158, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I fought alongside Lord Anduin Lothar as we drove the Horde from our lands on Azeroth. As the heir of Medivh\'s legacy, I could do no less.$B$BWhen the call finally came to invade this grim world - and put an end to the orcs\' evil forever - I stepped forward along with my friends Turalyon, Alleria, Danath and Kurdran.', '', 17157, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I see.', 'I see.', 17156, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am Khadgar, former apprentice to the fallen Guardian, Medivh. I\'m sure you\'ve heard his name before.$B$BIt was I who discovered that Medivh had been possessed by the Evil One, Sargeras - and that he had opened the Dark Portal between this world and Azeroth. Though I honored my Master, I was forced to slay him and put his tortured soul to rest.', '', 17155, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve heard your name spoken only in whispers, mage.  Who are you?', 'I\'ve heard your name spoken only in whispers, mage.  Who are you?', 17154, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No, old friend. You\'ve freed us all...', '', 17153, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The demon\'s fire has burnt out in my veins. I have... freed myself.\n', '', 17152, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('Grom\'s eyes go dim as the blood curse is lifted.', '', 17151, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Thrall... The blood haze has lifted.', '', 17150, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ack, disintegrated!  I guess I had the power setting too high?  And it almost hit the Wheeler Mobile!  Yikes, don\'t tell him!', '', 17149, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fall in men! It\'s time to drill!', '', 17148, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Long Tube Gadget Analyzer should tell me what I need to know.', '', 17147, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alright, let\'s see what makes this tech tick!', '', 17146, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Soup\'s on, men! Eat up. We\'ve got a long day ahead.', '', 17145, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('NOOOO!', '', 17144, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s breaks free of the blood elf\'s control!', '', 17143, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The boy believed you could be saved, but he didn\'t know what burns within your soul when in your heart, you know we are the same.\n', '', 17142, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A worthy effort, but futile.', '', 17141, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s roars in defiance.', '', 17140, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('His blood is mine, as is your whole misbegotten race.', '', 17139, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So predictable. I knew you would come. And I see you\'ve brought the mighty Hellscream.', '', 17138, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s laughs.', '', 17137, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Spirits give me strength! Take from my soul these old wounds and expose them for all to see! Let this child know his father! Let these people know their savior!', '', 17136, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('As you wish, Thrall, son of Durotan.', '', 17135, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Garrosh, son of Hellscream, your father lived and died as our greatest hero. Honor me by allowing me to show you what your father sacrificed so that we could live free of the demon\'s grasp.', '', 17134, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please excuse me, Greatmother. I will return soon.', '', 17133, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell him? Greatmother, that boy\'s father died so that all of us could live free of the blood curse. I will tell him nothing. I will show him! Show him and any that would doubt Hellscream\'s resolve exactly what Grom Hellscream did for all orcs!', '', 17132, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Grandson, will you... Will you tell Garrosh what you have told me about his father?', 17131, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shredders?!  They just won\'t cut it anymore.  They\'re so yesterday!$B$BIf we\'re going to build rockets - if we\'re going to get the X-52 off the ground - we need better tech!', '', 17130, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Blessed spirits! For twenty years, all we knew was that Grom was the first to drink from the cursed chalice and bring damnation down upon our people... It is the only truth his son, Garrosh has ever known.\n', 17129, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('He died our greatest hero. It was Grom who freed us all... I was by his side when he struck down Mannoroth and ended the curse forever.', '', 17128, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('But surely you heard, Greatmother.', '', 17127, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Thrall? You\'ve been a slave only to the past, grandson! But no more! When last I saw him, Durotan told me the name he would give his unborn son... He was... so proud...', 17126, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I never knew my father or mother. Orgrim told me many stories about them and their adventures on Draenor. He was my greatest teacher and dearest friend, Greatmother. He died a hero... They all died as heroes and for all of them, a song of honor remains.', '', 17125, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They died honorably, Greatmother.', '', 17124, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'There is no doubt - you are the heir of Durotan... my grandson. Draka told me she was with child before she and your father left our world, but I never dared dream that they would survive...\n', 17123, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('They... did not, Greatmother. They were killed shortly after I was born. I never knew them. I was raised as a slave. To this day, I carry the name of Thrall.\n', '', 17122, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Are they...', 17121, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Yes, you move like my son. You have his broad shoulders - ahh, and your mother\'s fierce eyes.\n', 17120, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good thing that we\'re surrounded by neighbors with excess machine parts.', 'Good thing that we\'re surrounded by neighbors with excess machine parts.', 17119, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey!  Come over here and take a look at this wanted poster.  You\'re not going to believe this!', 'Hey!  Come over here and take a look at this wanted poster.  You\'re not going to believe this!', 17118, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We can\'t let a failing servo slow down the construction of the X-52 Nether-Rocket!', 'We can\'t let a failing servo slow down the construction of the X-52 Nether-Rocket!', 17117, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hmm, arcane annihilators are pretty tough.  I wonder if Papa Wheeler knows what he\'s asking for?', 'Hmm, arcane annihilators are pretty tough.  I wonder if Papa Wheeler knows what he\'s asking for?', 17116, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Maybe I should gather up some other agents and head out there after this shift?', 'Maybe I should gather up some other agents and head out there after this shift?', 17115, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I can\'t believe that Papa Wheeler thinks he\'s going to dupe anyone into going out to Manaforge B\'naar!', 'I can\'t believe that Papa Wheeler thinks he\'s going to dupe anyone into going out to Manaforge B\'naar!', 17114, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
