('The battle for Warsong Gulch begins in 1 minute.', '', 10015, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let the battle begin!', '', 10014, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Finally, I am free! I come home soon, my dear!', '', 10013, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get the key and unlock these chains! Hitah\'ya the Keeper holds it... back of cave... ', '', 10012, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Vaelastrasz, no!!!', 'Vaelastrasz, no!!!', 10011, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I perform one final service. I pray it is sufficient...', '', 10010, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 26, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Invaders! Invaders! We\'re under attack, boys! Get \'em!', '', 10009, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You brought supplies from the enemy!  Hah! Well done $n!', '', 10008, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Supplies from our enemies!  Well done, $n!', '', 10007, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s is weakened by the orb!', '', 10006, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The High Priestess will feast on your bones!', 'The High Priestess will feast on your bones!', 10005, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dinner has arrived!', 'Dinner has arrived!', 10004, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Another fool falls for the trap!', 'Another fool falls for the trap!', 10003, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For the Horde!', 'For the Horde!', 10002, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Reporting for duty!', 'Reporting for duty!', 10001, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s good to see an engineer brave enough to make the device.   We goblin engineers laugh at danger!', '', 10000, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 11, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you figure out any way to improve the device let me know!', '', 9999, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Once you have built the device, you simply activate the device to be whisked away to lovely Gadgetzan!    Nearly everyone who has used the device has arrived on the pad here looking just the way they did when they began!\n\nThere have been some reported problems with transportees being replaced by their evil selves from an alternate universe, but I\'m sure we will have that worked out soon...', '', 9998, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I must build a beacon for this marvelous device!', 'I must build a beacon for this marvelous device!', 9997, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('With some of the technology that was recovered by bold gnomes venturing into Gnomeregan, I have managed to construct my greatest invention:  The Matter Transporter!    All I need now is a skilled Gnomish Engineer to build a powerful beacon attuned to the transporter.', '', 9996, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The theory behind it is that we completely destroy you with a massive explosion wherever you are and send those particles through a dimensional rip and then re-implode you at the machine here.   Instant Transport!    It might not work ALL the time, but what kind of goblin engineer are you!   If survival was your first priority you could never be a real Goblin Engineer!\nHere is the recipe you will need to make the Dimensional Ripper and try it out!\n\n', '', 9995, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This Dimensional Imploder sounds dangerous!  How can I make one?', 'This Dimensional Imploder sounds dangerous!  How can I make one?', 9994, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I have just completed a new dimensional imploder that will make me rich beyond my wildest goblin dreams!   All I need to do is get a skilled Goblin Engineer to build a dimensional ripper that connects to it and try it! \n', '', 9993, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I would like to buy from you.', 'I would like to buy from you.', 9992, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please teach me how to become a swordsmith, Seril.', 'Please teach me how to become a swordsmith, Seril.', 9991, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you wish to become a swordsmith, just ask.', '', 9990, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Back off or I\'ll cut you in half.', '', 9989, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please teach me how to become a hammersmith, Lilith.', 'Please teach me how to become a hammersmith, Lilith.', 9988, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I will teach you the way of the hammersmith. Just ask nicely.', 9987, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Don\'t get too close, $n. I\'m liable to fumble and bash your brains open with the face of my hammer.', 9986, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please teach me how to become an axesmith, Kilram.', 'Please teach me how to become an axesmith, Kilram.', 9985, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, a seasoned veteran you once were. Kilram can make you this again. I know you are capable, you merely need to ask and I shall teach you the way of the axesmith.', '', 9984, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am Kilram, master of the axe.', '', 9983, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Markhor, I wish to stable my pet.', 'Markhor, I wish to stable my pet.', 9982, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Zul\'jin shall return one day, $r. Mark my words. Until then, we all hold our positions and do what we can to keep the forest troll population intact.$B$BWith that said, as master huntsman of Revantusk Village, it is my responsibility to ensure that the world around us is safe for habitation.$B$BThe beasts of this area must be kept in check.$B$BAre you looking for work?\n', '', 9981, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What can you teach me?', 'What can you teach me?', 9980, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fishing is just so pleasant, mon. You know? I owe my state of bliss to my mentor, the greatest angler in the whole world - Nat Pagle. Have you heard of him, mon?$B$BIf you be looking for enlightenment, Nat Pagle be the one who gonna show you the way. ', '', 9979, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Don\'t be steppin\' on my goods, there.', 9978, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If it\'s broke, Slagtree can fix it!', '', 9977, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Welcome to Revantusk Village, stranger. I am Primal Torntusk, leader of the Revantusk trolls.', 9976, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ve got all the cooking supplies you\'ll ever need, mon!', '', 9975, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('BURN! You wretches! BURN!', '', 9974, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well done, my minions. The mortals\' courage begins to wane! Now, let\'s see how they contend with the true Lord of Blackrock Spire!!!', '', 9973, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Worthless $n!  Your friends will join you soon enough!', '', 9972, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This cannot be!  I am the master here!  You mortals are nothing to my kind!  Do you hear me? Nothing!', '', 9971, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The blood samples must be protected!  Destroy the intruders!', '', 9969, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Clever, mortals - but I am not so easily lured away from my sanctum!', '', 9968, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('None of your kind should be here!  You\'ve doomed only yourselves!', '', 9967, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Protect the flight!  These intruders die now!', '', 9966, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Nefarius\' hate has made me stronger than ever before! You should have fled while you could, mortals! The fury of Blackrock courses through my veins! \n', '', 9965, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Forgive me, $n! Your death only adds to my failure! ', '', 9964, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('No - not another one! I\'ll have your heads for this atrocity!', '', 9963, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fools! These eggs are more precious than you know!', '', 9962, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You\'ll pay for forcing me to do this!', '', 9961, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Foolish $n, you serve me now! ', '', 9960, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t fight in broken weapons and armor! Expert armor and weapon repairing done here - while you wait!', '', 9959, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Intruders have breached the hatchery! Sound the alarm! Protect the eggs at all costs!\n', '', 9958, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s shot a buff!', '', 9956, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free. \n', 'The Stockades are a high-security prison complex, hidden beneath the canal district of Stormwind city. Presided over by Warden Thelwater, the Stockades are home to petty crooks, political insurgents, murderers and a score of the most dangerous criminals in the land. Recently, a prisoner-led revolt has resulted in a state of pandemonium within the Stockades - where the guards have been driven out and the convicts roam free. \n', 9955, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.', 'The Stormwind Stockades are found near the mage quarter in Stormwind.', 9954, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stormwind Stockade', 'Stormwind Stockade', 9953, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Deadmines can be found beneath Moonbrook in the south of Westfall.', 'The Deadmines can be found beneath Moonbrook in the south of Westfall.', 9952, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Deadmines', 'Deadmines', 9951, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Once the jewel of northern Lordaeron, the city of Stratholme is where Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther Lightbringer, and slaughtered hundreds of his own subjects who were believed to have contracted the plague of undeath. Arthas\' surrender to the Lich King soon followed. The broken city is now inhabited by the undead Scourge - led by the powerful lich, Kel\'Thuzad, and a contingent of Scarlet Crusaders, led by Grand Crusader Dathrohan. The two sides are locked in constant, violent combat. \n', 'Once the jewel of northern Lordaeron, the city of Stratholme is where Prince Arthas turned against his mentor, Uther Lightbringer, and slaughtered hundreds of his own subjects who were believed to have contracted the plague of undeath. Arthas\' surrender to the Lich King soon followed. The broken city is now inhabited by the undead Scourge - led by the powerful lich, Kel\'Thuzad, and a contingent of Scarlet Crusaders, led by Grand Crusader Dathrohan. The two sides are locked in constant, violent combat. \n', 9950, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The ruined city of Stratholme lies in the Eastern Plaguelands to the north of the Plaguewood.', 'The ruined city of Stratholme lies in the Eastern Plaguelands to the north of the Plaguewood.', 9949, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Stratholme', 'Stratholme', 9948, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel\'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel\'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ', 'The Scholomance is housed in crypts beneath the Caer Darrow keep. Once owned by the noble Barov family, the keep fell to ruin after the Second War. As the wizard Kel\'Thuzad enlisted followers for his Cult of the Damned, he often promised immortality for those who served his Lich King. The Barovs fell to his influence and donated their keep, but the cultists killed the family and turned the crypts into a school of necromancy. Though Kel\'Thuzad no longer resides there, cultists and instructors still remain. ', 9947, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The School for Necromancy known as Scholomance is on the ruined island of Caer Darrow in the Western Plaguelands.', 'The School for Necromancy known as Scholomance is on the ruined island of Caer Darrow in the Western Plaguelands.', 9946, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Scholomance', 'Scholomance', 9945, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre\'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara\'s most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins\' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres. \n', 'Built twelve thousand years ago by a covert sect of night elf sorcerers, the ancient city of Eldre\'Thalas was used to protect Queen Azshara\'s most prized arcane secrets. Though it was ravaged by the Great Sundering of the world, much of the wondrous city still stands as the imposing Dire Maul. The ruins\' three distinct districts have been overrun by all manner of creatures - especially the spectral highborne, foul satyr and brutish ogres. \n', 9944, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.', 'The ruins of Dire Maul stand in central Ferelas.', 9943, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dire Maul', 'Dire Maul', 9942, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves\' holdings in the mountain\'s volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself. \n', 'The mighty fortress carved within the fiery bowels of Blackrock Mountain was held by the sinister Dark Iron dwarves for centuries until Nefarian - the cunning son of the dragon, Deathwing - took control of the upper Spire and made war on the dwarves\' holdings in the mountain\'s volcanic depths. Realizing that the dwarves were led by the mighty fire elemental, Ragnaros - Nefarian vowed to crush his enemies and claim the whole of Blackrock mountain for himself. \n', 9941, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blackrock Spire', 'Blackrock Spire', 9940, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.  \n', 'Once the capital city of the Dark Iron dwarves, this volcanic labyrinth now serves as the seat of power for Ragnaros the Firelord. Ragnaros has uncovered the secret to creating life from stone and plans to build an army of unstoppable golems to aid him in conquering the whole of Blackrock Mountain. Obsessed with defeating Nefarian and his draconic minions, Ragnaros will go to any extreme to achieve final victory.  \n', 9939, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.', 'Blackrock Mountain lies between Searing Gorge in the north and Burning Steppes in the south.', 9938, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Blackrock Depths', 'Blackrock Depths', 9937, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal\'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal\'ai\'s plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple\'s ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons.\n', 'Over a thousand years ago a group of troll priests known as the Atal\'ai attempted to bring back an ancient blood god named Hakkar the Soulflayer. After the resulting civil war the priests were defeated and exiled to the Swamp of Sorrows. There they erected a temple to Hakkar to prepare for his arrival into the physical world. The dragon Aspect Ysera soon learned of the Atal\'ai\'s plans and smashed the temple beneath the marshes. To this day, the temple\'s ruins are guarded by the mighty green dragons.\n', 9936, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.', 'The Sunken Temple can be found in the center of a great lake in eastern Swamp of Sorrows.', 9935, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sunken Temple', 'Sunken Temple', 9934, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar\'s spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ', 'Maraudon is one of the most sacred sites within Desolace. The great temple/cavern is the burial place of Zaetar, one of two immortal sons born to the demigod, Cenarius. Legend holds that Zaetar and the earth elemental princess, Theradras, sired the misbegotten centaur race. It is said that upon their emergence, the barbaric centaur turned on their father and killed him. Some believe that Theradras, in her grief, trapped Zaetar\'s spirit within the winding cavern - used its energies for some malign purpose. ', 9933, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.', 'Maraudon is located in the middle of the western coast of Desolace, in the Valley of Spears.', 9932, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Maraudon', 'Maraudon', 9931, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul\'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul\'Farrak\'s walls.\n', 'This sun-blasted city is home to the Sandfury trolls, known for their particular ruthlessness and dark mysticism. Troll legends tell of a powerful sword called Sul\'thraze the Lasher, a weapon capable of instilling fear and weakness in even the most formidable of foes. Long ago, the weapon was split in half. However, rumors have circulated that the two halves may be found somewhere within Zul\'Farrak\'s walls.\n', 9930, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The ruins of Zul\'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.', 'The ruins of Zul\'Farrak are located in the northwestern corner of the Tanaris Desert.', 9929, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Zul\'Farrak', 'Zul\'Farrak', 9928, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Uldaman is an ancient Titan vault that has laid buried within the earth since the world\'s creation. Dwarven excavations of the city have recently released the Titans\' first failed creations: the troggs. Legends say that when the Titans deemed the trogg experiment a failure they tried again, resulting in the creation of the dwarven race. These secrets are recorded on the fabled Discs of Norgannon - massive artifacts that lie at the bottom of the ancient city, protected by giant constructs of living stone. 
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('Join a group going to this dungeon.    <This choice will place you in a meetingstone queue>                              ', 'Join a group going to this dungeon.    <This choice will place you in a meetingstone queue>    \n', 9873, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let your spirits rise! Rally around your champion, bask in $g his:her; glory! Revel in the rallying cry of the dragon slayer!', 'Let your spirits rise! Rally around your champion, bask in $g his:her; glory! Revel in the rallying cry of the dragon slayer!', 9872, 0, 0, 22, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs\' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm\'s fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade\'s existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council. \n', 'Ragefire Chasm consists of a network of volcanic caverns below the orcs\' new capital city of Orgrimmar. Recently, rumors have spread that a cult loyal to the demonic Shadow Council has taken up residence within the Chasm\'s fiery depths. This cult, known as the Burning Blade, threatens the very sovereignty of Durotar. Many believe that the orc Warchief Thrall is aware of the Blade\'s existence and has chosen not to destroy it in the hopes that its members might lead him straight to the Shadow Council. \n', 9871, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Citizens of the Alliance, the Lord of Blackrock is slain! Nefarian has been subdued by the combined might of $n and $g his:her; allies!', 'Citizens of the Alliance, the Lord of Blackrock is slain! Nefarian has been subdued by the combined might of $n and $g his:her; allies!', 9870, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Look to this fallen dragon, $r. The might of the Horde is unquestionable!', '', 9869, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be lifted by $n\'s accomplishment! Revel in $g his:her; rallying cry!', '', 9868, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('NEFARIAN BE SLAIN! People of Orgrimmar, bow down before da might of $n and $g his:her; allies for dey have laid a mighty blow against da Black Dragonflight !', '', 9867, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m going to stay here until I catch a 68 Pound Grouper!  You on the other hand want to fly off somewhere, am I right?', '', 9866, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What can I do for you $c?', '', 9865, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You scared the fish away!  What do you want?', '', 9864, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Can\'t you see I\'m fishing here!', '', 9863, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am he that watches they. I am the fist of retribution. That which does quell the recalcitrant. Dare you defy the Warchief? Dare you face my merciless judgment?', '', 9862, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 15, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I... I have failed, $n. The Lord of Bla... The Lord of Blackrock is too powerful. He consumed my energy with... with ease. I turn... I... kill me... you must... you must kill me.', '', 9861, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('At last, the agony ends. I have failed you my Queen. I have failed us all...', '', 9860, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Place my hand on the orb.>', '<Place my hand on the orb.>', 9859, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The orb\'s markings match the brand on your hand.', '', 9858, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A large humanoid hand print is embedded on the surface of the orb. Despite what appears to be constant manipulation and handling, the orb remains unmarred.', '', 9857, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rogues? Stop hiding and face me!', '', 9856, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Warriors, I know you can hit harder than that! Let\'s see it!', '', 9855, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Shamans, show me what your totems can do!', '', 9854, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Paladins... I\'ve heard you have many lives. Show me.', '', 9853, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Warlocks, you shouldn\'t be playing with magic you don\'t understand. See what happens?', '', 9852, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Druids and your silly shapeshifting. Lets see it in action!', '', 9851, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mages too? You should be more careful when you play with magic...', '', 9850, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hunters and your annoying pea-shooters!', '', 9849, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Priests! If you\'re going to keep healing like that, we might as well make it a little more interesting!', '', 9848, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I cannot, Vaelastrasz! Surely something can be done to heal you!', 'I cannot, Vaelastrasz! Surely something can be done to heal you!', 9847, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you expect me to cower before the mighty legion of $n?$B$BYou are nothing to me. Less than nothing. Had I desired your head, it would have been presented to me on a pike.$B$BYou have made the mistake that all mortals make.$B$B<Lord Victor Nefarius sighs.>$B$BTime does strange things to those that use it as a form of currency.\n', '', 9846, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 273, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Let the games begin!', '', 9845, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Get up, little red wyrm...and destroy them!\n', '', 9844, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Alliance wins!', '', 9843, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Horde wins!', '', 9842, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'As long as those dwarves stay over there we\'ll have no trouble.  Where are you heading $n?', 9841, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make a Wild Leather Vest again?', 'Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make a Wild Leather Vest again?', 9840, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make Wild Leather Shoulders again?', 'Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make Wild Leather Shoulders again?', 9839, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make Wild Leather Leggings again?', 'Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make Wild Leather Leggings again?', 9838, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make a Wild Leather Helmet again?', 'Hey Jangdor - can you teach me how to make a Wild Leather Helmet again?', 9837, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
