('No one get past me and threaten da king!  Ungh, take it!!', '', 9418, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey, who Fengus callin\' a gnoll lover?!  Take da prisoners to da king; you smart to bring them with their weapons and show da king that they a threat.  I\'ll go see if Fengus talk smack when I give him da beatdown!  HAR!', '', 9416, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 5, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s goes into a drunken rage!', '', 9414, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s lets out a deep roar, alerting nearby allies and becoming enraged!', '', 9413, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Lorekeeper is an ancient. He has served under our glorious Queen!', 'The Lorekeeper is an ancient. He has served under our glorious Queen!', 9412, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yar, he\'s dead all right.  That makes you da new king... well, all of you!  Gordok is yours now, boss!  You should talk to me so you can learn everything there is about being da king!  I was... is his assistant!  Yeah, that\'s why I\'m called da crafty one!', '', 9411, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 4, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Many have come to this sanctuary, few have left. ', 'Many have come to this sanctuary, few have left. ', 9410, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Keep your voice down, stranger. You do not want to disrupt the Master\'s meditations.', 'Keep your voice down, stranger. You do not want to disrupt the Master\'s meditations.', 9409, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 20, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We mustn\'t anger the Master. His is a wrath that is cruel beyond measure.', 'We mustn\'t anger the Master. His is a wrath that is cruel beyond measure.', 9408, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 274, 0, 1, 2, 0, 39653),
('Who dares disrupt the sanctity of Eldre\'Thalas? Face me, cowards!', '', 9407, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('For 10,000 years I have ruled this kingdom. In that time, I have heard many fascinating tales from those that would walk the hallowed grounds of the House of Shen\'dralar.$B$BAs I am bound to this place, I often exchange stories with visitors. Do you have a story for me or perhaps you would like to hear a story?', '', 9406, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I suppose I can teach that to you.  You\'ll probably only be able to find ogre tannin here, but the other things you can find most anywhere!', '', 9405, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 273, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey Knot - I\'m a Tailor.  Think you could teach me how to make the ogre suit?', 'Hey Knot - I\'m a Tailor.  Think you could teach me how to make the ogre suit?', 9404, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hey Knot - I\'m a Leatherworker.  Think you could teach me how to make the ogre suit?', 'Hey Knot - I\'m a Leatherworker.  Think you could teach me how to make the ogre suit?', 9403, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I heard you was dead... well, you won\'t be easy to make dead after this!', '', 9402, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Call me \"Boss\".  What have you got for me!', 'Call me \"Boss\".  What have you got for me!', 9401, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You are da king of the Gordok!  You\'re A-number-one!', '', 9400, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I show you how smart I am, boss!  You be extra smart with mighty magic mojo now!$B$BUm... maybe Slip\'kik use magic on self. Dat would be good idea...', '', 9399, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yeah, you\'re a real brainiac.  Just how smart do you think you are, Slip\'kik?', 'Yeah, you\'re a real brainiac.  Just how smart do you think you are, Slip\'kik?', 9398, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You got me good boss!  How you get by Slip\'kik??  I smart though, I watch next time!  Har har!$B$BNobody get by Slip\'kik no more. Slip\'kik promise!', '', 9397, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fengus make you fierce!  Crazed!  RAR!', '', 9396, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am, am I?  Well what have you got for the new big dog of Gordok, Fengus?', 'I am, am I?  Well what have you got for the new big dog of Gordok, Fengus?', 9394, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You da man now, dog!', '', 9393, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A very sad tale. Thank you, spirit.', 'A very sad tale. Thank you, spirit.', 9392, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The people were destroyed in order to preserve the Prince\'s immortal life and near limitless powers. The power once divided among thousands now funnels into the Prince and the Shen\'dralar zealots. Those few remaining survivors are directly feeding power into the pylons in order to keep Immol\'thar imprisoned.$B$BShould the demon break free of its bonds, it would surely destroy what little is left of this once great bastion of arcana.', 9391, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('We live in a world of endless tragedy.', 'We live in a world of endless tragedy.', 9390, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Highborne ghosts that you see wandering through the courtyard and halls of Eldre\'Thalas were slain, not by invading Gordok ogres or satyrs, but by the Prince himself!', 9389, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m going to have to kill something, aren\'t I?', 'I\'m going to have to kill something, aren\'t I?', 9388, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The siphoned energies would sustain the Highborne\'s magic, allowing those within the walls of Eldre\'Thalas to feed their endless and growing magical pangs.$B$BThousands of years passed and the power required to keep Immol\'thar imprisoned while sustaining life within Eldre\'Thalas, began to shift. The cost to keep Immol\'thar bound grew to overshadow the rate at which energy could be siphoned and distributed. The once net gain turned to loss.', 9387, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fascinating. Continue, please.', 'Fascinating. Continue, please.', 9386, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Continue, please.', 'Continue, please.', 9385, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Prince plotted to imprison a demon of immense power behind a grand force field. The pylons would channel latent energies into the field, keeping it operational.$B$BWhile imprisoned, Immol\'thar would serve as a battery to the populace of Eldre\'Thalas.', 9384, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The Shen\'dralar were Queen Azshara\'s most revered arcanists. It was within these very walls that the Queen\'s most important demands were processed - often in secret.$B$BAfter the destruction of the Well and the subsequent lethargy that overcame the Highborne and lesser night elf sects, the Prince of Eldre\'Thalas, Tortheldrin, began construction of the pylons that you see littering the halls of the west wing.\n', 9383, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I know very little of the Highborne and nothing of the Shen\'dralar.', 'I know very little of the Highborne and nothing of the Shen\'dralar.', 9382, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Do you know of the Highborne? The Shen\'dralar?', 9381, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What happened here, spirit?', 'What happened here, spirit?', 9380, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Leave this place, stranger, lest it consume you as it has all that it has touched.', 9379, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Apply the Gordok war paint!', 'Apply the Gordok war paint!', 9378, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('OK boss, when you ready for da tribue from your henchmen, you let me know!', '', 9377, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s has grown to full size!', '', 9376, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s continues to grow!', '', 9375, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s begins to grow!', '', 9374, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What do you mean, buy?!  I\'m the king now... and it\'s good to be the king!', 'What do you mean, buy?!  I\'m the king now... and it\'s good to be the king!', 9373, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Show me what hooch you\'ve got to sell, Kreeg.', 'Show me what hooch you\'ve got to sell, Kreeg.', 9372, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You da boss now, yeah?  Long live da new king!$B$BKreeg let you look at Gordok hooch.  Ogre hooch best of all hooch, and Gordok hooch best of all ogre hooch!  Maybe you buy some from me, ya boss?!', '', 9371, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'THIS EVENT IS WORKING.', 9370, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, from what I\'ve gathered while waiting to be eaten by these yokels... it might not be necessary to kill every ogre you find here.$B$BThe ogres were going on and on the other day about how King Gordok came to power; specifically, he killed the previous king and took his place.  Well, the king\'s henchmen - those that Gordok spared - immediately swore fealty to the new king.$B$BWho knows - the ogre you save could very well be your own... figuratively speaking, of course!', '', 9369, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why should I bother fixing the trap?  Why not just eliminate the guard the old fashioned way?', 'Why should I bother fixing the trap?  Why not just eliminate the guard the old fashioned way?', 9368, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('Well then... show me the tribute!', 'Well then... show me the tribute!', 9367, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('All henchmen of da boss - Stomper Kreeg, all three of da Guards, Captain Kromcrush, and da Observer - give tribute to da new boss.  If you kill a henchman, then that henchman can\'t give tribute!  Each one you keep alive will give you more tribute.  Keep all of them alive and you get da BIG tribute!$B$BYeah!', '', 9366, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m the new king?  What are you talking about?', 'I\'m the new king?  What are you talking about?', 9365, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The demon is loose!  Quickly we must restrain him!', 'The demon is loose!  Quickly we must restrain him!', 9364, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Say hello to my little friends!', '', 9363, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Prepare to meet your maker.', 'Prepare to meet your maker.', 9362, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This is the end of the line, no friend of mine!', '', 9361, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('DIE?! You make Pusillin cry!', '', 9360, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('DIE!', 'DIE!', 9359, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Turn that frown upside down!', '', 9358, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why would you ever want to harm me!? Come. Friends we can be!', '', 9357, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Mark my words, I will catch you, imp. And when I do!', 'Mark my words, I will catch you, imp. And when I do!', 9356, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Why you little...', 'Why you little...', 9355, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Still alive? You do surprise. Watch me as I flee!', '', 9354, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Chase me if you dare! I run without a care!', '', 9353, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Game? Are you crazy?', 'Game? Are you crazy?', 9352, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I hold the key to lands of free! Chase me and you\'ll see!', '', 9351, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do you want to play a game, stinky?', '', 9350, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you want the key, you\'ll have to catch me!', '', 9349, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('OH NOES!  Da king is dead!  Uh... hail to da new king!  Yeah!', '', 9348, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You big boss now!  You king!  All hail King $n, King of Gordok!$B$BNow that you da boss, all henchmen will give you tribute!  You left some alive, yeah boss?', '', 9347, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('$n, I\'ll make sure all my friends in the Cartel know that you\'ve saved my life today.  Here - I\'m going to need to be able to travel light, so please help yourself to my cache of tailoring and leatherworking supplies!  Thanks again - see ya!', '', 9346, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You found a key?  Well, is it THE key?  I mean, is it the key to unlock these shackles?  Well $G sir : ma\'am;, there is only one way to find out!', '', 9345, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 21, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So, I found this shackle key...', 'So, I found this shackle key...', 9344, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me of Frostwolf Keep.', 'Tell me of Frostwolf Keep.', 9343, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me of Dun Baldar.', 'Tell me of Dun Baldar.', 9342, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Frostwolf Keep lies in the south corner of Alterac Valley and protects Frostwolf Village, home of orc clan of the same name.  All Horde territories in Alterac Valley stem from this one place of power.$B$BFrostwolf Keep was razed and is under reconstruction.', '', 9341, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Frostwolf Keep lies in the south corner of Alterac Valley and protects Frostwolf Village, home of orc clan of the same name.  All Horde territories in Alterac Valley stem from this one place of power.$B$BFrostwolf Keep is intact.', '', 9340, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dun Baldar is the strongest point of Alliance power in Alterac Valley.  Nestled in the northern reaches of the valley, Dun Baldar is the staging ground  for all advances to the south.$B$BDun Baldar was razed and is under reconstruction.', '', 9339, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dun Baldar is the strongest point of Alliance power in Alterac Valley.  Nestled in the northern reaches of the valley, Dun Baldar is the staging ground for all advances to the south.$B$BDun Baldar is intact.', '', 9338, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What little remained of Thunderaan\'s essence was stored within a talisman of elemental binding. Ragnaros then shattered the talisman in two flawless pieces. The pieces assigned to his Lieutenants...\n', '', 9337, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So what did Ragnaros do next?', 'So what did Ragnaros do next?', 9336, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Firelord\'s advances were wholly unknown to Thunderaan. Before my Lord could react, Sulfuras, legendary hammer of Ragnaros, would strike an unmerciful blow. Thunderaan fell, utterly defeated.$B$BThe Firelord feasted upon the essence of my Lord, but was unable to consume him entirely.', '', 9335, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Caught unaware? How?', 'Caught unaware? How?', 9334, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It was the Lieutenants of Ragnaros, Geddon and Garr, who would perpetrate the betrayal against my Lord. Thunderaan was caught unaware.', '', 9333, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Nod>.', '<Nod>.', 9332, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It was during the Elemental Sundering that the Firelord, Ragnaros, would seek to consume my Lord, Thunderaan, Prince of Air.$B$B<Demitrian bows his head, his face contorted in rage.>$B$BSpeak his name and I shall decorate this ravaged camp with your entrails. Be silent and listen.\n', '', 9331, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 273, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('A battle?', 'A battle?', 9330, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Vanndar Stormpike is the general of the Alliance military in Alterac, and directs his forces from Dun Baldar.$B$BIf he is defeated then the Alliance will surely lose the battle for Alterac.', '', 9329, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Vanndar Stormpike is the general of the Alliance military in Alterac, and directs his forces from Dun Baldar.$B$BIf he is defeated then the Alliance will surely lose the battle for Alterac.', '', 9328, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Galvangar is the trusted aid to Drek\'Thar.  He leads the Horde forces from the Iceblood Garrison, in the southern section of the the Field of Strife.$B$BCaptain Galvangar has been slain.', '', 9327, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Galvangar is the trusted aid to Drek\'Thar.  He leads the Horde forces from the Iceblood Garrison, in the southern section of the the Field of Strife.$B$BCaptain Galvangar is currently in the Iceblood Garrison.', '', 9326, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Drek\'Thar is the military and spiritual leader of the Frostwolf Clan in Alterac, leading his brethren from Frostwolf Keep.$B$BIf he is defeated then the Horde forces in Alterac will crumble.$B$BDrek\'Thar has been slain.', '', 9325, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Drek\'Thar is the military and spiritual leader of the Frostwolf Clan in Alterac, leading his brethren from Frostwolf Keep.$B$BIf he is defeated then the Horde forces in Alterac will crumble.', '', 9324, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Balinda Stonehearth leads the front line Alliance forces.  She is based in the Stonehearth Outpost, in the northern section of the Field of Strife.$B$BBalinda has been slain.', '', 9323, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Balinda Stonehearth leads the front line Alliance forces.  She is based in the Stonehearth Outpost, in the northern section of the Field of Strife.$B$BBalinda is currently in Stonehearth Outpost.', '', 9322, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me again about Alterac Valley...', 'Tell me again about Alterac Valley...', 9321, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me of Drek\'Thar.', 'Tell me of Drek\'Thar.', 9320, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me of Vanndar Stormpike.', 'Tell me of Vanndar Stormpike.', 9319, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me of Captain Galvangar.', 'Tell me of Captain Galvangar.', 9318, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me of Captain Balinda Stonehearth.', 'Tell me of Captain Balinda Stonehearth.', 9317, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Drek\'Thar is the military and spiritual leader of the Frostwolf Clan in Alterac, leading his brethren from Frostwolf Keep.$B$BIf he is defeated then the Horde forces in Alterac will crumble.$B$BDrek\'Thar is not currently in Alterac Valley.', '', 9316, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Vanndar Stormpike is the general of the Alliance military in Alterac, and directs his forces from Dun Baldar.$B$BIf he is defeated then the Alliance will surely lose the battle for Alterac.$B$BVanndar is not currently in Alterac Valley.', '', 9315, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Galvangar is the trusted aid to Drek\'Thar.  He leads the Horde forces from the Iceblood Garrison, in the southern section of the the Field of Strife.$B$BCaptain Galvangar has not yet entered the battle.', '', 9314, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Balinda Stonehearth leads the front line Alliance forces.  She is based in the Stonehearth Outpost, in the northern section of the Field of Strife.$B$BBalinda has not yet reentered the battle.', '', 9313, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Stormpikes uncovered ancient artifacts within Alterac Valley, but the Frostwolf orcs don\'t take kindly to explorers.  If the dwarves have to fight for knowledge of their ancestors, then so be it!$B$BTo win this battle, defeat the orc, Drek\'Thar, in Frostwolf Keep.  Fortune be with you, $c!', '', 9312, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alterac Valley has been home to the Frostwolf Clan for years; we will not let the dwarves and their Alliance trespass!  And so we battle!$B$BTo win back Alterac, defeat their general Vanndar Stormpike, in Dun Baldar.$B$BFor the Horde!', '', 9311, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Tell me about Alterac Valley.', 'Tell me about Alterac Valley.', 9310, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Galvangar has been slain!  Honor our fallen captain, and unleash yourself again the Alliance!', '', 9309, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Captain Balinda Stonehearth is dead!  Defeat Vanndar and the battle will be ours!', '', 9308, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The battle rages, and both our captain and the captain of our enemy are slain!$B$BDrek\'Thar now leads us from Frostwolf Keep, and the dwarf Vanndar Stormpike hides deep in Dun Baldar.  Defeat Vanndar and claim victory for the Horde!', '', 9307, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Stormpike general has fallen!  The battle is won!$B$BNow laugh as the Alliance scurries to recover its lost holdings.', '', 9306, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Both the Horde and Alliance captains have taken to the field.  Our Captain Galvangar directs the Frostwolves from Iceblood Garrison, and his rival, Captain Balinda Stonehearth, hides in her Stonehearth Outpost.$B$BThe battle has begun!', '', 9305, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('NO!!!  It puts the tannin in the basket, or it gets the mallet again!', '', 9304, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Both the Horde and Alliance captains have taken to the field.  Our Captain Balinda Stonehearth directs the Stormpike forces from the Stonehearth Outpost, and the enemy Captain Galvangar barks orders from within Iceblood Garrison.$B$BTo battle!', '', 9303, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Both the Horde and Alliance captains have fallen!  Defeat Drek\'Thar before it\'s too late!', '', 9302, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Their manifest forms weak from eons of battle, imprisoned beneath the world - the world that they themselves created - the corruption of the Titan Shapers would permeate through the surface and befoul the Old Gods.$B$BIt was then and there that the brothers did turn. For five millennia a battle was fought at the core of this world.\n', '', 9301, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Continue, please.', 'Continue, please.', 9300, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('In the time before time, what the usurpers would later call the First Age of Creation, my master and his siblings ruled over this world. It was they, the Old Gods, who created all.$B$BAnd it was they who would ultimately be cast down by those that would call themselves Shapers.\n', '', 9299, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am listening, Demitrian.', 'I am listening, Demitrian.', 9298, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I know much, listen and be educated, $r.', '', 9297, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
