('%s takes aim one last time...', '', 6109, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s takes aim again...', '', 6108, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s picks the orc target...', '', 6107, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s takes a more careful aim...', '', 6106, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hahah!  Revenge is mine!', '', 6105, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s cries.', '', 6104, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s snorts.', '', 6103, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s grumbles.', '', 6102, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s whimpers.', '', 6101, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good job you two.  Now go have a seat.', 'Good job you two.  Now go have a seat.', 6100, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now bow to me.', 'Now bow to me.', 6099, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Good, good.  Now bow to each other.', 'Good, good.  Now bow to each other.', 6098, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'None can stand against the Serpent Lords!', 6097, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am the serpent king! I can do anything! ', '', 6096, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The coils of death will crush you!', '', 6095, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You will never wake the dreamer!', '', 6094, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wanna buy a cockroach?', '', 6093, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('To Malyfous, I assume.', 'To Malyfous, I assume.', 6092, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ish nu!  That\'s enough!', 'Ish nu!  That\'s enough!', 6091, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So how about you deliver a message for me?', '', 6090, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'ll consider that the next time I run into one of these things.', 'I\'ll consider that the next time I run into one of these things.', 6089, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well, maybe \'pay\' isn\'t the best word to use. See, when I was stuck in the belly of that thing, I got to thinking:$B$BThis creature lives in hot, flaming magma and yet it doesn\'t take a lick of damage from the fire!$B$BIf only I could find a pristine hide from one of these beasts. I could take it back to my dear friend, Malyfous Darkhammer, in Everlook. If anyone could do anything with the hide of a beast like this, it would be him. \n', '', 6088, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Oh?', 'Oh?', 6087, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m not out of the belly of this beast for more than two minutes and someone is already asking me about my bathroom behavior??? $G Mister:Missy;, I\'d have smacked you silly for that question had you not been the one to rescue me!$B$BAnyhow! I\'m grateful for the assistance. Maybe I can pay you back?', '', 6086, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 1, 6, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I must know something: How did you go to the bathroom with that thing on?', 'I must know something: How did you go to the bathroom with that thing on? ', 6085, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Say, I sense a measure of disbelief in your voice - but yes, that\'s how it happened.', '', 6084, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('So let me get this straight. You were swimming, nay, doing backstrokes in molten lava with this... this lava suit of yours? Yes? And out of nowhere, this here beast swallowed you whole? ', 'So let me get this straight. You were swimming, nay, doing backstrokes in molten lava with this... this lava suit of yours? Yes? And out of nowhere, this here beast swallowed you whole? ', 6083, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Alrighty then! So I was down at the lava pits of the Molten Span, testing out my lava suit. Everything was going great. I was even able to swim around in that stuff without suffering a single injury!$B$BSo there I am, minding my own business, doing a few backstrokes, when out of nowhere this thing swallows me up whole! Had it not been for my lava suit and built in food pellet dispenser, I would have been done for!', '', 6082, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m all ears.', 'I\'m all ears.', 6081, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How?? Well, it\'s a long story.', '', 6080, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How the hell did you get in there to begin with?\n', 'How the hell did you get in there to begin with?\n', 6079, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Whew... I need a smoke and the touch of a fine gnomish woman - not particularly in that order!$B$BI\'ve been stuck inside the belly of that thing for months! What day is it anyway? Ah, nevermind. All that matters is that I\'m finally out.$B$BWOOO HOOO!', '', 6078, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 5, 4, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('My hatred is strong <snort>, but the time is right to tell you a tale, $r.$B$BLong ago a battle took place between gods. Agamaggan, our great boar god, fell to the earth after being defeated in the War of the Ancients, his blood raining down and his bones torn asunder. <snort>$B$BGreat thorns reached up out of the earth where his blood touched the ground, and his skull adorns one of the caverns to the south.', '', 6077, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Welcome to Stormwind!  I am one of the city\'s officers, aiding the citizenry of the city through our census bureau.  If you are in need of locating someone specific, then I might be able to assist you.  Through arcane methods and sharpened mental discipline, I am able to access these records.$B$BIf you have business with me, then please proceed!', '', 6076, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You! $R! Come here. <snort>$B$BTime is short, and my end <snort> is near. Mangletooth shall win; you will see. <snort>$B$BMy capture can still aid <snort> my people. The Razormane tribe is more powerful than the Bristlebacks!$B$BThe Horde looks to find out who leads the raids on their people. You <snort> shall aid Mangletooth in return for the information only I know. Mangletooth can help you! <snort> But you must help Mangletooth.', '', 6075, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now that\'s putting your hoof down!', 'Now that\'s putting your hoof down!', 6074, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('That\'s how it\'s done class!  You better be paying attention!', 'That\'s how it\'s done class!  You better be paying attention!', 6073, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now that\'s a War Stomp!  Good job!', 'Now that\'s a War Stomp!  Good job!', 6072, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('You surrendered.  I win.', 'You surrendered.  I win.', 6071, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Warchief has instructed me to study all kinds of weapons and armor. He has sent me here to the hub of both the tauren and orc cultures in the Barrens to meet as many travelers as possible, and to learn about the cultures of the Barrens.$B$BHe feels there\'s something to be learned from even the most pathetic of cultures... like the quilboar or centaur.', '', 6070, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I am an officer of the city, working in the capacity of the Undercity\'s census.  Since our liberation from the Scourge, we have tried to keep an accurate track of our city\'s populace.  Through arcane methods and sharpened mental discipline, I am able to access these records.  If you have business with me accordingly, please proceed.  You should know if you do, at any rate.', '', 6069, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ever vigilant in their protection of the natural world, the druids are guided by Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who resides in the Cenarion Enclave. You will find him and the other druid trainers in the northern section of Darnassus.', 'Ever vigilant in their protection of the natural world, the druids are guided by Archdruid Fandral Staghelm, who resides in the Cenarion Enclave. You will find him and the other druid trainers in the northern section of Darnassus.', 6068, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Who dares step into my domain!  Come!  Come, and be consumed!', '', 6067, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653);
INSERT INTO `broadcast_text` (`Text`, `Text1`, `ID`, `LanguageID`, `ConditionID`, `EmotesID`, `Flags`, `ChatBubbleDurationMs`, `SoundEntriesID1`, `SoundEntriesID2`, `EmoteID1`, `EmoteID2`, `EmoteID3`, `EmoteDelay1`, `EmoteDelay2`, `EmoteDelay3`, `VerifiedBuild`) VALUES
('Leaping leper gnomes! I\'ve been stuck in there for months. Thanks, gang.', '', 6066, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Brotherhood shall prevail!', '', 6065, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Fools! Our cause is righteous!', '', 6064, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Lapdogs, all of you!', '', 6063, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And stay down!', '', 6062, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('None may challenge the Brotherhood!', '', 6061, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('\"...\"$B$BThe body of the tauren druid lies still and unmoving.  It would seem as though he has finally passed from this world to his promised great beyond.', '', 6046, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, I speak a language you understand $r.  We are not animals, yet most of your kind continues to treat us as such!  Our differences though pale to the tragedy that has befallen this land.  Please, put aside your differences with my kind and hear my dying plea.$B$BI came to this land to mend what I could, and now that will be for naught unless you can aid me.  I ask for such aid with my last breaths of life.', '', 6045, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Please, help me $g brother : sister;...$B$BI will soon pass from this world, and though I suffer I know I shall not any more once I pass.  The wildlife though, my $g brother : sister;... the wildlife suffers too, and it knows no release.  I ask for your aid with my last breaths of life.', '', 6043, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s answers the call of Shy-Rotam.', '', 6040, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '%s roars out for her mate!', 6039, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Well Done!', 'Well Done!', 6038, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Don\'t let me die!', '', 6037, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Protect me from this $n! I must return to my brood.', '', 6036, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Help me kill $n!', '', 6035, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Have you spoken to either of my acolytes inside the tower yet, $n? We cannot complete your orb until you\'ve done one of their tasks. Speak to them now, if you\'re ready.', 6034, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s is summoned through a temporal rift!', '', 6033, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('ROOKERY MINION death DEBUG', 'ROOKERY MINION death DEBUG', 6032, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('ROOKERY MINION SPAWN DEBUG', 'ROOKERY MINION SPAWN DEBUG', 6031, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The felhound... a vicious creature indeed. It is not as physically strong as an infernal, but a wise warlock knows that brute force is not always the answer--if it was, you would have chosen the path of a warrior instead, wouldn\'t you?$B$BThe felhound draws upon the mana of its foes, using that and its quickness to overcome enemies. Its strength comes from the arcane and using that arcane power for its own ends.$B$BIf you wish to know more about infernals, then you should speak to Magaz across from me.', 6030, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The infernal is one of the most powerful demons a warlock could hope to have at $Ghis:her; side in battle. The creature is stong, well-armored, and delivers devastating blows upon any foe. If you were to choose to put the spirit of an infernal into your weapon, you would gain some of those benefits--greater health and regeneration and the like.$B$BIf you wish to know more about felhounds, then you should speak to Wytula across from me.', 6029, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Your errand must mean much, $c, to draw you so deep into the marsh...', 6028, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'It... is... not... the best... time, $n. I must concen... trate.', 6027, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Now\'s not a good time, $n.$B$BAre you insane?!', 6026, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Enough talk you two!  Commence fighting!', 'Enough talk you two!  Commence fighting!', 6025, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Not all Forsaken are driven by Sylvanas\' will, $n. Some of us are driven by true power--power we earn for ourselves.', 6024, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Listen to your elders, $n. If you are strong of will and dedicated, there is no power you cannot control.', 6023, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Tell Lexlort if he wants the information, all he has to do is pay! Unfortunately, that means he can\'t kill me if he wants the information - since I burned the battle plans and all...', 6022, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'This is where I get off, suckers!', 6021, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want you both to demonstrate the techniques I have taught you for the benefit of the younger students here.  Ready...  begin!', 'I want you both to demonstrate the techniques I have taught you for the benefit of the younger students here.  Ready...  begin!', 6020, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hello once again, $n.  I sense that the flow of time remains threatened by forces that are quite powerful indeed.  Your continued assistance is always welcomed by the bronze dragonflight.$B$BWhile the past is set in its ways, the future is always changing.  The decisions you make in the here and now help guide that change.', 6019, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hello there, $n.  I am known as Chronormu, but you may call me Chromie.  I am comfortable with such familiarity.$B$BNow - how did I know your name, you ask?  I am one of the bronze dragonflight, forever attuned to the ebb and flow of time.  You could say that we have met before.  To that end, we shall also meet again.', 6018, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Place Rend\'s head on the stake.', 'Place Rend\'s head on the stake.', 6017, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The Valley of Trials will temper even the weakest into a warrior worthy to join the Horde. Those who cannot rise to its tests will be left to bake in the scorching desert sun.', '', 6016, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be bathed in the power of the Warchief! Drink in his might! Battle for the glory of the Horde!', '', 6015, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be bathed in my power! Drink in my might! Battle for the glory of the Horde!', '', 6014, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Honor your heroes! On this day, they have dealt a great blow against one of our most hated enemies! The false Warchief, Rend Blackhand, has fallen!', '', 6013, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('The stake is covered with the remnants of those foolish enough to anger the Warchief.', '', 6012, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wow, it\'s 3 degrees Kraklenheit. Keep looking.', '', 6011, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s 40 degrees Kraklenheit. Can you feel the heat? No? I really couldn\'t either.', '', 6010, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('18 degrees Kraklenheit. It\'s kind of cold, actually...', '', 6009, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Measuring by Kraklenheit, it is 428,000 degrees! That\'s Krakley!', '', 6008, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('DING! 428,000 degrees Kraklenheit, exactly! Well, approximately. Almost. Somewhere around there...', '', 6007, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('It\'s 428,000 degrees Kraklenheit... What\'s happening, hot stuff!?', '', 6006, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hulfnar!  Thontek!  Stand and address me.', 'Hulfnar!  Thontek!  Stand and address me.', 6005, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('As you wish, Eitrigg.', 'As you wish, Eitrigg.', 6004, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Perhaps. Go now, young one. Seek council with the Warchief. He will surely wish to know of your discovery.', '', 6003, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 25, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Perhaps there exists a way?', 'Perhaps there exists a way?', 6002, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Indeed. Nefarian, brood of Deathwing, rules the Spire now. Rend is under the command of the dragon.$B$BIf only you could somehow manage to pass through the Halls of Ascension.$B$B<Eitrigg sighs.>$B$BAlas, only those deemed worthy by the black flight earn privilege to ascend.\n', '', 6001, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, so that is how they pushed the Dark Iron to the lower parts of the Spire.', 'Ah, so that is how they pushed the Dark Iron to the lower parts of the Spire.', 6000, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I\'m certain you will. Perhaps one day you could deliver a message to an old friend of mine. I hear he still wanders those woods.$B$B<Eitrigg bows his head for a moment, as if in prayer.>$B$BSo Rend, yes... Rend and his brother Maim ruled the Spire, in constant conflict with the Dark Iron dwarves. They managed to displace the dwarves in the upper portion of the city, but only after the dragons came and only after the death of Maim.', '', 5999, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I will take you up on that offer, Eitrigg.', 'I will take you up on that offer, Eitrigg.', 5998, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Eitrigg laughs.>$B$BYoung one, the world has not always been in such disarray. It was a time before the Scourge had sacked the land. Before those parts of Lordaeron were known as the Plaguelands.$B$BIt was there that Thrall rescued me from death and it was then that I joined the new Horde... but I digress. This is a story for another time. Yes, another time... Perhaps...', '', 5997, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 11, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hearthglen?? But...\n', 'Hearthglen?? But...\n', 5996, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I left. I would not remain with the Blackrock. No, the deaths of my children would not be in vain. I would not serve under an inept, power hungry maniac such as Rend.$B$BI took shelter in the woods of Lordaeron, living as a hermit near Hearthglen.', '', 5995, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What do you mean?', 'What do you mean?', 5994, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, young one, you need not convince me of such things, the Warchief and I have much history. Your dedication, however, is noted.$B$BAs I was saying, Rend had found a new home for his people, and I was among those who would wearily follow.$B$BFrom one conflict arose others... countless others. It was in those battles for Blackrock Spire between the Blackrock clan and the Dark Iron dwarves that my sons were both slain. It was then that I realized my time among the Blackrock clan had come to an end.', '', 5993, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('There is only one Warchief, Eitrigg!', 'There is only one Warchief, Eitrigg!', 5992, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Rend, son of Blackhand: Impotent chieftain of the Blackrock clan. A more stubborn fool does not exist.$B$BAt the end of the second War, Rend and his brother, Maim, fled to find sanctuary within the mountainous stronghold of Blackrock Spire. It was there that Rend declared himself Warchief of the weakened Blackrock clan.', '', 5991, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hello, Eitrigg. I bring news from Blackrock Spire.', 'Hello, Eitrigg. I bring news from Blackrock Spire.', 5990, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Greetings, young $c.', '', 5989, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s takes aim...', '', 5988, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s and Raider Kerr charge into battle...', '', 5987, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s and Raider Kerr let their wolves rest a bit and drink...', '', 5986, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s destroys the pike!', '', 5985, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s attacks the pike!', '', 5984, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah a visitor! Must be an adventurer, we don\'t get many tourists down this way. Grab a chair and a drink, make yourself comfortable. Say, you look like you have some meat on your bones. You thinkin about competing in the cage matches?', 'Ah a visitor! Must be an adventurer, we don\'t get many tourists down this way. Grab a chair and a drink, make yourself comfortable. Say, you look like you have some meat on your bones. You thinkin about competing in the cage matches?', 5983, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s bows before Krang Stonehoof', '%s bows before Krang Stonehoof', 5982, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Yes, sir. Thank you, sir!', 'Yes, sir. Thank you, sir!', 5981, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I did not doubt you for even one second, $n.$B$BHere are your orders, $n. I know that you will not let me down.\n', '', 5980, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Sir! Until my body ceases to function!', 'Sir! Until my body ceases to function!', 5979, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('And modest too... Perhaps it is your time, then, $n.$B$BAre you prepared to enter the fortress of the Blackrock orcs? To wreak havoc? To tear asunder the foundation of the mountain citadel?', '', 5978, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 25, 6, 6, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I do not deserve such praise, Warlord Goretooth.', 'I do not deserve such praise, Warlord Goretooth.', 5977, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Aye, I could tell just by looking at you, $n. You remind me very much of myself as a young warrior of the Horde.$B$BYou will undoubtedly go far in life and even further in death.$B$B<Goretooth salutes.>', '', 5976, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 66, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I pray for such things.', 'I pray for such things.', 5975, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I dream, $n... oh yes, I dream. In my dreams I die a thousand times in a thousand different ways. Some would call dreams such as mine nightmares. NOT I! In dreams I die in the thick of battle. For each single death of my own, ten thousand enemies of the Horde fall before me. It is glorious!', '', 5974, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 5, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Dreams?', 'Dreams?', 5973, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Truly, I envy you: To battle in the name of the Horde, at the forefront of conflict. Mine is a job of command.$B$BCertainly, in my youth, I lived out the dreams that make my old age bearable. I now revel in the glory of victory, the bitter taste of defeat - all through the soldiers I command.\n', '', 5972, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What roles?', 'What roles?', 5971, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('<Goretooth spits.>$B$BI am a warrior of the Horde, $n. It fills me with rage to know that our enemies sit in a fortress, less than a day\'s ride from Kargath, plotting against us.$B$BHow I long to break free from the bonds of duty and destroy them all in the name of the Warchief.$B$BAlas, we all have roles we must fulfill.\n', '', 5970, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 14, 5, 1, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Welcome to the Crossroads, $c. My name is Thork--I lead the defenses here in the name of the Warchief.$B$BPlease, feel free to make yourself at home. As long as you mind your business, no one should have any problem with you taking up some space.$B$BThere are many threats to our safety here. If you\'ve already become familiar with the lay of the land, speak to the others here--perhaps they have tasks for you to do.', '', 5969, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Do not push me, or I will impale you on my horns!', 'Do not push me, or I will impale you on my horns!', 5968, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Bring it on!', 'Bring it on!', 5967, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Start running!', 'Start running!', 5966, 3, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'You turn the body over and see the marks from blades and spells upon the deceased orc--her armor all but destroyed, her hair matted to her face.$B$BBased on Mankrik\'s description of her, there is no doubt in your mind that this was his wife.$B$BHe will be upset by the news, but you are sure he should know the truth.', 5965, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I inspect the body further.', 'I inspect the body further.', 5964, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'The body is that of a female orc warrior.$B$BIt is clear that she died in battle, probably against the quilboar in the area.', 5963, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I had to go and requisition an Abomination... an Abomination!', '', 5962, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Maybe I should have just bought some off of Faruza?', '', 5961, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Ah, this must be him now... no?  Bah!', '', 5960, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('As if I had all eternity.', '', 5959, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('If you want something done right, do it yourself!', '', 5958, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('At this rate I could have gathered them myself!', '', 5957, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('How long can it take to pick a handful of weeds?', '', 5956, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What could be taking so long?', '', 5955, 1, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Hmmm, this one looks like something that would be better off as a windchime. Take notes class... This is NOT what you want to summon in the heat of battle.', 'Hmmm, this one looks like something that would be better off as a windchime. Take notes class... This is NOT what you want to summon in the heat of battle.', 5954, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 94, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Wow, this one is just plain useless. Let me try again.', 'Wow, this one is just plain useless. Let me try again.', 5953, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 11, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('This one is slightly better than the last. However, it still suffers from the same flimsy bone structure as the others. When you summon one of these, you are on the right path.', 'This one is slightly better than the last. However, it still suffers from the same flimsy bone structure as the others. When you summon one of these, you are on the right path.', 5952, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 6, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Note the weak binding structure of this one. Be sure to finish your incantations or this is what you will end up with.', 'Note the weak binding structure of this one. Be sure to finish your incantations or this is what you will end up with.', 5951, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Now this is an example of what not to summon. Look, it\'s frail and brittle. One good whack from a mace will send bone shards flying.', 'Now this is an example of what not to summon. Look, it\'s frail and brittle. One good whack from a mace will send bone shards flying.', 5950, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Use staff, tell Raze what do! Show Raze poacher! Raze smash!', '', 5949, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s has been encaged.', '', 5948, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Haha! Perfect!', 5947, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 11, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '%s pours the corrupted water onto the cat.', 5946, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'I\'m very curious to see what this sample of water will do!', 5945, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 11, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s points to the parchment on the ground.', '', 5944, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I thank you, $n. Your dedication to my plea gives rest to my lost wife\'s spirit, and for that I could never repay you enough.$B$BI cannot say that my hatred will ever cease for the quilboar, but it is satiated for now.$B$BNow I must begin to rebuild my life.', '', 5943, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('What kind of a Horde are we if we refuse to deliver justice? The cowards all turned their backs on me in my time of need, $c. At the Crossroads they claimed I was blinded by my own rage, that I was acting rash and reckless.$B$B<Mankrik spits on the ground.>$B$BThey did not see what I have seen, have never lost what I have lost. I will not rest until I have my vengeance.', '', 5942, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 274, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s snarls ferociously.', '', 5941, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s follows $n obediently.', '', 5940, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s jumps into the moonwell, and goes underwater...', '', 5939, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('%s recasts the cleansing spell.', '', 5938, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Be cleansed!', '', 5937, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I want to release the corrupted saber to Winna.', 'I want to release the corrupted saber to Winna.', 5936, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('Grrr...', '', 5935, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('I present to you the rabid thistle bear, Tharnariun.', 'I present to you the rabid thistle bear, Tharnariun.', 5934, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Hi, $n.  No hard feelings, ok?', 5933, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '', 5932, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', '$n!  You\'re back!  And not a moment too soon!', 5931, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Finally, free at last... I must be going now, thanks for helping me escape. I can get back to Freewind Post by myself.', 5930, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'More Grimtotems are coming this way!', 5929, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Here they come.', 5928, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Look out, the Grimtotem are upon us!', 5927, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
('', 'Be on guard... Arnak has some strange power over the Grimtotem... they will not be happy to see me escape.', 5926, 0, 0, 0, 65, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 39653),
